msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Django project is committed to ensuring that websites built with Django "
"are usable by everyone, including people with disabilities. Django's built-"
"in components, such as the admin interface and default form rendering, "
"should adhere to established accessibility standards and meet our own "
"targets for supporting specific input devices and assistive technologies."
msgstr ""

msgid "Accessibility standards"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We work to conform with the `Web Content Accessibility Guidelines`_ (WCAG), "
"version 2.2, at the AA level. WCAG is the most established standard for web "
"accessibility. `AA-level guidelines`_ are the most common legal compliance "
"target worldwide."
msgstr ""

msgid "We also aim to follow other best practices, such as:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"WCAG 2.2 `AAA-level guidelines`_ – stricter criteria that go beyond the AA "
"level."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The upcoming `WCAG 3.0`_ guidelines – a new, evolving standard that aims to "
"unify and improve upon previous versions of WCAG."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`Authoring Tool Accessibility Guidelines`_ (ATAG) 2.0 – guidelines for "
"software and services that are used to produce web content."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To learn more about accessibility without diving straight into standards, we "
"recommend `The A11Y Project`_, a community-driven effort to make digital "
"accessibility easier."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support targets and testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Beyond standards, we want to make sure Django actually works for people "
"using a wide range of input devices and assistive technologies. This has "
"benefits to make sure Django works better `for everyone`_. The best way to "
"do this effectively is to take accessibility considerations into account as "
"part of designing features. If in doubt, consult with users who rely on "
"assistive technologies or with accessibility experts. You can reach out to "
"the `Accessibility team`_ via the `Accessibility Django forum topic`_ or via "
"the ``#accessibility`` channel on the `Django Discord server`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing baseline"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Design the UI with accessibility in mind, and the testing will only be "
"needed as a final check. For more complex interfaces, confer with other "
"contributors to decide on testing targets. Reach out to the `Accessibility "
"team`_ for support and to coordinate testing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Always test user interface changes with:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keyboard-only navigation. Common issues include:"
msgstr ""

msgid "An interactive element can't be reached using the Tab or arrow keys."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An interactive element \"traps\" input focus and prevents navigating away."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An interactive element doesn't give a visible indication when it has input "
"focus."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The focus order is inconsistent with the logical order that's communicated "
"visually."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Accessibility Insights`_ browser extension's automated checks feature, "
"or an equivalent tool with the `Axe`_ checker."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where the UI changes could affect those modalities, also test with:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Touch-only navigation. Common issues include:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A touch target (interactive element) is too small."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hover-based based interaction which does not translate to touch, such as a "
"hover only tooltip."
msgstr ""

msgid "400% browser zoom. Common issues include:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Content is cut off or disappears when zoomed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Content that does not inherently require a two-dimensional layout causes "
"scrolling in both directions (vertical and horizontal). Two-dimensional "
"scrolling is acceptable for content like images, maps, videos, and data "
"tables, which require both dimensions to be usable."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Forced-colors mode (for example Windows Contrast Themes). Note that this can "
"be tested via the ``\"high_contrast\"`` mode in the :ref:`screenshot tests "
"<screenshot-tests>`. Common issues include:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Over-reliance on color for meaning, which is lost in forced-colors mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use of ``!important`` or inline styles may break forced-colors mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Recommended assistive technologies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Where the UI changes could affect assistive technologies, here are popular "
"free options we recommend testing with."
msgstr ""

msgid "For Windows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`NVDA`_ - recommended with Firefox ESR"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Narrator`_ - recommended with Microsoft Edge"
msgstr ""

msgid "Windows Magnifier"
msgstr ""

msgid "Windows Speech Recognition"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Contrast themes`_"
msgstr ""

msgid "For macOS:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`VoiceOver`_ - recommended with Safari"
msgstr ""

msgid "macOS Zoom"
msgstr ""

msgid "macOS Voice Control"
msgstr ""

msgid "For Linux:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Orca`_ - recommended with Firefox ESR"
msgstr ""

msgid "For mobile or tablet:"
msgstr ""

msgid "VoiceOver on iOS, or TalkBack on Android"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The following are popular licensed options. If you are a user of these, or "
"can work with a user holding a license, also test against:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`JAWS`_ on Windows"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Dragon`_ on Windows"
msgstr ""

msgid "Known issues and how to help"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are parts of Django that do not meet our accessibility targets. We "
"actively work on fixing issues, both as part of ongoing maintenance and "
"bigger overhauls. To learn about known issues, and get involved, see:"
msgstr ""

msgid "``#accessibility`` on the `Django Discord server`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `Accessibility Django forum topic`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "`Accessibility issues on the ticket tracker`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "Our `django accessibility improvements`_ project board."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `Accessibility team`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reporting bugs and requesting features"
msgstr "Tuairisciú fabhtanna agus gnéithe"

msgid ""
"Please report security issues **only** to security@djangoproject.com.  This "
"is a private list only open to long-time, highly trusted Django developers, "
"and its archives are not public. For further details, please see :doc:`our "
"security policies </internals/security>`."
msgstr ""
"Tuairiscigh saincheisteanna slándála** amháin le do thoil chuig "
"security@djangoproject.com. Is liosta príobháideach é seo atá oscailte ach "
"d'fhorbróirí Django fadtréimhseacha, an-iontaofa, agus níl a chartlanna "
"poiblí. Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach le do thoil: doc: `ár bpolas</"
"internals/security> aithe slándála'."

msgid "Reporting bugs"
msgstr "Fhabhtanna a thu"

msgid ""
"Before reporting a bug on the `ticket tracker <https://"
"code.djangoproject.com/>`_ consider these points:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check that someone hasn't already filed the bug report by `searching`_ or "
"running `custom queries`_ in the ticket tracker."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Don't use the ticket system to ask support questions. Use the `Django "
"Forum`_ or the `Django Discord server`_ for that."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Don't reopen issues that have been marked \"wontfix\" without finding "
"consensus to do so on the `Django Forum`_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Don't use the ticket tracker for lengthy discussions, because they're likely "
"to get lost. If a particular ticket is controversial, please move the "
"discussion to the `Django Forum`_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Well-written bug reports are *incredibly* helpful. However, there's a "
"certain amount of overhead involved in working with any bug tracking system "
"so your help in keeping our ticket tracker as useful as possible is "
"appreciated. In particular:"
msgstr ""
"Tá tuairiscí fabht dea-scríofa * thar a bheith cabhrach. Mar sin féin, tá "
"méid áirithe lasbhairde bainteach le hobair le haon chóras rianaithe fabht "
"ionas go bhfuil meas ag do chabhair lenár rianaitheoir ticéad a choinneáil "
"chomh úsáideach agus is féidir. Go háirithe:"

msgid ""
"**Do** read the :doc:`FAQ </faq/index>` to see if your issue might be a well-"
"known question."
msgstr ""
"**Déan** léigh an:doc: `FAQ` chun a fháil amach an bhféadfadh do cheist a "
"bheith ina cheist aithe</faq/index> anta."

msgid ""
"**Do** ask on `Django Forum`_ or the `Django Discord server`_ *first* if "
"you're not sure if what you're seeing is a bug."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Do** write complete, reproducible, specific bug reports. You must include "
"a clear, concise description of the problem, and a set of instructions for "
"replicating it. Add as much debug information as you can: code snippets, "
"test cases, exception backtraces, screenshots, etc. A nice small test case "
"is the best way to report a bug, as it gives us a helpful way to confirm the "
"bug quickly."
msgstr ""
"**Déan** tuarascálacha fabht iomlána, in-atáirgthe, a scríobh. Caithfidh tú "
"cur síos soiléir, gonta ar an bhfadhb a áireamh, agus sraith treoracha chun "
"í a mhacasamhlú. Cuir an oiread faisnéise dífhabhtaithe agus is féidir leat: "
"snippets cód, cásanna tástála, cúltaca eisceachta, scannáin, srl Is é cás "
"tástála deas beag an bealach is fearr chun fabht a thuairisciú, mar tugann "
"sé bealach cabhrach dúinn an fabht a dhearbhú go tapa."

msgid ""
"**Don't** post to `Django Forum`_ only to announce that you have filed a bug "
"report. All the tickets are mailed to another list, |django-updates|, which "
"is tracked by developers and interested community members; we see them as "
"they are filed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To understand the lifecycle of your ticket once you have created it, refer "
"to :doc:`triaging-tickets`."
msgstr ""
"Chun saolré do thicéad a thuiscint nuair a bheidh sé cruthaithe agat, féach "
"ar:doc: `triaging-tickets`."

msgid "Reporting user interface bugs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your bug impacts anything visual in nature, there are a few additional "
"guidelines to follow:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Include screenshots in your ticket which are the visual equivalent of a "
"minimal test case. Show off the issue, not the crazy customizations you've "
"made to your browser."
msgstr ""
"Cuir scannáin san áireamh i do thicéad atá comhionann amhairc le cás tástála "
"íosta. Taispeáin an tsaincheist, ní na saincheaptha craiceáilte a rinne tú "
"ar do bhrabhsálaí."

msgid ""
"If the issue is difficult to show off using a still image, consider "
"capturing a *brief* screencast. If your software permits it, capture only "
"the relevant area of the screen."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé deacair an cheist a thaispeáint ag baint úsáide as íomhá fhór, "
"smaoinigh ar scáileán gearrthán* a ghabháil. Má cheadaíonn do bhogearraí é, "
"ní ghabháil ach an limistéar ábhartha den scáileán."

msgid ""
"If you're offering a patch that changes the look or behavior of Django's UI, "
"you **must** attach before *and* after screenshots/screencasts. Tickets "
"lacking these are difficult for triagers to assess quickly."
msgstr ""
"Má tá paiste á dtairiscint agat a athraíonn cuma nó iompar Chomhéadain "
"Django, ní mór duit** a cheangal roimh* agus* tar éis scáileán/scáileáin "
"scáileáin. Tá sé deacair do thríóirí ticéid nach bhfuil siad seo acu a mheas "
"go tapa."

msgid ""
"Screenshots don't absolve you of other good reporting practices. Make sure "
"to include URLs, code snippets, and step-by-step instructions on how to "
"reproduce the behavior visible in the screenshots."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuireann scáileáin scáileáin ort ó dhea-chleachtais tuairiscithe eile. "
"Déan cinnte URLanna, snippets cód, agus treoracha céim ar chéim a áireamh "
"maidir le conas an t-iompar atá le feiceáil sna scannáin a atáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"Make sure to set the UI/UX flag on the ticket so interested parties can find "
"your ticket."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte bratach UI/UX a shocrú ar an ticéad ionas gur féidir le "
"páirtithe leasmhara do thicéad a fháil."

msgid ""
"If the issue relates to accessibility, please link to the "
"relevant :ref:`accessibility standard <accessibility-standards>` if "
"applicable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Requesting features"
msgstr "Gnéithe a iarraidh"

msgid ""
"We're always trying to make Django better, and your feature requests are a "
"key part of that. Here are some tips on how to make a request most "
"effectively:"
msgstr ""
"Táimid i gcónaí ag iarraidh Django a dhéanamh níos fearr, agus is cuid "
"lárnach de sin iad d'iarrataí gné. Seo roinnt leideanna maidir le conas "
"iarratas a dhéanamh is éifeachtaí:"

msgid ""
"Evaluate whether the feature idea requires changes in Django's core. If your "
"idea can be developed as an independent application or module — for "
"instance, you want to support another database engine — we'll probably "
"suggest that you develop it independently. Then, if your project gathers "
"sufficient community support, we may consider it for inclusion in Django."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Propose the feature in the `new feature ideas`_ GitHub project (not in the "
"ticket tracker) by creating a new item in the **Idea** column. This is where "
"the community and the :ref:`Steering Council <steering-council>` evaluate "
"new ideas for the Django ecosystem. This step is especially important for "
"large or complex proposals. We prefer to discuss any significant changes to "
"Django's core before any development begins. In some cases, a feature may be "
"better suited as a third-party package, where it can evolve independently of "
"Django's release cycle."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Describe clearly and concisely what the missing feature is and how you'd "
"like to see it implemented. Include example code (non-functional is OK) if "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Déan cur síos soiléir agus go hachomair cad é an ghné atá in easnamh agus "
"conas ar mhaith leat é a fheiceáil i bhfeidhm. Cuir cód samplaí san áireamh "
"(tá neamhfheidhmiúil ceart go leor) más féidir."

msgid ""
"Explain *why* you'd like the feature. Explaining a minimal use case will "
"help others understand where it fits in, and if there are already other ways "
"of achieving the same thing."
msgstr ""
"Mínigh cén fá* gur mhaith leat an ghné. Cuideoidh míniú cás íosta úsáide le "
"daoine eile tuiscint a fháil ar an áit a luíonn sé isteach, agus má tá "
"bealaí eile ann cheana chun an rud céanna a bhaint amach."

msgid "See also: :ref:`documenting-new-features`."
msgstr "Féach freisin: :ref: `documenting-new-features `."

msgid "Requesting performance optimizations"
msgstr "Optamú feidhmíochta a iarraidh"

msgid ""
"Reports of a performance regression, or suggested performance optimizations, "
"should provide benchmarks and commands for the ticket triager to reproduce."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go soláthródh tuairiscí ar aischéimniú feidhmíochta, nó "
"barrfheabhsú feidhmíochta molta, tagarmharcanna agus orduithe don triager "
"ticéad a atáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`django-asv-benchmarks` for more details of Django's existing "
"benchmarks."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `django-asv-tagarmharcans` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoi "
"thagarmharcanna Django atá ann cheana."

msgid "How we make decisions"
msgstr "Conas a dhéanaimid cinntí"

msgid ""
"Whenever possible, we aim for rough consensus. Emoji reactions are used on "
"issues within the `new feature ideas`_ GitHub project to track community "
"feedback. The following meanings are assigned to each reaction:"
msgstr ""

msgid "👍: I support this feature and would use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"👎: I oppose this feature or believe it would cause issues for me or Django"
msgstr ""

msgid "😕: I have no strong opinion on this feature"
msgstr ""

msgid "🎉: This feature seems like a straightforward and beneficial addition"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The :ref:`Steering Council <steering-council>` will regularly review the "
"ideas in the project, moving those with community support through the "
"following stages:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Idea"
msgstr ""

msgid "Approved - Idea refinement - Team creation"
msgstr ""

msgid "In progress"
msgstr ""

msgid "Working solution - Review - Feedback"
msgstr ""

msgid "Needs maintainer (Django only)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Done"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Occasionally, discussions on feature ideas or the direction of Django may "
"take place on the Django Forum. These discussions may include informal "
"votes, which follow the voting style invented by Apache and used on Python "
"itself, where votes are given as +1, +0, -0, or -1. Roughly translated, "
"these votes mean:"
msgstr ""

msgid "+1: \"I love the idea and I'm strongly committed to it.\""
msgstr "+1: “Is breá liom an smaoineamh agus táim tiomanta go láidir dó.”"

msgid "+0: \"Sounds OK to me.\""
msgstr "+0: “Fuaimeanna ceart go leor dom.”"

msgid "-0: \"I'm not thrilled, but I won't stand in the way.\""
msgstr "-0: “Níl áthas orm, ach ní sheasfaidh mé ar an mbealach.”"

msgid ""
"-1: \"I strongly disagree and would be very unhappy to see the idea turn "
"into reality.\""
msgstr ""
"-1: “Ní aontaím go láidir agus bheadh mé an-míshásta an smaoineamh a "
"fheiceáil ag titim ina réaltacht.”"

msgid ""
"Although these votes are informal, they'll be taken very seriously. After a "
"suitable voting period, if an obvious consensus arises we'll follow the "
"votes."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil na vótaí seo neamhfhoirmiúil, glacfar i ndáiríre iad. Tar éis "
"tréimhse vótála oiriúnach, má thagann comhdhearcadh soiléir chun cinn "
"leanfaimid na vótaí."

msgid "Committing code"
msgstr "Cód tiomanta"

msgid ""
"This section is addressed to the mergers and to anyone interested in knowing "
"how code gets committed into Django. If you're a community member who wants "
"to contribute code to Django, look at :doc:`writing-code/working-with-git` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an chuid seo dírithe ar na cumaisc agus d'aon duine ar bith a bhfuil suim "
"acu a fháil amach conas a thiomnaíonn cód i Django. Más ball pobail tú atá "
"ag iarraidh cód a chur le Django, féach ar:doc: `writing-code/working-with-"
"git` ina ionad."

msgid "Handling pull requests"
msgstr "Iarrataí tarraingthe a"

msgid ""
"Since Django is hosted on GitHub, patches are provided in the form of pull "
"requests."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhfuil Django á óstáil ar GitHub, cuirtear paistí ar fáil i "
"bhfoirm iarratais tarraingthe."

msgid ""
"When committing a pull request, make sure each individual commit matches the "
"commit guidelines described below. Contributors are expected to provide the "
"best pull requests possible. In practice mergers - who will likely be more "
"familiar with the commit guidelines - may decide to bring a commit up to "
"standard themselves."
msgstr ""
"Agus iarratas tarraingthe á dhéanamh agat, déan cinnte go gcomhlíonann gach "
"tiomantas aonair na treoirlínte tiomanta Táthar ag súil go soláthróidh "
"ranníocóirí na hiarratais tarraingthe is fearr Go praiticiúil féadfaidh "
"cumaisc - a mbeidh níos eolaí ar na treoirlínte tiomanta - cinneadh a "
"dhéanamh tiomantas a thabhairt suas go dtí an caighdeán iad féin."

msgid ""
"You may want to have Jenkins or GitHub actions test the pull request with "
"one of the pull request builders that doesn't run automatically, such as "
"Oracle or Selenium. See the `CI wiki page`_ for instructions."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat gníomhartha Jenkins nó GitHub a thástáil ar an "
"iarratas tarraingthe le duine de na tógálaithe iarratais tarraingthe nach "
"ritheann go huathoibríoch, mar shampla Oracle nó Selenium. Féach an "
"`leathanach wiki CI `_ le haghaidh treoracha."

msgid ""
"If you find yourself checking out pull requests locally more often, this git "
"alias will be helpful:"
msgstr ""
"Má aimsíonn tú tú féin ag seiceáil iarratais tarraingthe go háitiúil níos "
"minice, beidh an t-alias git seo cabhrach:"

msgid ""
"Add it to your ``~/.gitconfig``, and set ``upstream`` to be ``django/"
"django``. Then you can run ``git pr ####`` to checkout the corresponding "
"pull request."
msgstr ""
"Cuir é le do ``~/.gitconfig``, agus socraigh ``upstream`` mar ``django/"
"django``. Ansin is féidir leat ``git pr ####`` a rith chun an t-iarratas "
"tarraingthe comhfhreagrach a sheiceáil."

msgid ""
"At this point, you can work on the code. Use ``git rebase -i`` and ``git "
"commit --amend`` to make sure the commits have the expected level of "
"quality. Once you're ready:"
msgstr ""
"Ag an bpointe seo, is féidir leat oibriú ar an gcód. Úsáid ``git rebase -i`` "
"agus ``git commit --amend`` chun a chinntiú go bhfuil an leibhéal cáilíochta "
"ag súil leis ag na gealltanais. Nuair a bheidh tú réidh:"

msgid ""
"Force push to the branch after rebasing on main but before merging and "
"pushing to upstream. This allows the commit hashes on main and the branch to "
"match which automatically closes the pull request."
msgstr ""
"Fórsa brú go dtí an brainse tar éis athbhunú ar an bpríomhlíonra ach roimh "
"chumasc agus brú go dtí an sruth. Ligeann sé seo do na hashes geallta ar an "
"bpríomhlíonra agus an brainse a mheaitseáil a dhúnann an t-iarratas "
"tarraingt go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"If a pull request doesn't need to be merged as multiple commits, you can use "
"GitHub's \"Squash and merge\" button on the website. Edit the commit message "
"as needed to conform to :ref:`the guidelines <committing-guidelines>` and "
"remove the pull request number that's automatically appended to the "
"message's first line."
msgstr ""
"Mura gá iarraidh tarraingthe a chumasc mar ghealltanais iolracha, is féidir "
"leat cnaipe “Squash agus cumaisc” GitHub a úsáid ar an suíomh Gréasáin. Cuir "
"an teachtaireacht <committing-guidelines>tiomanta in eagar de réir mar is gá "
"chun comhlíonadh la:ref: `na treoirlínte `agus bain an uimhir iarratais "
"tarraingthe a chuirtear isteach go huathoibríoch le chéad líne na "
"teachtaireachta."

msgid ""
"When rewriting the commit history of a pull request, the goal is to make "
"Django's commit history as usable as possible:"
msgstr ""
"Agus stair thiomanta iarratais tarraingthe á athscríobh agat, is é an aidhm "
"stair thiomanta Django a dhéanamh chomh inúsáidte agus is féidir:"

msgid ""
"If a patch contains back-and-forth commits, then rewrite those into one. For "
"example, if a commit adds some code and a second commit fixes stylistic "
"issues introduced in the first commit, those commits should be squashed "
"before merging."
msgstr ""
"Má tá gealltanais anar-anall i bpaiste, ansin iad sin a athscríobh i gceann "
"amháin. Mar shampla, má chuireann tiomantas cód éigin leis agus má "
"shocraíonn an dara tiomantas saincheisteanna stíleacha a tugadh isteach sa "
"chéad thiomantas, ba chóir na gealltanais sin a scriosadh sula ndéantar iad "
"a chumasc."

msgid ""
"Separate changes to different commits by logical grouping: if you do a "
"stylistic cleanup at the same time as you do other changes to a file, "
"separating the changes into two different commits will make reviewing "
"history easier."
msgstr ""
"Athruithe ar leithligh ar ghealltanais éagsúla trí ghrúpáil loighciúil: má "
"dhéanann tú glantachán stíle ag an am céanna agus a dhéanann tú athruithe "
"eile ar chomhad, beidh sé níos fusa athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an stair trí "
"na hathruithe a roinnt ina dhá ghealltanas éagsúla."

msgid "Beware of merges of upstream branches in the pull requests."
msgstr "Bí cúramach le cumaisc brainsí suas srutha sna hiarratais tarraingthe."

msgid ""
"Tests should pass and docs should build after each commit. Neither the tests "
"nor the docs should emit warnings."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go rith na tástálacha agus ba chóir doiciméid a thógáil tar éis "
"gach Níor chóir do na tástálacha ná na doiciméid rabhaidh a eisiúint."

msgid ""
"Trivial and small patches usually are best done in one commit. Medium to "
"large work may be split into multiple commits if it makes sense."
msgstr ""
"Is fearr paistí triobhála agus beaga de ghnáth a dhéanamh i dtiomantas "
"amháin. Féadfar obair mheánmhéide go mór a roinnt ina iliomad gealltanais má "
"tá ciall aige."

msgid ""
"Practicality beats purity, so it is up to each merger to decide how much "
"history mangling to do for a pull request. The main points are engaging the "
"community, getting work done, and having a usable commit history."
msgstr ""
"Buaileann praiticiúlacht íonacht, mar sin tá sé faoi gach cumaisc cinneadh a "
"dhéanamh cé mhéad staire atá le déanamh le haghaidh iarratas tarraingthe. Is "
"iad na príomhphointí ná an pobal a mhealladh, obair a dhéanamh, agus stair "
"tiomanta inúsáidte a bheith agat."

msgid "Committing guidelines"
msgstr "Treoirlínte a"

msgid ""
"In addition, please follow the following guidelines when committing code to "
"Django's Git repository:"
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, lean na treoirlínte seo a leanas agus tú ag déanamh cód do "
"stór Git Django:"

msgid ""
"Never change the published history of ``django/django`` branches by force "
"pushing. If you absolutely must (for security reasons for example), first "
"discuss the situation with the team."
msgstr ""
"Ná athraigh stair foilsithe brainsí ``django/django`` trí bhrú fórsa. Más gá "
"duit go hiomlán (ar chúiseanna slándála mar shampla), plé an cás leis an "
"bhfoireann ar dtús."

msgid ""
"For any medium-to-big changes, where \"medium-to-big\" is according to your "
"judgment, please bring things up on the `Django Forum`_ before making the "
"change."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you bring something up and nobody responds, please don't take that to "
"mean your idea is great and should be implemented immediately because nobody "
"contested it. Everyone doesn't always have a lot of time to read discussions "
"immediately, so you may have to wait a couple of days before getting a "
"response."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write detailed commit messages in the past tense, not present tense."
msgstr ""
"Scríobh teachtaireachtaí tiomanta mionsonraithe san am atá caite, ní am "
"reatha."

msgid "Good: \"Fixed Unicode bug in RSS API.\""
msgstr "Go maith: “Fhabht Unicode seasta i RSS API.”"

msgid "Bad: \"Fixes Unicode bug in RSS API.\""
msgstr "Droch: “Socraíonn fabht Unicode i RSS API.”"

msgid "Bad: \"Fixing Unicode bug in RSS API.\""
msgstr "Droch: “Socrú fabht Unicode i RSS API.”"

msgid ""
"The commit message should be in lines of 72 chars maximum. There should be a "
"subject line, separated by a blank line and then paragraphs of 72 char "
"lines. The limits are soft. For the subject line, shorter is better. In the "
"body of the commit message more detail is better than less:"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an teachtaireacht tiomanta i línte de 72 chars ar a "
"mhéad. Ba chóir go mbeadh líne ábhair ann, scartha le líne bán agus ansin "
"míreanna de 72 líne char. Tá na teorainneacha bog. Maidir leis an líne "
"ábhair, is fearr níos giorra. I gcorp na teachtaireachta tiomanta is fearr "
"níos mó mionsonraí ná níos lú:"

msgid ""
"Credit the contributors in the commit message: \"Thanks A for the report and "
"B for review.\" Use git's `Co-Authored-By`_ as appropriate."
msgstr ""
"Creidmheas do na ranníocóirí sa teachtaireacht tiomanta: “Go raibh maith "
"agat A as an tuarascáil agus B le haghaidh athbhreithniú.” Úsáid `Co-"
"Authored-By`_ git de réir mar is cuí."

msgid ""
"For commits to a branch, prefix the commit message with the branch name. For "
"example: \"[1.4.x] Fixed #xxxxx -- Added support for mind reading.\""
msgstr ""
"Maidir le tiomantas do bhrainse, réimsigh an teachtaireacht tiomanta le "
"hainm na brainse. Mar shampla: “[1.4.x] Seasta #xxxxx -- Tacaíocht bhreise "
"le haghaidh léamh intinne.”"

msgid ""
"Limit commits to the most granular change that makes sense. This means, use "
"frequent small commits rather than infrequent large commits. For example, if "
"implementing feature X requires a small change to library Y, first commit "
"the change to library Y, then commit feature X in a separate commit. This "
"goes a *long way* in helping everyone follow your changes."
msgstr ""
"Tiomann teorainn don athrú is gráinneach a dhéanann ciall. Ciallaíonn sé "
"seo, bain úsáid as gealltanais bheaga go minic seachas tiomantas móra is "
"annamh. Mar shampla, má éilíonn athrú beag ar leabharlann Y a chur i "
"bhfeidhm gné X, déan an t-athrú a dhéanamh ar leabharlann Y ar dtús, ansin "
"déan gné X i dtiomantas ar leithligh. Téann sé seo* bealach fad* chun cabhrú "
"le gach duine d'athruithe a leanúint."

msgid ""
"Separate bug fixes from feature changes. Bugfixes may need to be backported "
"to the stable branch, according to :ref:`supported-versions-policy`."
msgstr ""
"Socruithe fabht ar leithligh ó athruithe gné. B'fhéidir go gcaithfear "
"fabhtshocruithe a chur ar ais chuig an mbrainse chobhsaí, de réir: ref: "
"`supportted-versions-policy `."

msgid ""
"If your commit closes a ticket in the Django `ticket tracker`_, begin your "
"commit message with the text \"Fixed #xxxxx\", where \"xxxxx\" is the number "
"of the ticket your commit fixes. Example: \"Fixed #123 -- Added whizbang "
"feature.\". We've rigged Trac so that any commit message in that format will "
"automatically close the referenced ticket and post a comment to it with the "
"full commit message."
msgstr ""
"Má dhúnann do thiomantas ticéad sa `rianaitheoir ticéad`_ Django, cuir tús "
"le do theachtaireacht tiomanta leis an téacs “Seasta #xxxxx “, áit is é "
"“xxxxx” uimhir an ticéad a shocraíonn do thiomantas. Sampla: “Seasta #123 -- "
"Gné whizbang curtha leis.”. Tá Trac curtha againn ionas go ndúnfaidh aon "
"teachtaireacht tiomanta san fhormáid sin an ticéad tagartha go huathoibríoch "
"agus go gcuirfidh trácht air leis an teachtaireacht iomlán tiomanta."

msgid "For the curious, we're using a `Trac plugin`_ for this."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le daoine fiosracha, táimid ag baint úsáide as `breiseán Trac `_ "
"chuige seo."

msgid ""
"Note that the Trac integration doesn't know anything about pull requests. So "
"if you try to close a pull request with the phrase \"closes #400\" in your "
"commit message, GitHub will close the pull request, but the Trac plugin will "
"not close the same numbered ticket in Trac."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil aon rud ar eolas ag comhtháthú Trac faoi "
"iarratais tarraingthe. Mar sin má dhéanann tú iarratas tarraingthe a dhúnadh "
"leis an abairt “dúnann #400\" i do theachtaireacht tiomanta, dúnfaidh GitHub "
"an t-iarratas tarraingthe, ach ní dhúnfaidh an breiseán Trac an ticéad "
"uimhrithe céanna i Trac."

msgid ""
"If your commit references a ticket in the Django `ticket tracker`_ but does "
"*not* close the ticket, include the phrase \"Refs #xxxxx\", where \"xxxxx\" "
"is the number of the ticket your commit references. This will automatically "
"post a comment to the appropriate ticket."
msgstr ""
"Má thagraíonn do thiomantas ticéad sa `rianaitheoir ticéad`_ Django ach ní "
"dhúnnaí* an ticéad, cuir an abairt “Refs #xxxxx “san áireamh, áit ar “xxxxx” "
"uimhir an ticéid a thagann do thiomantas. Cuirfidh sé seo trácht ar an "
"ticéad cuí go huathoibríoch."

msgid "Write commit messages for backports using this pattern:"
msgstr ""
"Scríobh teachtaireachtaí tiomanta do chúlphortanna ag baint úsáide as an "
"bpatrún seo:"

msgid "For example:"
msgstr "Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"There's a `script on the wiki <https://code.djangoproject.com/wiki/"
"MergerTips#AutomatingBackports>`_ to automate this."
msgstr ""
"Tá `script ar an wiki`_ chun é seo a uathoibri< https://"
"code.djangoproject.com/wiki/MergerTips#AutomatingBackports> ú."

msgid "If the commit fixes a regression, include this in the commit message:"
msgstr ""
"Má shocraíonn an tiomantas aischéimniú, cuir é seo san áireamh sa "
"teachtaireacht tiomanta:"

msgid "(use the commit hash where the regression was introduced)."
msgstr "(bain úsáid as an hash tiomanta inar tugadh isteach an aischéimniú)."

msgid "Reverting commits"
msgstr "Tiomantas a thabhairt ar ais"

msgid "Nobody's perfect; mistakes will be committed."
msgstr "Níl aon duine foirfe; déanfar botúin."

msgid ""
"But try very hard to ensure that mistakes don't happen. Just because we have "
"a reversion policy doesn't relax your responsibility to aim for the highest "
"quality possible. Really: double-check your work, or have it checked by "
"another merger **before** you commit it in the first place!"
msgstr ""
"Ach déan iarracht an-chrua a chinntiú nach dtarlóidh botúin. Díreach toisc "
"go bhfuil beartas aisghabhála againn ní mhaolaítear do fhreagracht chun "
"díriú a dhéanamh ar an gcaighdeán is airde is féidir. I ndáiríre: déan do "
"chuid oibre a sheiceáil faoi dhó, nó déan í a sheiceáil trí chumasc eile** "
"roimhe** déanann tú é sa chéad áit!"

msgid "When a mistaken commit is discovered, please follow these guidelines:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a aimsítear tiomantas mícheart, lean na treoirlínte seo le do thoil:"

msgid "If possible, have the original author revert their own commit."
msgstr "Más féidir, cuir ar an údar bunaidh a thiomantas féin a chur ar ais."

msgid ""
"Don't revert another author's changes without permission from the original "
"author."
msgstr "Ná cuir athruithe údair eile ar ais gan cead ón údar bunaidh."

msgid ""
"Use git revert -- this will make a reverse commit, but the original commit "
"will still be part of the commit history."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid git revert - déanfaidh sé seo tiomantas ar ais, ach beidh an tiomantas "
"bunaidh fós mar chuid de stair an tiomanta."

msgid ""
"If the original author can't be reached (within a reasonable amount of time "
"-- a day or so) and the problem is severe -- crashing bug, major test "
"failures, etc. -- then ask for objections on the `Django Forum`_ then revert "
"if there are none."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the problem is small (a feature commit after feature freeze, say), wait "
"it out."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an fhadhb beag (gné a thiomann tar éis reoite gné, abair), fan amach í."

msgid ""
"If there's a disagreement between the merger and the reverter-to-be then try "
"to work it out on the `Django Forum`_ . If an agreement can't be reached "
"then it should be put to a vote."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the commit introduced a confirmed, disclosed security vulnerability then "
"the commit may be reverted immediately without permission from anyone."
msgstr ""
"Má thug an tiomantas leochaileacht slándála dearbhaithe, nochtaithe isteach "
"ansin féadfar an tiomantas a chur ar ais láithreach gan cead ó aon duine."

msgid ""
"The release branch maintainer may back out commits to the release branch "
"without permission if the commit breaks the release branch."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh an cothabhálaí brainse scaoilte gealltanais a chur ar ais don "
"bhrainse scaoilte gan cead má bhriseann an tiomantas an brainse scaoilte."

msgid ""
"If you mistakenly push a topic branch to ``django/django``, delete it. For "
"instance, if you did: ``git push upstream feature_antigravity``, do a "
"reverse push: ``git push upstream :feature_antigravity``."
msgstr ""
"Má bhrúiteann tú brainse ábhar ar dhearmad chuig `django/django``, scrios é. "
"Mar shampla, má rinne tú: `git push upstream feature_antigravity``, déan brú "
"droim: ``git push upstream:feature_antigravity``."

msgid "An overview of the contributing process and what's involved."
msgstr "Forbhreathnú ar an bpróiseas rannchuidithe agus a bhfuil i gceist."

msgid "Contributing to Django"
msgstr "Ag cur le Django"

msgid ""
"Django is a community that lives on its volunteers. As it keeps growing, we "
"always need more people to help others. You can contribute in many ways, "
"either on the framework itself or in the wider ecosystem."
msgstr ""
"Is pobal é Django a chónaíonn ar a saorálaithe. De réir mar atá sé ag fás, "
"teastaíonn níos mó daoine uainn i gcónaí chun cabhrú le daoine eile. Is "
"féidir leat rannchuidiú ar go leor bealaí, ar an gcreat féin nó san "
"éiceachóras níos leithne."

msgid "Communication channels"
msgstr "Bealaí cumarsáide"

msgid ""
"We're passionate about helping Django users make the jump to contributing "
"members of the community. Communication is key - working on Django is being "
"part of a conversation. Join it, to become familiar with what we're doing "
"and how we talk about it. You'll be able to form relationships with more "
"experienced contributors who are there to help guide you towards success."
msgstr ""
"Táimid paiseanta faoi chabhrú le húsáideoirí Django léim a dhéanamh chun "
"baill den phobal a rannchuidiú. Tá cumarsáid ríthábhachtach - tá obair ar "
"Django mar chuid de chomhrá. Bí leis, chun dul i dtaithí ar an méid atá á "
"dhéanamh againn agus ar an gcaoi a labhraímid faoi. Beidh tú in ann caidrimh "
"a fhoirmiú le rannpháirtithe níos mó taithí atá ann chun cabhrú leat a "
"threorú i dtreo rath."

msgid "Join the Django community"
msgstr "Bí i bpobal Django"

msgid ""
"There are several ways you can help the Django community and others to "
"maintain a great ecosystem to work in:"
msgstr ""
"Tá bealaí éagsúla ann is féidir leat cabhrú le pobal Django agus le daoine "
"eile éiceachóras iontach a choinneáil chun oibriú ann:"

msgid ""
"Join the `Django Forum`_. This forum is a place for discussing the Django "
"framework and applications and projects that use it. This is also a good "
"place to ask and answer any questions related to installing, using, or "
"contributing to Django."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Join the `Django Discord server`_ to discuss and answer questions. By "
"explaining Django to other users, you're going to learn a lot about the "
"framework yourself."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Blog about Django. We syndicate all the Django blogs we know about on the "
"`community page`_; if you'd like to see your blog on that page you can "
"`register it here`_."
msgstr ""
"Blag faoi Django. Déanaimid na blaganna Django go léir a fhios againn fúthu "
"ar an `leathanach pobail `_; más mian leat do bhlag a fheiceáil ar an "
"leathanach sin is féidir leat é a chlárú anseo `_."

msgid ""
"Contribute to open-source Django projects, write some documentation, or "
"release your own code as an open-source pluggable application. The ecosystem "
"of pluggable applications is a big strength of Django, help us build it!"
msgstr ""
"Cuir le tionscadail foinse oscailte Django, scríobh roinnt doiciméadú, nó "
"scaoil do chód féin mar fheidhmchlár inphlocálaithe foinse oscailte. Is "
"neart mór de Django é éiceachóras na bhfeidhmchlár inphlugáilte, cuidigh "
"linn é a thógáil!"

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Ag tosnú"

msgid ""
"Django encourages and welcomes new contributors, and makes an effort to help "
"them become experienced, confident contributors to Open Source Software "
"(OSS). Our documentation contains guidance for first-time contributors, "
"including:"
msgstr ""
"Spreagann Django rannpháirtithe nua agus fáilte roimh rannpháirtithe nua, "
"agus déanann sé iarracht cabhrú leo a bheith ina rannpháirtithe muiníneacha "
"le Bogearraí Foinse Oscailte (OS Tá treoir inár ndoiciméad do rannpháirtithe "
"céaduaire, lena n-áirítear:"

msgid "Work on the Django framework"
msgstr "Oibrigh ar chreat Django"

msgid ""
"If you enjoy working *with* Django, wait until you start working *on* it. "
"Really, **anyone** can do something to improve Django, which will improve "
"the experience of lots of people!"
msgstr ""
"Má thaitníonn leat oibriú* le* Django, fan go dtí go dtosaíonn tú ag obair* "
"ar* air. I ndáiríre, is féidir le haon** rud éigin a dhéanamh chun Django a "
"fheabhsú, rud a fheabhsóidh eispéireas a lán daoine!"

msgid "The work on Django itself falls into three major areas:"
msgstr "Tagann an obair ar Django féin i dtrí phríomhréimse:"

msgid "Contributing code"
msgstr "Cód rannpháirteach"

msgid ""
"Fix a bug, or add a new feature. You can make a pull request and see **your "
"code** in the next version of Django."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht, nó cuir gné nua leis. Is féidir leat iarratas tarraingthe a "
"dhéanamh agus **do chód** a fheiceáil sa chéad leagan eile de Django."

msgid "Contributing documentation"
msgstr "Doiciméadú ranní"

msgid ""
"Django's documentation is one of its key strengths. It's informative and "
"thorough. You can help to improve the documentation and keep it relevant as "
"the framework evolves."
msgstr ""
"Tá cáipéisíocht Django ar cheann dá phríomhláidreachtaí. Tá sé faisnéiseach "
"agus críochnúil. Is féidir leat cabhrú leis an doiciméadú a fheabhsú agus é "
"a choinneáil ábhartha de réir mar a fhorbraíonn an creat."

msgid "Localizing Django"
msgstr "Logáil Django"

msgid ""
"Django is translated into over 100 languages - There's even some translation "
"for Klingon?! The i18n team is always looking for translators to help "
"maintain and increase language reach."
msgstr ""
"Aistrítear Django go breis agus 100 teanga - Tá roinnt aistriúcháin ann do "
"Chlingon fiú?! Tá foireann i18n ag lorg aistritheoirí i gcónaí chun cabhrú "
"le rochtain teanga a chothabháil agus a mhéadú."

msgid "Other ways of contributing"
msgstr "Bealaí eile chun rannchuidiú"

msgid ""
"Explore additional avenues of contributing to Django beyond coding. Django's "
"`ticket tracker`_ is the central hub for managing issues, improvements, and "
"contributions to Django. It's a valuable resource where you can report bugs "
"you encounter or assist in triaging existing tickets to ensure a smooth "
"development workflow."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Django also has a :ref:`process for suggesting ideas <requesting-features>` "
"where you can join the community in discussing ideas for new features. "
"Beyond the Django codebase, there's a `vibrant ecosystem`_ that is "
"maintained by the community that you can contribute to."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Explore the ways you can make a difference below, and join us in making "
"Django better for everyone."
msgstr ""

msgid "We're looking forward to working with you. Welcome aboard!"
msgstr "Táimid ag tnúth le bheith ag obair leat. Fáilte ar bord!"

msgid ""
"Various parts of Django, such as the admin site and validation error "
"messages, are internationalized. This means they display differently "
"depending on each user's language or country. For this, Django uses the same "
"internationalization and localization infrastructure available to Django "
"applications, described in the :doc:`i18n documentation </topics/i18n/"
"index>`."
msgstr ""
"Déantar codanna éagsúla de Django, mar an suíomh riaracháin agus "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide bailíochtaithe, a idirnáisiúnú. Ciallaíonn sé seo "
"go dtaispeánann siad go difriúil ag brath ar theanga nó tír gach úsáideora. "
"Chuige seo, úsáideann Django an bonneagar idirnáisiúnaithe agus logánaithe "
"céanna atá ar fáil d’fheidhmchláir Django, a bhfuil cur síos air "
"sa :doc:`i18n document </topics/i18n/index>`."

msgid "Translations"
msgstr "Aistriúcháin"

msgid ""
"Translations are contributed by Django users worldwide. The translation work "
"is coordinated at `Transifex`_."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann úsáideoirí Django aistriúcháin ar fud an domhain. Comhordaítear an "
"obair aistriúcháin ag `Transifex`_."

msgid ""
"If you find an incorrect translation or want to discuss specific "
"translations, go to the `Django project page`_. If you would like to help "
"out with translating or adding a language that isn't yet translated, here's "
"what to do:"
msgstr ""
"Má aimsíonn tú aistriúchán mícheart nó má theastaíonn uait aistriúcháin "
"shonracha a phlé, téigh chuig leathanach tionscadail `Django`_. Más mian "
"leat cabhrú le teanga nach bhfuil aistrithe go fóill a aistriú nó a chur "
"leis, seo cad atá le déanamh:"

msgid "Introduce yourself on the `Django internationalization forum`_."
msgstr "Cuir tú féin in aithne ar an `fóram idirnáisiúnaithe Django `_."

msgid "Make sure you read the notes about :ref:`specialties-of-django-i18n`."
msgstr "Déan cinnte go léann tú na nótaí fao:ref: `speicties-of-django-i18n`."

msgid "Sign up at `Transifex`_ and visit the `Django project page`_."
msgstr ""
"Cláraigh ag `Transifex`_ agus tabhair cuairt ar leathanach tionscadail "
"`Django`_."

msgid ""
"On the `Django project page`_, choose the language you want to work on, "
"**or** -- in case the language doesn't exist yet -- request a new language "
"team by clicking on the \"Request language\" link and selecting the "
"appropriate language."
msgstr ""
"Ar an leathanach `Django`_, roghnaigh an teanga ar mhaith leat oibriú air, "
"**nó** - i gcás nach bhfuil an teanga ann fós - iarr foireann nua teanga trí "
"chliceáil ar an nasc “Iarr teanga” agus an teanga iomchuí a roghnú."

msgid ""
"Then, click the \"Join this Team\" button to become a member of this team. "
"Every team has at least one coordinator who is responsible to review your "
"membership request. You can also contact the team coordinator to clarify "
"procedural problems and handle the actual translation process."
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cliceáil ar an gcnaipe \"Bí páirteach san Fhoireann seo\" chun bheith "
"i do bhall den fhoireann seo. Tá comhordaitheoir amháin ar a laghad ag gach "
"foireann atá freagrach as d’iarratas ballraíochta a athbhreithniú. Is féidir "
"leat dul i dteagmháil le comhordaitheoir na foirne freisin chun fadhbanna "
"nós imeachta a shoiléiriú agus chun an próiseas aistriúcháin féin a "
"láimhseáil."

msgid ""
"Once you are a member of a team choose the translation resource you want to "
"update on the team page. For example, the \"core\" resource refers to the "
"translation catalog that contains all non-contrib translations. Each of the "
"contrib apps also has a resource (prefixed with \"contrib\")."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú ina bhall d'fhoireann roghnaigh an acmhainn aistriúcháin "
"is mian leat a nuashonrú ar leathanach na foirne. Mar shampla, tagraíonn an "
"acmhainn “croí” don chatalóg aistriúcháin ina bhfuil gach aistriúchán neamh-"
"chonraitheach. Tá acmhainn ag gach ceann de na feidhmchláir contrib freisin "
"(réamhshocraithe le “contrib”)."

msgid ""
"For more information about how to use Transifex, read the `Transifex User "
"Guide`_."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi conas Transifex a úsáid, léigh an "
"`Treoir Úsáideora Transifex`_."

msgid ""
"Translations from Transifex are only integrated into the Django repository "
"at the time of a new :term:`feature release <Feature release>`. We try to "
"update them a second time during one of the following :term:`patch release "
"<Patch release>`\\s, but that depends on the translation manager's "
"availability. So don't miss the string freeze period (between the release "
"candidate and the feature release) to take the opportunity to complete and "
"fix the translations for your language!"
msgstr ""
"<Feature release>Ní dhéantar aistriúcháin ó Transifex a chomhtháthú ach sa "
"stór Django tráth nua:term: `scaoileadh gné `. Déanaimid iarracht iad a "
"nuashonrú an dara huair le linn ceann de <Patch release>na nithe seo a "
"leanas: téarma: `scaoileadh paiste `\\ s, ach braitheann sé sin ar "
"infhaighteacht an bhainisteora aistriúcháin. Mar sin ná caill an tréimhse "
"reoite teaghrán (idir an t-iarrthóir scaoilte agus an scaoileadh gné) chun "
"an deis a thapú na haistriúcháin do do theanga a chur i gcrích agus a shocrú!"

msgid "Formats"
msgstr "Formáidí"

msgid ""
"You can also review ``conf/locale/<locale>/formats.py``. This file describes "
"the date, time and numbers formatting particularities of your locale. "
"See :doc:`/topics/i18n/formatting` for details."
msgstr ""
"<locale>Is féidir leat athbhreithniú a dhéanamh freisin ar `conf/locale/ /"
"formats.py ``. Déanann an comhad seo cur síos ar shainiúlachtaí formáidithe "
"dáta, am agus uimhreacha do shuímh áitiúil. Féach: doc: `/topics/i18n/"
"formatting` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The format files aren't managed by the use of Transifex. To change them, you "
"must:"
msgstr ""
"Ní bhainistítear na comhaid formáide trí úsáid Transifex. Chun iad a athrú, "
"ní mór duit:"

msgid ""
":doc:`Create a pull request<writing-code/submitting-patches>` against the "
"Django Git ``main`` branch, as for any code change."
msgstr ""
":doc: `Cruthaigh iarratas tarraing` i gcoinne brainse `@@<writing-code/"
"submitting-patches> `main`` Django Git, mar aon athrú cód."

msgid ""
"Open a ticket in Django's ticket system, set its ``Component`` field to "
"``Translations``, set the \"has patch\" flag, and include the link to the "
"pull request."
msgstr ""
"Oscail ticéad i gcóras ticéad Django, socraigh a réimse ``Comhpháirte`` go "
"``Aistriúcháin ``, socraigh an bratach “tá paiste”, agus cuir an nasc leis "
"an iarratas tarraingthe san áireamh."

msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "Doiciméadúchán"

msgid ""
"There is also an opportunity to translate the documentation, though this is "
"a huge undertaking to complete entirely (you have been warned!). We use the "
"same `Transifex tool <https://app.transifex.com/django/django-docs/>`_. The "
"translations will appear at ``https://docs.djangoproject.com/<language_code>/"
"`` when at least the ``docs/intro/*`` files are fully translated in your "
"language."
msgstr ""
"Tá deis ann freisin an doiciméadú a aistriú, cé gur gnóthas ollmhór é seo le "
"críochnú go hiomlán (tugadh rabhadh duit!). Úsáidimid an uirlis chéanna "
"`Transifex`_. < https://app.transifex.com/django/django-docs/> Beidh na "
"haistriúcháin le feiceáil ag ``https://docs.djangoproject.com/ "
"<language_code>/`` nuair a bheidh na comhaid `docs/intro/*`` ar a laghad "
"aistrithe go hiomlán i do theanga."

msgid ""
"Once translations are published, updated versions from Transifex will be "
"irregularly ported to the `django/django-docs-translations <https://"
"github.com/django/django-docs-translations>`_ repository and to the "
"documentation website. Only translations for the latest stable Django "
"release are updated."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh na haistriúcháin foilsithe, déanfar leaganacha nuashonraithe "
"ó Transifex a aistriú go neamhrialta chuig an stór `django/django-docs-"
"translations <https://github.com/django/django-docs-translations>`_ agus "
"chuig an stór doiciméadaithe. Ní dhéantar ach aistriúcháin don scaoileadh "
"cobhsaí Django is déanaí a nuashonrú."

msgid "Advice for new contributors"
msgstr "Comhairle do rannpháirtithe nua"

msgid ""
"New contributor and not sure what to do? Want to help but just don't know "
"how to get started? This is the section for you."
msgstr ""
"Ranníocóir nua agus nach bhfuil cinnte cad atá le déanamh? Ar mhaith leat "
"cabhrú ach níl a fhios agat conas tosú? Is é seo an chuid duitse."

msgid "Get up and running!"
msgstr "Téigh suas agus ag rith!"

msgid ""
"If you are new to contributing to Django, the :doc:`/intro/contributing` "
"tutorial will give you an introduction to the tools and the workflow."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú nua ag cur le Django, tabharfaidh an rang teagaisc: :doc: `/intro/"
"rannpháirtíoch` réamhrá duit ar na huirlisí agus ar an sreabhadh oibre."

msgid ""
"This page contains more general advice on ways you can contribute to Django, "
"and how to approach that."
msgstr ""
"Tá comhairle níos ginearálta ar an leathanach seo maidir le bealaí is féidir "
"leat cur le Django, agus conas dul chuige sin."

msgid ""
"If you are looking for a reference on the details of making code "
"contributions, see the :doc:`/internals/contributing/writing-code/index` "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag lorg teistiméireachta ar na sonraí maidir le ranníocaíochtaí cód "
"a dhéanamh, féach an doiciméadú :doc:`/inmheánach/ranníocaíocht/cód-scríobh/"
"innéacs`."

msgid "First steps"
msgstr "Na chéad chéimeanna"

msgid "Start with these steps to discover Django's development process."
msgstr ""
"Tosaigh leis na céimeanna seo chun próiseas forbartha Django a fháil amach."

msgid "Triage tickets"
msgstr "Ticéid triage"

msgid ""
"If an `unreviewed ticket`_ reports a bug, try and reproduce it. If you can "
"reproduce it and it seems valid, make a note that you confirmed the bug and "
"accept the ticket. Make sure the ticket is filed under the correct component "
"area. Consider writing a patch that adds a test for the bug's behavior, even "
"if you don't fix the bug itself. See more at :ref:`how-can-i-help-with-"
"triaging`"
msgstr ""
"Má thuairiscíonn `ticéad gan athbhreithniúnaí' _ fabht, déan iarracht é a "
"atáirgeadh. Más féidir leat é a atáirgeadh agus is cosúil go bhfuil sé "
"bailí, déan nóta gur dheimhnigh tú an fabht agus glacann tú leis an ticéad. "
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil an ticéad comhdaithe faoin limistéar comhpháirt "
"cheart. Smaoinigh ar phaiste a scríobh a chuireann tástáil ar iompar an "
"fhabhta, fiú mura ndéanann tú an fabht féin a shocrú. Féach tuilleadh "
"ag:ref: `how can-i-help-with-triaging`"

msgid "Review patches of accepted tickets"
msgstr "Athbhreithniú ar phaistí ticéid"

msgid ""
"This will help you build familiarity with the codebase and processes. Mark "
"the appropriate flags if a patch needs docs or tests. Look through the "
"changes a patch makes, and keep an eye out for syntax that is incompatible "
"with older but still supported versions of Python. :doc:`Run the tests </"
"internals/contributing/writing-code/unit-tests>` and make sure they pass. "
"Where possible and relevant, try them out on a database other than SQLite. "
"Leave comments and feedback!"
msgstr ""
"Cuideoidh sé seo leat eolas a thógáil ar an mbunachar cóid agus ar na "
"próisis. Marcáil na bratacha cuí má theastaíonn doiciméid nó tástálacha ó "
"phaiste. Féach tríd na hathruithe a dhéanann paiste, agus coinnigh súil "
"amach ar chomhréireacht atá neamhchomhoiriúnach le leaganacha níos sine ach "
"le tacaíocht fós de Python. :doc: `Rith na tástálacha' agus déan cinnte go "
"d</internals/contributing/writing-code/unit-tests> téann siad. Nuair is "
"féidir agus ábhartha, bain triail as iad ar bhunachar sonraí seachas SQLite. "
"Fág tuairimí agus aiseolas!"

msgid "Keep old patches up-to-date"
msgstr "Coinnigh sean-phaistí cothrom"

msgid ""
"Oftentimes the codebase will change between a patch being submitted and the "
"time it gets reviewed. Make sure it still applies cleanly and functions as "
"expected. Updating a patch is both useful and important! See more "
"on :doc:`writing-code/submitting-patches`."
msgstr ""
"Is minic a athróidh an bunachar cóid idir paiste atá á chur isteach agus an "
"t-am a athbhreithniú air. Déan cinnte go bhfuil feidhm aige go glan fós agus "
"feidhmíonn sé mar a bhíothas ag Tá sé úsáideach agus tábhachtach paiste a "
"nuashonrú! Féach tuilleadh ar:doc: `scríbhneoireach-code/submitting-patches`."

msgid "Write some documentation"
msgstr "Scríobh roinnt doiciméad"

msgid ""
"Django's documentation is great but it can always be improved. Did you find "
"a typo? Do you think that something should be clarified? Go ahead and "
"suggest a documentation patch! See also the guide on :doc:`writing-"
"documentation`."
msgstr ""
"Tá cáipéisíocht Django iontach ach is féidir é a fheabhsú i gcónaí. An "
"bhfuair tú clóscríobh? An gceapann tú gur chóir rud éigin a shoiléiriú? "
"Téigh ar aghaidh agus moladh paiste doiciméadaithe! Féach freisin an treoir "
"ar:doc: `scríbhneoireach-doiciméadúcháin `."

msgid ""
"The `reports page`_ contains links to many useful Trac queries, including "
"several that are useful for triaging tickets and reviewing patches as "
"suggested above."
msgstr ""
"Tá naisc chuig go leor ceisteanna úsáideacha Trac san `leathanach "
"tuairiscí`_, lena n-áirítear roinnt atá úsáideach chun ticéid a thriail agus "
"chun paistí a athbhreithniú mar a mholtar thuas."

msgid "Sign the Contributor License Agreement"
msgstr "Sínigh an Chomhaontú Ceadúnais"

msgid ""
"The code that you write belongs to you or your employer. If your "
"contribution is more than one or two lines of code, you need to sign the "
"`CLA`_. See the `Contributor License Agreement FAQ`_ for a more thorough "
"explanation."
msgstr ""
"Is leat féin nó le d’fhostóir an cód a scríobhann tú. Má tá do ranníocaíocht "
"níos mó ná líne nó dhó de chód, ní mór duit an `CLA`_ a shíniú. Féach ar an "
"`Ceisteanna Coitianta ar an gComhaontú um Cheadúnas Ranníocóra`_ le haghaidh "
"míniú níos cruinne."

msgid "Guidelines"
msgstr "Treorlínte"

msgid ""
"As a newcomer on a large project, it's easy to experience frustration. "
"Here's some advice to make your work on Django more useful and rewarding."
msgstr ""
"Mar núíosach ar thionscadal mór, is furasta frustrachas a fháil. Seo roinnt "
"comhairle chun do chuid oibre ar Django a dhéanamh níos úsáideach agus níos "
"luachmhaire."

msgid "Pick a subject area"
msgstr "Roghnaigh réimse ábhair"

msgid ""
"This should be something that you care about, that you are familiar with or "
"that you want to learn about. You don't already have to be an expert on the "
"area you want to work on; you become an expert through your ongoing "
"contributions to the code."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo rud a bhfuil cúram ort faoi, a bhfuil eolas agat "
"air nó ar mhaith leat foghlaim faoi. Ní gá duit a bheith ina shaineolaí "
"cheana féin ar an réimse is mian leat oibriú air; bíonn tú i do shaineolaí "
"trí do chuid ranníocaíochtaí leanúnacha leis an gcód."

msgid "Analyze tickets' context and history"
msgstr "Déan anailís ar chomhthéacs agus stair tic"

msgid ""
"Trac isn't an absolute; the context is just as important as the words. When "
"reading Trac, you need to take into account who says things, and when they "
"were said. Support for an idea two years ago doesn't necessarily mean that "
"the idea will still have support. You also need to pay attention to who "
"*hasn't* spoken -- for example, if an experienced contributor hasn't been "
"recently involved in a discussion, then a ticket may not have the support "
"required to get into Django."
msgstr ""
"Ní iomlán é Trac; tá an comhthéacs chomh tábhachtach leis na focail. Agus "
"Trac á léamh agat, ní mór duit a chur san áireamh cé a deir rudaí, agus "
"nuair a dúradh iad. Ní gá go gciallaíonn tacaíocht do smaoineamh dhá bhliain "
"ó shin go mbeidh tacaíocht ag an smaoineamh fós. Ní mór duit aird a "
"thabhairt freisin ar cé náir* labhair - mar shampla, mura raibh ranníocóir a "
"bhfuil taithí acu páirteach i bplé le déanaí, ansin b'fhéidir nach mbeidh an "
"tacaíocht a theastaíonn ag ticéad chun dul isteach i Django."

msgid "Start small"
msgstr "Tosaigh beag"

msgid ""
"It's easier to get feedback on a little issue than on a big one. See the "
"`easy pickings`_."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé níos éasca aiseolas a fháil ar cheist bheag ná ar cheann mór. Féach na "
"“roghnaithe éasca” _."

msgid "Confirm support before engaging in a big task"
msgstr "Deimhnigh tacaíocht sula ndéanann tú tasc mór"

msgid ""
"This means getting someone else to confirm that a bug is real before you fix "
"the issue, and ensuring that there's consensus on a proposed feature before "
"you go implementing it."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo duine eile a fháil chun a dheimhniú go bhfuil fabht fíor "
"sula ndéanann tú an cheist a shocrú, agus a chinntiú go bhfuil comhaontú ar "
"ghné atá beartaithe sula dtéann tú i bhfeidhm í."

msgid "Be bold! Leave feedback!"
msgstr "Bí trom! Fág aiseolas!"

msgid ""
"Sometimes it can be scary to put your opinion out to the world and say "
"\"this ticket is correct\" or \"this patch needs work\", but it's the only "
"way the project moves forward. The contributions of the broad Django "
"community ultimately have a much greater impact than that of any one person. "
"We can't do it without **you**!"
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta is féidir go mbeadh sé scanrúil do thuairim a chur amach don "
"domhan agus a rá “tá an ticéad seo ceart” nó “teastaíonn obair ón bpaiste "
"seo”, ach is é seo an t-aon bhealach a bhogann an tionscadal ar aghaidh. "
"Bíonn tionchar i bhfad níos mó ag ranníocaíochtaí pobal leathan Django sa "
"deireadh ná tionchar ag aon duine amháin. Ní féidir linn é a dhéanamh "
"gan**tús**!"

msgid "Be cautious when marking things \"Ready For Check-in\""
msgstr "Bí cúramach agus rudaí á mharcáil “Réidh le Seiceáil isteach”"

msgid ""
"If you're really not certain if a ticket is ready, don't mark it as such. "
"Leave a comment instead, letting others know your thoughts. If you're mostly "
"certain, but not completely certain, you might also try asking on the "
"``#contributing-getting-started`` channel in the `Django Discord server`_ to "
"see if someone else can confirm your suspicions."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú cinnte i ndáiríre an bhfuil ticéad réidh, ná déan é a "
"mharcáil mar sin. Fág trácht ina ionad sin, ag cur in iúl do chuid smaointe "
"do dhaoine eile. Má tá tú cinnte den chuid is mó, ach nach bhfuil tú cinnte "
"go hiomlán, b'fhéidir go ndéanfá iarracht a iarraidh ar an gcainéal "
"``#contributing -getting-started`` sa fhreastalaí `Django Discord`_ chun a "
"fheiceáil an féidir le duine eile d'amhras a dhearbhú."

msgid "Wait for feedback, and respond to feedback that you receive"
msgstr "Fan le haghaidh aiseolas, agus freagra ar aiseolas a fhaigheann tú"

msgid ""
"Focus on one or two tickets, see them through from start to finish, and "
"repeat. The shotgun approach of taking on lots of tickets and letting some "
"fall by the wayside ends up doing more harm than good."
msgstr ""
"Dírigh ar thicéad amháin nó dhó, féach iad ó thús go deireadh, agus déan "
"arís. Críochnaíonn an cur chuige gunna a bhaineann le go leor ticéad a "
"ghlacadh agus ligean do chuid acu titim ar thaobh an bhealaigh níos mó "
"díobhála ná leas."

msgid "Be rigorous"
msgstr "Bí dian"

msgid ""
"When we say \":pep:`8`, and must have docs and tests\", we mean it. If a "
"patch doesn't have docs and tests, there had better be a good reason. "
"Arguments like \"I couldn't find any existing tests of this feature\" don't "
"carry much weight. While it may be true, that means you have the extra-"
"important job of writing the very first tests for that feature, not that you "
"get a pass from writing tests altogether."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a deirimid “:pep: `8`, agus caithfimid doiciméid agus tástálacha a "
"bheith againn”, ciallaíonn muid é. Mura bhfuil doiciméid agus tástálacha ag "
"paiste, b'fhearr go mbeadh cúis mhaith ann. Ní bhíonn mórán meáchain ag "
"argóintí mar “Ní raibh mé in ann aon tástálacha atá ann cheana ar an ngné "
"seo a fháil”. Cé go bhféadfadh sé a bheith fíor, ciallaíonn sé sin go bhfuil "
"an post thábhachtach agat na chéad tástálacha a scríobh don ghné sin, ní go "
"bhfaigheann tú pas ó thástálacha scríbhneoireachta ar fad."

msgid "Be patient"
msgstr "Bí foighneach"

msgid ""
"It's not always easy for your ticket or your patch to be reviewed quickly. "
"This isn't personal. There are a lot of tickets and pull requests to get "
"through."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhíonn sé éasca i gcónaí do thicéad nó do phaiste a athbhreithniú go "
"tapa. Níl sé seo pearsanta. Tá a lán ticéad agus iarratais tarraingthe ann "
"chun dul tríd."

msgid ""
"Keeping your patch up to date is important. Review the ticket on Trac to "
"ensure that the *Needs tests*, *Needs documentation*, and *Patch needs "
"improvement* flags are unchecked once you've addressed all review comments."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach do phaiste a choinneáil suas chun dáta. Déan athbhreithniú "
"ar an ticéad ar Trac chun a chinntiú go ndéantar na bratacha *Riachtanas*, "
"*Doiciméadú Riachtanacha*, agus *Caithfear feabhsú ar phais* a sheiceáil "
"nuair a bheidh aghaidh agat ar gach trácht athbhreithnithe."

msgid ""
"Remember that Django has an eight-month release cycle, so there's plenty of "
"time for your patch to be reviewed."
msgstr ""
"Cuimhnigh go bhfuil timthriall scaoilte ocht mhí ag Django, mar sin tá neart "
"ama ann chun do phaiste a athbhreithniú."

msgid ""
"Finally, a well-timed reminder can help. See :ref:`contributing code FAQ "
"<new-contributors-faq>` for ideas here."
msgstr ""
"Ar deireadh, is féidir le meabhrúchán dea-ama a bheith ina chuidiú. "
"Féach :ref:`cód ranníocach Ceisteanna Coitianta <new-contributors-faq>` le "
"haghaidh smaointe anseo."

msgid "Triaging tickets"
msgstr "Ticéid triail"

msgid ""
"Django uses Trac_ for managing the work on the code base. Trac is a "
"community-tended garden of the bugs people have found and the features "
"Django has decided to add. As in any garden, sometimes there are weeds to be "
"pulled and sometimes there are flowers and vegetables that need picking. We "
"need your help to sort out one from the other, and in the end, we all "
"benefit together."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Like all gardens, we can aspire to perfection, but in reality there's no "
"such thing. Even in the most pristine garden there are still snails and "
"insects. In a community garden there are also helpful people who -- with the "
"best of intentions -- fertilize the weeds and poison the roses. It's the job "
"of the community as a whole to self-manage, keep the problems to a minimum, "
"and educate those coming into the community so that they can become valuable "
"contributing members."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le gach gairdín, is féidir linn a bheith ag súil le foirfeacht, ach i "
"ndáiríre níl aon rud den sórt sin ann. Fiú sa ghairdín is pristine tá "
"seilidí agus feithidí fós ann. I ngairdín pobail tá daoine cabhracha ann "
"freisin - leis an rún is fearr - a thorthú na fiailí agus a nimhionn na "
"rósanna. Is obair an phobail ina iomláine é féin-bhainistiú, na fadhbanna a "
"choinneáil ar a laghad, agus oideachas a chur ar fáil dóibh siúd a thagann "
"isteach sa phobal ionas gur féidir leo a bheith ina mbaill luachmhara "
"rannpháirteach."

msgid ""
"Similarly, while we aim for Trac to be a perfect representation of the state "
"of Django's progress, we acknowledge that this will not happen. By "
"distributing the load of Trac maintenance to the community, we accept that "
"there will be mistakes. Trac is \"mostly accurate\", and we give allowances "
"for the fact that sometimes it will be wrong. That's okay. We're "
"perfectionists with deadlines."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, cé go bhfuil sé mar aidhm againn go mbeidh Trac ina "
"léiriú foirfe ar staid dul chun cinn Django, admhaímid nach dtarlóidh sé "
"seo. Trí ualach cothabhála Trac a dháileadh ar an bpobal, glacaimid leis go "
"mbeidh botúin ann. Tá Trac “cruinn den chuid is mó”, agus tugaimid liúntais "
"as go mbeidh sé mícheart uaireanta. Tá sé sin ceart go leor. Is "
"foirfeachtóirí muid le spriocdhátaí."

msgid ""
"We rely on the community to keep participating, keep tickets as accurate as "
"possible, and raise issues for discussion on the `Django Forum`_ when there "
"is confusion or disagreement."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Django is a community project, and every contribution helps. We can't do "
"this without **you**!"
msgstr ""
"Is tionscadal pobail é Django, agus cabhraíonn gach ranníocaíocht. Ní féidir "
"linn é seo a dhéanamh gan**tús**!"

msgid "Triage workflow"
msgstr "Sreabhadh oibre triage"

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, not all reports in the ticket tracker provide all "
"the :doc:`required details<bugs-and-features>`. A number of tickets have "
"proposed solutions, but those don't necessarily meet all the "
"requirements :ref:`adhering to the guidelines for contributing <patch-"
"style>`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One way to help out is to *triage* tickets that have been created by other "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Bealach amháin le cabhrú amach is ea ticéid a chruthaigh úsáideoirí eile "
"*trialó*."

msgid ""
"Most of the workflow is based around the concept of a ticket's :ref:`triage "
"stages <triage-stages>`. Each stage describes where in its lifetime a given "
"ticket is at any time. Along with a handful of flags, this attribute easily "
"tells us what and who each ticket is waiting on."
msgstr ""
"<triage-stages>Tá an chuid is mó den sreabhadh oibre bunaithe ar choincheap "
"an ticéad: ref: `céimeanna triage `. Déanann gach céim cur síos ar an áit a "
"bhfuil ticéad ar leith ag am ar bith i rith a shaoil. In éineacht le dornán "
"bratacha, insíonn an tréith seo dúinn go héasca cad agus cé a bhfuil gach "
"ticéad ag fanacht air."

msgid "Since a picture is worth a thousand words, let's start there:"
msgstr "Ós rud é gur fiú míle focal pictiúr, tosaímid ansin:"

msgid "Django's ticket triage workflow"
msgstr "Sreabhadh oibre triage ticéad Django"

msgid "We've got two roles in this diagram:"
msgstr "Tá dhá ról againn sa léaráid seo:"

msgid ""
"Mergers: people with commit access who are responsible for making the final "
"decision to merge a change."
msgstr ""
"Cumaisc: daoine a bhfuil rochtain tiomanta acu atá freagrach as an gcinneadh "
"deiridh a dhéanamh athrú a chumasc."

msgid ""
"Ticket triagers: anyone in the Django community who chooses to become "
"involved in Django's development process. Our Trac installation is "
"intentionally left open to the public, and anyone can triage tickets. Django "
"is a community project, and we encourage :ref:`triage by the community<how-"
"can-i-help-with-triaging>`."
msgstr ""
"Trialóirí ticéad: duine ar bith i bpobal Django a roghnaíonn páirt a bheith "
"páirteach i bpróiseas forbartha Django. Fágtar ár suiteáil Trac ar oscailt "
"don phobal d'aon ghnó, agus is féidir le duine ar bith ticéid a thrialú. "
"<how-can-i-help-with-triaging>Is tionscadal pobail é Django, agus "
"spreagaimid:ref: `triage ag an bpobal `."

msgid "By way of example, here we see the lifecycle of an average ticket:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, feicimid saolré meánticéad anseo:"

msgid ""
"Alice creates a ticket and sends an incomplete pull request (no tests, "
"incorrect implementation)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn Alice ticéad agus seolann sí iarratas tarraingt neamhiomlán (gan "
"tástálacha, cur i bhfeidhm mícheart)."

msgid ""
"Bob reviews the pull request, marks the ticket as \"Accepted\", \"needs "
"tests\", and \"patch needs improvement\", and leaves a comment telling Alice "
"how the patch could be improved."
msgstr ""
"Athbhreithníonn Bob an t-iarratas tarraingt, marcálann sé an ticéad mar "
"\"Glactha\", \"tástálacha riachtanas\", agus \"feabhsaítear an paiste\", "
"agus fágann sé nóta ag insint do Alice conas a d'fhéadfaí an paiste a "
"fheabhsú."

msgid ""
"Alice updates the pull request, adding tests (but not changing the "
"implementation). She removes the two flags."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíonn Alice an iarratas tarraingthe, ag cur tástálacha leis (ach gan "
"an cur i bhfeidhm a athrú) Baineann sí an dá bhratach."

msgid ""
"Charlie reviews the pull request and resets the \"patch needs improvement\" "
"flag with another comment about improving the implementation."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Charlie athbhreithniú ar an iarratas tarraingt agus athshocraíonn sé "
"an bhratach “feabhas ar an bpaiste” le trácht eile ar an gcur i bhfeidhm a "
"fheabhsú."

msgid ""
"Alice updates the pull request, fixing the implementation. She removes the "
"\"patch needs improvement\" flag."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíonn Alice an t-iarratas tarraingthe, ag socrú an cur chun Baineann "
"sí an bratach “is gá feabhsú ar phaiste”."

msgid ""
"Daisy reviews the pull request and marks the ticket as \"Ready for checkin\"."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Daisy athbhreithniú ar an iarratas tarraingthe agus marcálann an "
"ticéad mar “Réidh le seiceáil”."

msgid ""
"Jacob, a :ref:`merger <mergers-team>`, reviews the pull request and merges "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Jacob, a: ref: `cumaisc <mergers-team>`, athbhreithniú ar an iarraidh "
"tarraingthe agus cumasc é."

msgid ""
"Some tickets require much less feedback than this, but then again some "
"tickets require much much more."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn i bhfad níos lú aiseolais ná seo le roinnt ticéid, ach ansin arís "
"bíonn i bhfad níos mó ag teastáil ó roinnt ticéid."

msgid "Triage stages"
msgstr "Céimeanna triage"

msgid ""
"Below we describe in more detail the various stages that a ticket may flow "
"through during its lifetime."
msgstr ""
"Anseo thíos déanaimid cur síos níos mionsonraithe ar na céimeanna éagsúla a "
"bhféadfadh ticéad dul tríd le linn a shaolré."

msgid "Unreviewed"
msgstr "Gan athbhreithniú"

msgid ""
"The ticket has not been reviewed by anyone who felt qualified to make a "
"judgment about whether the ticket contained a valid issue or ought to be "
"closed for any of the various reasons."
msgstr ""

msgid "Accepted"
msgstr "Glactha"

msgid ""
"The big gray area! The absolute meaning of \"accepted\" is that the issue "
"described in the ticket is valid and is in some stage of being worked on. "
"Beyond that there are several considerations:"
msgstr ""
"An limistéar mór liath! Is é an brí iomlán a bhaineann le “glacadh leis” ná "
"go bhfuil an tsaincheist a thuairiscítear sa ticéad bailí agus go bhfuil sé "
"i gcéim éigin á n-oibriú air. Thairis sin tá roinnt breithnithe ann:"

msgid "**Accepted + No Flags**"
msgstr "** Glacadh leis + Gan Bratacha**"

msgid ""
"The ticket is valid, but no one has submitted a patch for it yet. Often this "
"means you could safely start writing a fix for it. This is generally more "
"true for the case of accepted bugs than accepted features. A ticket for a "
"bug that has been accepted means that the issue has been verified by at "
"least one triager as a legitimate bug - and should probably be fixed if "
"possible."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For new features, accepted tickets should only exist after the idea has gone "
"through the appropriate :ref:`process for suggesting new features "
"<requesting-features>` and received community and :ref:`Steering Council "
"<steering-council>` approval, or been accepted in a DEP."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Accepted + Has Patch**"
msgstr "** Glactar leis + Tá Paiste aiste**"

msgid ""
"The ticket is waiting for people to review the supplied solution. This means "
"downloading the patch and trying it out, verifying that it contains tests "
"and docs, running the test suite with the included patch, and leaving "
"feedback on the ticket."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ticéad ag fanacht le daoine athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an réiteach a "
"soláthraíodh. Ciallaíonn sé seo an paiste a íoslódáil agus é a thriail, a "
"fhíorú go bhfuil tástálacha agus doiciméid ann, an tsraith tástála a rith "
"leis an bpaiste atá san áireamh, agus aiseolas a fhágáil ar an ticéad."

msgid "**Accepted + Has Patch + Needs ...**"
msgstr "** Glactar leis + Tá Riachtanais Paiste + aige... **"

msgid ""
"This means the ticket has been reviewed, and has been found to need further "
"work. \"Needs tests\" and \"Needs documentation\" are self-explanatory. "
"\"Patch needs improvement\" will generally be accompanied by a comment on "
"the ticket explaining what is needed to improve the code."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo go ndearnadh athbhreithniú ar an ticéad, agus fuarthas "
"amach go dteastaíonn breis oibre Tá “tástálacha riachtanais” agus "
"“Doiciméadú riachtanais” féinmhínithe De ghnáth beidh trácht ar an ticéad ag "
"gabháil le “Feabhsú riachtanach paiste” ag míniú cad atá riachtanach chun an "
"cód a fheabhsú."

msgid "Ready For Checkin"
msgstr "Réidh le haghaidh Seiceála"

msgid ""
"The ticket was reviewed by any member of the community other than the person "
"who supplied the patch and found to meet all the requirements for a commit-"
"ready contribution. A :ref:`merger <mergers-team>` now needs to give a final "
"review prior to being committed."
msgstr ""
"Rinne aon bhall den phobal athbhreithniú ar an ticéad seachas an duine a "
"sholáthair an paiste agus fuair sé amach go gcomhlíonann sé na ceanglais go "
"léir maidir le ranníocaíocht réidh le coiste. A: Tagairt: Caithfidh `cumais "
"<mergers-team>c `athbhreithniú deiridh a thabhairt anois sula ndéantar é."

msgid ""
"There are a lot of pull requests. It can take a while for your patch to get "
"reviewed. See the :ref:`contributing code FAQ<new-contributors-faq>` for "
"some ideas here."
msgstr ""
"Tá a lán iarratais tarraingthe ann. Féadfaidh sé tamall a thógáil go "
"ndéanfar athbhreithniú ar do phaiste. Féach an:ref: `Cóid rannchuidiúcháin "
"Coitianta <new-contributors-faq>`le haghaidh roinnt smaointe anseo."

msgid "Someday/Maybe"
msgstr "Lá éigin/B'fhéidir"

msgid ""
"This stage isn't shown on the diagram. It's used sparingly to keep track of "
"long-term changes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These tickets are uncommon and overall less useful since they don't describe "
"concrete actionable issues."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other triage attributes"
msgstr "Tréithe triage eile"

msgid ""
"A number of flags, appearing as checkboxes in Trac, can be set on a ticket:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir roinnt bratacha, atá le feiceáil mar bhosca seiceála i Trac, a "
"shocrú ar thicéad:"

msgid "Has patch"
msgstr "Tá paiste aiste aige"

msgid ""
"This means the ticket has an associated solution. These will be reviewed to "
"ensure they adhere to the :doc:`documented guidelines <writing-code/"
"submitting-patches>`."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo go bhfuil réiteach gaolmhar ag an ticéad. <writing-code/"
"submitting-patches>Déanfar athbhreithniú orthu seo chun a chinntiú go "
"gcloíonn siad leis na:doc: `treoirlínte doiciméadaithe '."

msgid ""
"The following three fields (Needs documentation, Needs tests, Patch needs "
"improvement) apply only if a patch has been supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheidh feidhm ag na trí réimse seo a leanas (Doiciméadú Riachtanas, "
"Tástálacha Riachtanas, Feabhsú ar Phaistí) ach amháin má tá paiste curtha ar "
"fáil."

msgid "Needs documentation"
msgstr "Ní mór doiciméadú"

msgid ""
"This flag is used for tickets with patches that need associated "
"documentation. Complete documentation of features is a prerequisite before "
"we can check them into the codebase."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an bratach seo le haghaidh ticéid le paistí a dteastaíonn "
"cáipéisíocht ghab Is réamhriachtanas é doiciméadú iomlán na ngnéithe sula "
"bhféadfaimis iad a sheiceáil isteach sa chód bhunachar."

msgid "Needs tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha is gá"

msgid ""
"This flags the patch as needing associated unit tests. Again, this is a "
"required part of a valid contribution."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé seo an paiste de dhíth go bhfuil tástálacha aonaid gaolmhara de "
"dh Arís, is cuid riachtanach é seo de ranníocaíocht bhailí."

msgid "Patch needs improvement"
msgstr "Ní mór feabhsú ar phaiste"

msgid ""
"This flag means that although the ticket *has* a solution, it's not quite "
"ready for checkin. This could mean the patch no longer applies cleanly, "
"there is a flaw in the implementation, or that the code doesn't meet our "
"standards."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn an bratach seo cé go bhfuil réiteach ag an ticéad*, nach bhfuil "
"sé réidh go leor le haghaidh seiceála. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a chiallú nach "
"mbaineann an paiste go glan a thuilleadh, tá locht sa chur i bhfeidhm, nó "
"nach gcomhlíonann an cód ár gcaighdeáin."

msgid "Easy pickings"
msgstr "Piocadh éasca"

msgid "Tickets that would require small, easy, changes."
msgstr "Ticéid a mbeadh athruithe beaga éasca ag teastáil uathu."

msgid "Type"
msgstr "Cineál"

msgid "Tickets should be categorized by *type* between:"
msgstr "Ba chóir ticéid a chatagóiriú de réir *cineál* idir:"

msgid "New Feature"
msgstr "Gné Nua"

msgid "For adding something new."
msgstr "Chun rud éigin nua a chur leis."

msgid "Bug"
msgstr "Bug"

msgid "For when an existing thing is broken or not behaving as expected."
msgstr ""
"Maidir nuair a bhíonn rud atá ann cheana briste nó gan iompar mar a bhíothas "
"ag súil leis."

msgid "Cleanup/optimization"
msgstr "Glanantach/barrfheabhsú"

msgid ""
"For when nothing is broken but something could be made cleaner, better, "
"faster, stronger."
msgstr ""
"Maidir nuair nach bhfuil aon rud briste ach d'fhéadfaí rud éigin a dhéanamh "
"níos glaine, níos fearr, níos gasta, níos láidre."

msgid "Component"
msgstr "Comhpháirt"

msgid ""
"Tickets should be classified into *components* indicating which area of the "
"Django codebase they belong to. This makes tickets better organized and "
"easier to find."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir ticéid a aicmiú ina*comhpháirteanna* a léiríonn cén limistéar den "
"chód bonn Django leis a mbaineann siad. Déanann sé seo ticéid eagraithe níos "
"fearr agus níos éasca a aimsiú."

msgid "Severity"
msgstr "Déine"

msgid ""
"The *severity* attribute is used to identify blockers, that is, issues that "
"should get fixed before releasing the next version of Django. Typically "
"those issues are bugs causing regressions from earlier versions or "
"potentially causing severe data losses. This attribute is quite rarely used "
"and the vast majority of tickets have a severity of \"Normal\"."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an tréith* solúbth* chun blocálaithe a aithint, is é sin, "
"saincheisteanna ba chóir a shocrú sula scaoiltear an chéad leagan eile de "
"Django. De ghnáth is fabhtanna iad na saincheisteanna sin a chuireann "
"aischéimnithe ó leaganacha níos luaithe nó a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ina Is "
"annamh a úsáidtear an tréith seo agus tá déine “Gnáth” ag formhór mór na "
"dticéad."

msgid "Version"
msgstr "Leagan"

msgid ""
"It is possible to use the *version* attribute to indicate in which version "
"the reported bug was identified."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an tréith* leagan* a úsáid chun a léiriú cén leagan a aithníodh an "
"fabht tuairiscithe."

msgid "UI/UX"
msgstr "UI/UX"

msgid ""
"This flag is used for tickets that relate to User Interface and User "
"Experiences questions. For example, this flag would be appropriate for user-"
"facing features in forms or the admin interface."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an bhratach seo le haghaidh ticéid a bhaineann le ceisteanna "
"Comhéadain Úsáideora agus Eispéiris Úsáideora. Mar shampla, bheadh ​​an "
"bhratach seo oiriúnach do ghnéithe atá os comhair úsáideoirí i bhfoirmeacha "
"nó sa chomhéadan riaracháin."

msgid "Cc"
msgstr "Cc"

msgid ""
"You may add your username or email address to this field to be notified when "
"new contributions are made to the ticket."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat d’ainm úsáideora nó do sheoladh ríomhphoist a chur leis an "
"réimse seo le go gcuirfear ar an eolas tú nuair a dhéantar ranníocaíochtaí "
"nua leis an ticéad."

msgid "Keywords"
msgstr "Eochairfhocal"

msgid ""
"With this field you may label a ticket with multiple keywords. This can be "
"useful, for example, to group several tickets on the same theme. Keywords "
"can either be comma or space separated. Keyword search finds the keyword "
"string anywhere in the keywords. For example, clicking on a ticket with the "
"keyword \"form\" will yield similar tickets tagged with keywords containing "
"strings such as \"formset\", \"modelformset\", and \"ManagementForm\"."
msgstr ""
"Leis an réimse seo is féidir leat ticéad a lipéadú le go leor eochairfhocail "
"Is féidir leis seo a bheith úsáideach, mar shampla, chun roinnt ticéid a "
"ghrúpáil ar an téama céanna. Is féidir le heochairfhocail a bheith scartha "
"le camóg nó spás. Faigheann cuardach eochairfhocal an sreang eochairfhocal "
"áit ar bith Mar shampla, cliceáil ar thicéad leis an eochairfhocal “foirm” "
"beidh ticéid den chineál céanna clib le heochairfhocail ina bhfuil teaghráin "
"mar “formset”, “modelformset”, agus “ManagementForm”."

msgid "Closing Tickets"
msgstr "Ticéid Dúnta"

msgid ""
"When a ticket has completed its useful lifecycle, it's time for it to be "
"closed. Closing a ticket is a big responsibility, though. You have to be "
"sure that the issue is really resolved, and you need to keep in mind that "
"the reporter of the ticket may not be happy to have their ticket closed "
"(unless it's fixed!). If you're not certain about closing a ticket, leave a "
"comment with your thoughts instead."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh a shaolré úsáideach críochnaithe ag ticéad, tá sé in am é a "
"dhúnadh. Is freagracht mhór é ticéad a dhúnadh, áfach. Caithfidh tú a bheith "
"cinnte go bhfuil an cheist réiteach i ndáiríre, agus ní mór duit a "
"choinneáil i gcuimhne nach mbeadh tuairisceoir an ticéad sásta a dticéad a "
"bheith dúnta (mura bhfuil sé socraithe!). Mura bhfuil tú cinnte faoi ticéad "
"a dhúnadh, fág trácht le do chuid smaointe ina ionad sin."

msgid "If you do close a ticket, you should always make sure of the following:"
msgstr ""
"Má dhúnann tú ticéad, ba cheart duit na rudaí seo a leanas a chinntiú i "
"gcónaí:"

msgid "Be certain that the issue is resolved."
msgstr "Bí cinnte go bhfuil an cheist réiteach."

msgid "Leave a comment explaining the decision to close the ticket."
msgstr "Fág trácht a mhíníonn an cinneadh an ticéad a dhúnadh."

msgid ""
"If there is a way they can improve the ticket to reopen it, let them know."
msgstr ""
"Má tá bealach ann gur féidir leo an ticéad a fheabhsú chun é a athoscailt, "
"cuir in iúl dóibh."

msgid ""
"If the ticket is a duplicate, reference the original ticket. Also cross-"
"reference the closed ticket by leaving a comment in the original one -- this "
"allows to access more related information about the reported bug or "
"requested feature."
msgstr ""
"Más dúblach an ticéad, déan tagairt don ticéad bunaidh. Déan crostagairt "
"freisin don ticéad dúnta trí nóta tráchta a fhágáil sa bhuntéacs -- "
"ceadaíonn sé seo rochtain a fháil ar fhaisnéis níos gaolmhaire faoin bhfabht "
"tuairiscithe nó faoin ngné iarrtha."

msgid ""
"**Be polite.** No one likes having their ticket closed. It can be "
"frustrating or even discouraging. The best way to avoid turning people off "
"from contributing to Django is to be polite and friendly and to offer "
"suggestions for how they could improve this ticket and other tickets in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"**Bí póilíneach.** Ní maith le duine ar bith a dticéad a bheith dúnta. "
"D'fhéadfadh sé a bheith frustrach nó fiú díspreagach. Is é an bealach is "
"fearr chun daoine a chasadh as cur le Django ná a bheith béasach agus "
"cairdiúil agus moltaí a thairiscint maidir le conas a d'fhéadfaidís an "
"ticéad seo agus na ticéid eile a fheabhsú sa todhchaí."

msgid "A ticket can be resolved in a number of ways:"
msgstr "Is féidir ticéad a réiteach ar roinnt bealaí:"

msgid "fixed"
msgstr "socraithe"

msgid "Used once a patch has been rolled into Django and the issue is fixed."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear nuair a bheidh paiste rollta isteach i Django agus socraítear an "
"tsaincheist."

msgid "invalid"
msgstr "neamhbhailí"

msgid ""
"Used if the ticket is found to be incorrect. This means that the issue in "
"the ticket is actually the result of a user error, or describes a problem "
"with something other than Django, or isn't a bug report or feature request "
"at all (for example, some new users submit support queries as tickets)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear má aimsítear go bhfuil an ticéad mícheart. Ciallaíonn sé seo go "
"bhfuil an tsaincheist sa ticéad mar thoradh ar earráid úsáideora i ndáiríre, "
"nó go ndéanann sé cur síos ar fhadhb le rud éigin seachas Django, nó nach "
"tuarascáil fabht nó iarratas ar ghné í ar chor ar bith (mar shampla, "
"cuireann roinnt úsáideoirí nua ceisteanna tacaíochta mar thicéid)."

msgid "wontfix"
msgstr "wontfix"

msgid ""
"Used when someone decides that the request isn't appropriate for "
"consideration in Django. Sometimes a ticket is closed as \"wontfix\" with a "
"request for the reporter to start a discussion on the `Django Forum`_ if "
"they feel differently from the rationale provided by the person who closed "
"the ticket. Other times, a discussion precedes the decision to close a "
"ticket. Always use the forum to get a consensus before reopening tickets "
"closed as \"wontfix\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "duplicate"
msgstr "dúbailt"

msgid ""
"Used when another ticket covers the same issue. By closing duplicate "
"tickets, we keep all the discussion in one place, which helps everyone."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear nuair a chlúdaíonn ticéad eile an cheist chéanna. Trí thicéid "
"dúblacha a dhúnadh, coinnímid an plé go léir in aon áit amháin, rud a "
"chuidíonn le gach duine."

msgid "worksforme"
msgstr "worksforme"

msgid ""
"Used when the ticket doesn't contain enough detail to replicate the original "
"bug."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear nuair nach bhfuil go leor sonraí sa ticéad chun an fabht bunaidh a "
"mhacasamhlú."

msgid "needsinfo"
msgstr "eolas riachtanais"

msgid ""
"Used when the ticket does not contain enough information to replicate the "
"reported issue but is potentially still valid. The ticket should be reopened "
"when more information is supplied."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear é nuair nach mbíonn go leor faisnéise sa ticéad chun an "
"tsaincheist tuairiscithe a mhacasamhlú ach go bhféadfadh sé a bheith bailí "
"fós. Ba cheart an ticéad a athoscailt nuair a chuirtear tuilleadh eolais ar "
"fáil."

msgid ""
"If you believe that the ticket was closed in error -- because you're still "
"having the issue, or it's popped up somewhere else, or the triagers have "
"made a mistake -- please reopen the ticket and provide further information. "
"Again, please do not reopen tickets that have been marked as \"wontfix\" and "
"bring the issue to the `Django Forum`_ instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "How can I help with triaging?"
msgstr "Conas is féidir liom cabhrú le triaging?"

msgid ""
"The triage process is primarily driven by community members. Really, "
"**ANYONE** can help."
msgstr ""
"Tá an próiseas triage á thiomáint go príomha ag baill an phobail. I "
"ndáiríre, is féidir le haon éig** cabhrú."

msgid ""
"To get involved, start by `creating an account on Trac`_. If you have an "
"account but have forgotten your password, you can reset it using the "
"`password reset page`_."
msgstr ""
"Chun páirt a ghlacadh, tosú trí `cuntas a chruthú ar Trac`_. Má tá cuntas "
"agat ach má tá dearmad déanta agat ar do phasfhocal, is féidir leat é a "
"athshocrú ag baint úsáide as an `leathanach athshocraithe pasfhocal`_."

msgid "Then, you can help out by:"
msgstr "Ansin, is féidir leat cabhrú amach trí:"

msgid ""
"Closing \"Unreviewed\" tickets as \"invalid\", \"worksforme\", or "
"\"duplicate\", or \"wontfix\"."
msgstr ""
"Ticéid “Neamhathbhreithnithe” a dhúnadh mar “neamhbhailí”, “worksforme”, nó "
"“dúblach”, nó “wontfix”."

msgid ""
"Closing \"Unreviewed\" tickets as \"needsinfo\" when the description is too "
"sparse to be actionable."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Correcting the \"Needs tests\", \"Needs documentation\", or \"Has patch\" "
"flags for tickets where they are incorrectly set."
msgstr ""
"Na bratacha “Tástálacha Riachtanais”, “Doiciméadú riachtanais”, nó bratacha "
"“Tá paiste” a cheartú le haghaidh ticéid ina bhfuil siad socraithe go "
"mícheart."

msgid ""
"Setting the \"`Easy pickings`_\" flag for tickets that are small and "
"relatively straightforward."
msgstr ""
"Ag socrú an bhratach “Easy picings`_” le haghaidh ticéid atá beag agus "
"réasúnta simplí."

msgid "Set the *type* of tickets that are still uncategorized."
msgstr "Socraigh an cineál* ticéad atá fós gan catagóir."

msgid ""
"Checking that old tickets are still valid. If a ticket hasn't seen any "
"activity in a long time, it's possible that the problem has been fixed but "
"the ticket hasn't yet been closed."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil go bhfuil sean-ticéid fós bailí. Mura bhfaca ticéad aon "
"ghníomhaíocht le fada an lá, is féidir go bhfuil an fhadhb socraithe ach "
"níor dúnadh an ticéad fós."

msgid ""
"Identifying trends and themes in the tickets. If there are a lot of bug "
"reports about a particular part of Django, it may indicate we should "
"consider refactoring that part of the code. If a trend is emerging, you "
"should raise it for discussion (referencing the relevant tickets) on the "
"`Django Forum`_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Verify if solutions submitted by others are correct. If they are correct and "
"also contain appropriate documentation and tests then move them to the "
"\"Ready for Checkin\" stage. If they are not correct then leave a comment to "
"explain why and set the corresponding flags (\"Patch needs improvement\", "
"\"Needs tests\" etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Fíoraigh an bhfuil réitigh a chuireann daoine eile isteach ceart. Má tá siad "
"ceart agus má tá cáipéisíocht agus tástálacha iomchuí iontu freisin, bog iad "
"go dtí an chéim “Réidh le haghaidh Seiceála”. Mura bhfuil siad ceart ansin "
"fág trácht chun míniú cén fáth agus na bratacha comhfhreagracha a shocrú "
"(“Teastaíonn feabhsú ar phaiste”, “Tástálacha riachtanais” srl.)."

msgid ""
"The `Reports page`_ contains links to many useful Trac queries, including "
"several that are useful for triaging tickets and reviewing proposals as "
"suggested above."
msgstr ""
"Tá naisc chuig go leor ceisteanna úsáideacha Trac sa leathanach "
"`Tuairiscí`_, lena n-áirítear roinnt atá úsáideach chun ticéid a thriail "
"agus athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar thograí mar a mholtar thuas."

msgid "You can also find more :doc:`new-contributors`."
msgstr "Is féidir leat tuilleadh a fháil freisin: doc: `new-contributors`."

msgid ""
"However, we do ask the following of all general community members working in "
"the ticket database:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, iarrann muid an méid seo a leanas ó gach ball ginearálta "
"pobail atá ag obair sa bhunachar sonraí ticéad:"

msgid ""
"Please **don't** promote your own tickets to \"Ready for checkin\". You may "
"mark other people's tickets that you've reviewed as \"Ready for checkin\", "
"but you should get at minimum one other community member to review a patch "
"that you submit."
msgstr ""
"Le do thoil, **ná cuir do thicéid féin a chur chun cinn go “Réidh le "
"seiceáil”. Féadfaidh tú ticéid daoine eile a rinne tú athbhreithniú a "
"mharcáil mar “Réidh le seiceáil”, ach ba cheart duit ball pobail amháin eile "
"a fháil ar a laghad chun paiste a chuireann tú isteach a athbhreithniú."

msgid ""
"Please **don't** reverse a decision without posting a message to the `Django "
"Forum`_ to find consensus."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you're unsure if you should be making a change, don't make the change but "
"instead leave a comment with your concerns on the ticket, or post a message "
"to the `Django Forum`_. It's okay to be unsure, but your input is still "
"valuable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bisecting a regression"
msgstr "Aischéimniú a dhíghilt"

msgid ""
"A regression is a bug that's present in some newer version of Django but not "
"in an older one. An extremely helpful piece of information is the commit "
"that introduced the regression. Knowing the commit that caused the change in "
"behavior helps identify if the change was intentional or if it was an "
"inadvertent side-effect. Here's how you can determine this."
msgstr ""
"Is fabht é aischéimniú atá i láthair i roinnt leagan níos nuaí de Django ach "
"ní i gceann níos sine. Píosa faisnéise thar a bheith cabhrach is ea an "
"tiomantas a thug isteach an aischéimniú. Cuidíonn eolas a fháil ar an "
"ngealltanas a bhí ina chúis leis an athrú ar iompar a aithint an raibh an t-"
"athrú d'aon ghnó nó an raibh fo-iarsacht neamhthuigneach ann. Seo mar is "
"féidir leat é seo a chinneadh."

msgid ""
"Begin by writing a regression test for Django's test suite for the issue. "
"For example, we'll pretend we're debugging a regression in migrations. After "
"you've written the test and confirmed that it fails on the latest main "
"branch, put it in a separate file that you can run standalone. For our "
"example, we'll pretend we created ``tests/migrations/test_regression.py``, "
"which can be run with:"
msgstr ""
"Tosaigh trí thástáil aischéimnithe a scríobh do shraith tástála Django don "
"tsaincheist. Mar shampla, ligeanfaimid go bhfuilimid ag dífhabhtú "
"aischéimnithe in imirce. Tar éis duit an tástáil a scríobh agus a dhearbhú "
"go dteipeann air ar an bpríomhbhrainse is déanaí, cuir é i gcomhad ar "
"leithligh ar féidir leat a reáchtáil go neamhspleách Mar shampla, "
"ligeanfaimid go gcruthaíomar ``tests/migrations/test_regression.py``, ar "
"féidir é a reáchtáil le:"

msgid ""
"Next, we mark the current point in history as being \"bad\" since the test "
"fails:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, déanaimid an pointe reatha sa stair a mharcáil mar “dona” ós rud é go "
"dteipeann ar an tástáil:"

msgid ""
"Now, we need to find a point in git history before the regression was "
"introduced (i.e. a point where the test passes). Use something like ``git "
"checkout HEAD~100`` to check out an earlier revision (100 commits earlier, "
"in this case). Check if the test fails. If so, mark that point as \"bad\" "
"(``git bisect bad``), then check out an earlier revision and recheck. Once "
"you find a revision where your test passes, mark it as \"good\":"
msgstr ""
"Anois, ní mór dúinn pointe a aimsiú i stair git sula dtugadh isteach an "
"aischéimniú (ie pointe ina dtéann an tástáil). Úsáid rud éigin cosúil le "
"``git checkout HEAD~100`` chun athbhreithniú níos luaithe a sheiceáil (100 "
"gealltanais níos luaithe, sa chás seo). Seiceáil má theipeann ar an tástáil. "
"Más ea, marcáil an pointe sin mar “olc” (``git bisect bad ``), ansin "
"seiceáil athbhreithniú níos luaithe agus athsheiceáil. Nuair a aimsíonn tú "
"athbhreithniú ina dtéann do thástáil, marcáil é mar “maith”:"

msgid ""
"Now we're ready for the fun part: using ``git bisect run`` to automate the "
"rest of the process:"
msgstr ""
"Anois táimid réidh don chuid spraoi: `git bisect run`` a úsáid chun an chuid "
"eile den phróiseas a uathoibriú:"

msgid ""
"You should see ``git bisect`` use a binary search to automatically checkout "
"revisions between the good and bad commits until it finds the first \"bad\" "
"commit where the test fails."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go bhfeicfeá ``git bisect`` úsáid a bhaint as cuardach dénártha "
"chun na hathbhreithnithe idir maith agus olc a sheiceáil amach go "
"huathoibríoch go dtí go bhfaighidh sé an chéad ghealltanas \"olc\" nuair a "
"theipeann ar an tástáil."

msgid ""
"Now, report your results on the Trac ticket, and please include the "
"regression test as an attachment. When someone writes a fix for the bug, "
"they'll already have your test as a starting point."
msgstr ""
"Anois, tuairiscigh do thorthaí ar an ticéad Trac, agus cuir an tástáil "
"aischéimnithe mar cheangaltán le do thoil. Nuair a scríobhann duine socrú "
"don fhabht, beidh do thástáil acu cheana féin mar phointe tosaigh."

msgid "Coding style"
msgstr "Stíl chódú"

msgid ""
"Please follow these coding standards when writing code for inclusion in "
"Django."
msgstr ""
"Lean na caighdeáin códaithe seo le do thoil agus cód á scríobh agat le cur "
"san áireamh in Django."

msgid "Pre-commit checks"
msgstr "Seiceálacha réamhthiomanta"

msgid ""
"`pre-commit <https://pre-commit.com>`_ is a framework for managing pre-"
"commit hooks. These hooks help to identify simple issues before committing "
"code for review. By checking for these issues before code review it allows "
"the reviewer to focus on the change itself, and it can also help to reduce "
"the number of CI runs."
msgstr ""
"Is creat é `réamh-choimite`_ chun crúca< https://pre-commit.com> í "
"réamhthiomanta a bhainistiú. Cuidíonn na crúcaí seo le saincheisteanna "
"simplí a aithint sula ndéanann siad cód le haghaidh Trí na saincheisteanna "
"seo a sheiceáil roimh athbhreithniú ar chód tugann sé deis don "
"athbhreithneoir díriú ar an athrú féin, agus féadfaidh sé cabhrú freisin le "
"líon na rith CI a laghdú."

msgid "To use the tool, first install ``pre-commit`` and then the git hooks:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an uirlis a úsáid, suiteáil ``pre-chommit`` ar dtús agus ansin na "
"crúcaí git:"

msgid ""
"On the first commit ``pre-commit`` will install the hooks, these are "
"installed in their own environments and will take a short while to install "
"on the first run. Subsequent checks will be significantly faster. If an "
"error is found an appropriate error message will be displayed. If the error "
"was with ``black`` or ``isort`` then the tool will go ahead and fix them for "
"you. Review the changes and re-stage for commit if you are happy with them."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcéad tiomantas suiteálfaidh ``réamh-choimite`` na crúcaí, "
"suiteáiltear iad seo ina dtimpeallachtaí féin agus tógfaidh siad tamall "
"gairid iad a shuiteáil ar an gcéad rith. Beidh seiceálacha ina dhiaidh sin i "
"bhfad níos tapa Má aimsítear earráid taispeánfar teachtaireacht earráide "
"iomchuí. Má bhí an earráid le ``dub`` nó ``isort`` ansin rachaidh an uirlis "
"ar aghaidh agus iad a shocrú duit. Déan athbhreithniú ar na hathruithe agus "
"déan athchéim a dhéanamh le tiomantas má tá tú sásta leo."

msgid "Python style"
msgstr "Stíl Python"

msgid ""
"All files should be formatted using the :pypi:`black` auto-formatter. This "
"will be run by ``pre-commit`` if that is configured."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir gach comhad a fhormáidiú ag baint úsáide as an uath-"
"fhormáiditheoir: pypi: `black`. Reáchtálfaidh ``réamh-chommit`` é seo má tá "
"sé sin cumraithe."

msgid ""
"The project repository includes an ``.editorconfig`` file. We recommend "
"using a text editor with `EditorConfig`_ support to avoid indentation and "
"whitespace issues. The Python files use 4 spaces for indentation and the "
"HTML files use 2 spaces."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn stór an tionscadail comhad ``.editorconfig``. Molaimid eagarthóir "
"téacs a úsáid le tacaíocht `EditorConfig`_ chun saincheisteanna insint agus "
"spás bán a sheachaint. Úsáideann na comhaid Python 4 spás le haghaidh "
"ionchur agus úsáideann na comhaid HTML 2 spás."

msgid "Unless otherwise specified, follow :pep:`8`."
msgstr "Mura sonraítear a mhalairt, lean: pep: `8`."

msgid ""
"Use :pypi:`flake8` to check for problems in this area. Note that our "
"``.flake8`` file excludes some errors that we don't consider as gross "
"violations. Remember that :pep:`8` is only a guide, so respect the style of "
"the surrounding code as a primary goal."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An exception to :pep:`8` is our rules on line lengths. Don't limit lines of "
"code to 79 characters if it means the code looks significantly uglier or is "
"harder to read. We allow up to 88 characters as this is the line length used "
"by ``black``. This check is included when you run ``flake8``. Documentation, "
"comments, and docstrings should be wrapped at 79 characters, even "
"though :pep:`8` suggests 72."
msgstr ""
"Eisceacht to:pep: `8` is iad ár rialacha maidir le fad líne. Ná teorainn le "
"línte cód go 79 carachtar má chiallaíonn sé go bhfuil cuma níos gránna ar an "
"gcód nó go bhfuil sé níos deacra é a léamh. Ceadaímid suas le 88 carachtar "
"mar is é seo an fad líne a úsáideann ``dub`. Cuirtear an seiceáil seo san "
"áireamh nuair a ritheann tú ``flake8``. Ba chóir doiciméadú, tráchtanna, "
"agus docstrings a fhilleadh ag 79 carachtar, fiú cé go molann: pep: `8` 72."

msgid ""
"String variable interpolation may use :py:ref:`%-formatting <old-string-"
"formatting>`, :py:ref:`f-strings <f-strings>`, or :py:meth:`str.format` as "
"appropriate, with the goal of maximizing code readability."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh idirphóireacht athraitheach teaghrána:py:ref: `%-formáidiú "
"`, :py:ref:` <old-string-formatting>f-strings `, nó:py:meth: `str.format` "
"mar is cuí, leis an aidhm léiteacht cód a uasmh <f-strings>éadú."

msgid ""
"Final judgments of readability are left to the Merger's discretion. As a "
"guide, f-strings should use only plain variable and property access, with "
"prior local variable assignment for more complex cases::"
msgstr ""
"Fágtar breithiúnais dheiridh ar inléiteacht faoi rogha an Cumaisc. Mar "
"threoir, níor cheart go n-úsáidfeadh f-teaghráin ach rochtain shimplí athróg "
"agus réadmhaoin, le sannadh athróg áitiúil roimhe seo le haghaidh cásanna "
"níos casta:"

msgid ""
"f-strings should not be used for any string that may require translation, "
"including error and logging messages. In general ``format()`` is more "
"verbose, so the other formatting methods are preferred."
msgstr ""
"níor cheart f-teaghráin a úsáid le haghaidh teaghrán ar bith a bhféadfadh "
"aistriúchán a bheith ag teastáil uaidh, lena n-áirítear teachtaireachtaí "
"earráide agus logáil. Go ginearálta bíonn ``formáid()`` níos briathartha, "
"mar sin is fearr na modhanna formáidithe eile."

msgid ""
"Don't waste time doing unrelated refactoring of existing code to adjust the "
"formatting method."
msgstr ""
"Ná cuir am amú ag déanamh athfhachtóirí neamhghaolmhara ar an gcód atá ann "
"cheana chun an modh formáidithe a choigeartú."

msgid ""
"Avoid use of \"we\" in comments, e.g. \"Loop over\" rather than \"We loop "
"over\"."
msgstr ""
"Seachain úsáid “muid” i dtráchtanna, m.sh. “Lúb thar” seachas “Táimid lúb "
"thart”."

msgid ""
"Use underscores, not camelCase, for variable, function and method names "
"(i.e. ``poll.get_unique_voters()``, not ``poll.getUniqueVoters()``)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid béim, ní CamelCase, le haghaidh ainmneacha athróg, feidhm agus modh "
"(ie ``poll.get_unique_votes () ``, ní ``poll.getUniqueVoters ()``)."

msgid ""
"Use ``InitialCaps`` for class names (or for factory functions that return "
"classes)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``InitialCaps`` le haghaidh ainmneacha ranga (nó le haghaidh "
"feidhmeanna monarcha a thugann ranganna ar ais)."

msgid "In docstrings, follow the style of existing docstrings and :pep:`257`."
msgstr "I docstrings, lean stíl na docstrings atá ann cheana agus: pep: `257`."

msgid ""
"In tests, use :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertRaisesMessage` "
"and :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertWarnsMessage` instead "
"of :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertRaises` "
"and :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertWarns` so you can check the exception or "
"warning message. Use :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertRaisesRegex` "
"and :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertWarnsRegex` only if you need regular "
"expression matching."
msgstr ""
"I dtástálacha, bain úsáid ai:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestcase.assertRaisesMessage` agus:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase.assertWarnsMessage` in ionad:meth: "
"`~UnitTest.TestCase.AsserTraises` agus:meth: `~UnitTest.TestCase.Asserns` "
"ionas gur féidir leat an eisceacht nó teachtaireacht rabhaidh. Úsáid: Meth: "
"`~UnitTest.TestCase.AsserTraisesRegex` agus:meth: "
"`~UnitTest.TestCase.AssertWarnsRegex` ach amháin má theastaíonn meaitseáil "
"léirithe rialta uait."

msgid ""
"Use :meth:`assertIs(…, True/False)<unittest.TestCase.assertIs>` for testing "
"boolean values, rather than :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertTrue` "
"and :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertFalse`, so you can check the actual "
"boolean value, not the truthiness of the expression."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: Meth: `Assertis (..., True/False) <unittest.TestCase.assertIs>`chun "
"luachanna boolean a thástáil, seachas: meth: `~UnitTest.TestCase.AssertTrue` "
"agus:meth: `~UnitTest.TestCase.assertFalse`, ionas gur féidir leat an luach "
"boolean iarbhír a sheiceáil, ní fírinneacht an abairt."

msgid ""
"In test docstrings, state the expected behavior that each test demonstrates. "
"Don't include preambles such as \"Tests that\" or \"Ensures that\"."
msgstr ""
"I ndocstrings tástála, luaigh an t-iompar a bhfuiltear ag súil leis a "
"léiríonn gach tástáil. Ná cuir réamhshamhlacha mar “Tástálacha sin” nó "
"“Cinntíonn sé sin” san áireamh."

msgid ""
"Reserve ticket references for obscure issues where the ticket has additional "
"details that can't be easily described in docstrings or comments. Include "
"the ticket number at the end of a sentence like this::"
msgstr ""
"Tagairtí ticéad a chur in áirithe le haghaidh saincheisteanna doiléire ina "
"bhfuil sonraí breise sa ticéad nach féidir cur síos a dhéanamh orthu go "
"héasca i ndocstrings nó i dtuairimí. Cuir uimhir an ticéad san áireamh ag "
"deireadh abairt mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Where applicable, use unpacking generalizations compliant with :pep:`448`, "
"such as merging mappings (``{**x, **y}``) or sequences (``[*a, *b]``). This "
"improves performance, readability, and maintainability while reducing errors."
msgstr ""

msgid "Imports"
msgstr "Allmhairí"

msgid ""
"Use :pypi:`isort` to automate import sorting using the guidelines below."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid :pypi:`isort` chun sórtáil iompórtála a uathoibriú ag baint úsáide as "
"na treoirlínte thíos."

msgid "Quick start:"
msgstr "Tús tapa:"

msgid ""
"This runs ``isort`` recursively from your current directory, modifying any "
"files that don't conform to the guidelines. If you need to have imports out "
"of order (to avoid a circular import, for example) use a comment like this::"
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé seo ``isort`` go athshlánach ó d'eolaire reatha, ag modhnú aon "
"chomhaid nach gcomhlíonann leis na treoirlínte. Más gá duit allmhairí a "
"bheith as ord (chun allmhairiú ciorclach a sheachaint, mar shampla) bain "
"úsáid as trácht mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Put imports in these groups: future, standard library, third-party "
"libraries, other Django components, local Django component, try/excepts. "
"Sort lines in each group alphabetically by the full module name. Place all "
"``import module`` statements before ``from module import objects`` in each "
"section. Use absolute imports for other Django components and relative "
"imports for local components."
msgstr ""
"Cuir allmhairí sna grúpaí seo: todhchaí, leabharlann chaighdeánach, "
"leabharlanna tríú páirtí, comhpháirteanna Django eile, comhpháirt áitiúil "
"Django, déan iarracht / seachas. Sórtáil na línte i ngach grúpa in ord "
"aibítre de réir ainm iomlán an mhodúil. Cuir gach ráiteas ``modúil "
"iompórtála`` roimh ``ó réada iompórtála modúil`` i ngach roinn. Bain úsáid "
"as allmhairí absalóideacha le haghaidh comhpháirteanna Django eile agus "
"allmhairí coibhneasta le haghaidh comhpháirteanna áitiúla."

msgid ""
"On each line, alphabetize the items with the upper case items grouped before "
"the lowercase items."
msgstr ""
"Ar gach líne, déan na míreanna aibítir leis na míreanna uachtarcháis atá "
"grúpáilte roimh na míreanna beaga."

msgid ""
"Break long lines using parentheses and indent continuation lines by 4 "
"spaces. Include a trailing comma after the last import and put the closing "
"parenthesis on its own line."
msgstr ""
"Briseadh línte fada ag baint úsáide as lúibíní agus línte leanúna le 4 spás. "
"Cuir camóg siar san áireamh tar éis an allmhairiú deireanach agus cuir an "
"lúibín deiridh ar a líne féin."

msgid ""
"Use a single blank line between the last import and any module level code, "
"and use two blank lines above the first function or class."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid líne bán amháin idir an t-allmhairiú deireanach agus aon chód leibhéal "
"an mhodúil, agus bain úsáid as dhá líne bán os cionn an chéad fheidhm nó an "
"rang."

msgid "For example (comments are for explanatory purposes only):"
msgstr "Mar shampla (tá tuairimí chun críocha míniúcháin amháin):"

msgid "``django/contrib/admin/example.py``"
msgstr "``django/contrib/admin/example.py``"

msgid "Use convenience imports whenever available. For example, do this ::"
msgstr "Úsáid allmhairí áisiúlachta aon uair atá Mar shampla, déan seo:"

msgid "instead of::"
msgstr "in ionad:"

msgid "Template style"
msgstr "Stíl teimpléad"

msgid "Follow the below rules in Django template code."
msgstr "Lean na rialacha thíos i gcód teimpléad Django."

msgid "``{% extends %}`` should be the first non-comment line."
msgstr "Ba chóir gurb é ``{% leathnaíonn%}`` an chéad líne neamh-trácht."

msgid "Do this:"
msgstr "Déan é seo:"

msgid "Or this:"
msgstr "Nó seo:"

msgid "Don't do this:"
msgstr "Ná déan é seo:"

msgid "Put exactly one space between ``{{``, variable contents, and ``}}``."
msgstr ""
"Cuir spás amháin go díreach idir ``{{``, ábhar athraitheach, agus ``}}``."

msgid "In ``{% load ... %}``, list libraries in alphabetical order."
msgstr "I ``{% load...%} `, liostaigh leabharlanna in ord aibítre."

msgid "Put exactly one space between ``{%``, tag contents, and ``%}``."
msgstr "Cuir spás amháin go díreach idir ``{%``, ábhar clibeanna, agus ``%}``."

msgid ""
"Put the ``{% block %}`` tag name in the ``{% endblock %}`` tag if it is not "
"on the same line."
msgstr ""
"Cuir ainm an chlib ``{% block%}`` sa chlib ``{% endblock%}`` mura bhfuil sé "
"ar an líne chéanna."

msgid ""
"Inside curly braces, separate tokens by single spaces, except for around the "
"``.`` for attribute access and the ``|`` for a filter."
msgstr ""
"Taobh istigh de bhraiceanna cuartha, comharthaí ar leithligh de réir "
"spásanna aonair, ach amháin timpeall an ``.`` le haghaidh rochtana tréithe "
"agus an ``|`` le haghaidh scagaire."

msgid ""
"Within a template using ``{% extends %}``, avoid indenting top-level ``{% "
"block %}`` tags."
msgstr ""
"Laistigh de theimpléad ag baint úsáide as ``{% leathnaíonn%}``, seachain "
"clibeanna ``{% block%} `a chur isteach."

msgid "View style"
msgstr "Féach ar stíl"

msgid ""
"In Django views, the first parameter in a view function should be called "
"``request``."
msgstr ""
"I dtuairimí Django, ba chóir “iarratas” a thabhairt ar an gcéad pharaiméadar "
"i bhfeidhm amharc."

msgid "Do this::"
msgstr "Déan seo:"

msgid "Don't do this::"
