msgstr "``def get_absolute_url () ``"

msgid "Any custom methods"
msgstr "Aon mhodhanna saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"If ``choices`` is defined for a given model field, define each choice as a "
"mapping, with an all-uppercase name as a class attribute on the model. "
"Example::"
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhínítear “roghanna” do réimse samhail ar leith, sainmhínigh gach "
"rogha mar mhapáil, le ainm uile-uachtaracha mar thréith aicme ar an "
"tsamhail. Sampla::"

msgid "Alternatively, consider using :ref:`field-choices-enum-types`::"
msgstr ""
"De rogha air sin, smaoinigh ar úsáid:ref: `field-choices-enum-typepes`::"

msgid "Use of ``django.conf.settings``"
msgstr "Úsáid ``django.conf.settings``"

msgid ""
"Modules should not in general use settings stored in "
"``django.conf.settings`` at the top level (i.e. evaluated when the module is "
"imported). The explanation for this is as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir modúil úsáid go ginearálta socruithe a stóráiltear i "
"`django.conf.settings`` ag an leibhéal barr (ie meastóireacht nuair a "
"dhéantar an modúl a allmhairiú). Is é seo a leanas an míniú ar seo:"

msgid ""
"Manual configuration of settings (i.e. not relying on "
"the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment variable) is allowed and "
"possible as follows::"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear cumraíocht láimhe na socruithe (ie gan brath ar an athróg "
"comhshaoil: envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`) agus is féidir mar seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid ""
"However, if any setting is accessed before the ``settings.configure`` line, "
"this will not work. (Internally, ``settings`` is a ``LazyObject`` which "
"configures itself automatically when the settings are accessed if it has not "
"already been configured)."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má dhéantar rochtain ar aon socrú roimh an líne "
"``settings.configure``, ní oibreoidh sé seo. (Go hinmheánach, is "
"``lazyObject`` é `socruithe ``a chumraíonn é féin go huathoibríoch nuair a "
"bhíonn rochtain ar na socruithe mura bhfuil sé cumraithe cheana féin)."

msgid "So, if there is a module containing some code as follows::"
msgstr "Mar sin, má tá modúl ann ina bhfuil cód éigin mar seo a leanas::"

msgid ""
"...then importing this module will cause the settings object to be "
"configured. That means that the ability for third parties to import the "
"module at the top level is incompatible with the ability to configure the "
"settings object manually, or makes it very difficult in some circumstances."
msgstr ""
"... ansin beidh an modúl seo a allmhairiú mar thoradh ar an réad socruithe a "
"chumrú. Ciallaíonn sé sin go bhfuil an cumas do thríú páirtithe an modúl a "
"iompórtáil ag an leibhéal barr comhoiriúnach leis an gcumas an réad "
"socruithe a chumrú de láimh, nó go ndéanann sé an-deacair i gcúinsí áirithe."

msgid ""
"Instead of the above code, a level of laziness or indirection must be used, "
"such as ``django.utils.functional.LazyObject``, "
"``django.utils.functional.lazy()`` or ``lambda``."
msgstr ""
"In ionad an chód thuas, caithfear leibhéal leisce nó intreo a úsáid, mar "
"shampla ``django.utils.functional.lazyobject``, "
"`django.utils.functional.lazy () ``nó ``lambda``."

msgid "Miscellaneous"
msgstr "Ilghnéitheach"

msgid ""
"Mark all strings for internationalization; see the :doc:`i18n documentation "
"</topics/i18n/index>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Marcáil na teaghráin go léir le haghaidh idirnáisiúnaithe; féach an "
"doiciméadú: doc: `i</topics/i18n/index> 18n` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"Remove ``import`` statements that are no longer used when you change "
"code. :pypi:`flake8` will identify these imports for you. If an unused "
"import needs to remain for backwards-compatibility, mark the end of with ``# "
"NOQA`` to silence the flake8 warning."
msgstr ""
"Bain ráitis ```allmhairi`` nach n-úsáidtear a thuilleadh nuair a athraíonn "
"tú cód. :pypi: aithneoidh `flake8` na hallmhairí seo duit. Más gá allmhairiú "
"neamhúsáidte fanacht le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais, marcáil deireadh le "
"`# NOQA`` chun an rabhadh flake8 a thostú."

msgid ""
"Systematically remove all trailing whitespaces from your code as those add "
"unnecessary bytes, add visual clutter to the patches and can also "
"occasionally cause unnecessary merge conflicts. Some IDE's can be configured "
"to automatically remove them and most VCS tools can be set to highlight them "
"in diff outputs."
msgstr ""
"Bain gach spás bán rianúil ó do chód go córasach de réir mar a chuireann "
"siad sin béite neamhriachtanacha leis, cuireann siad neamhghnách amhairc "
"leis na paistí agus is féidir leo coimhlintí cumaisc gan ghá a chur faoi Is "
"féidir roinnt IDE a chumrú chun iad a bhaint go huathoibríoch agus is féidir "
"an chuid is mó d'uirlisí VCS a shocrú chun aird a tharraingt orthu in "
"aschuir diff."

msgid ""
"Please don't put your name in the code you contribute. Our policy is to keep "
"contributors' names in the ``AUTHORS`` file distributed with Django -- not "
"scattered throughout the codebase itself. Feel free to include a change to "
"the ``AUTHORS`` file in your patch if you make more than a single trivial "
"change."
msgstr ""
"Ná cuir d'ainm sa chód a chuireann tú le do thoil. Is é ár mbeartas "
"ainmneacha rannpháirtithe a choinneáil sa chomhad ``AUTHORS` a dháiltear le "
"Django - gan scaipthe ar fud an chód-bhunachar féin. Ná bíodh leisce ort "
"athrú ar an gcomhad ``AUTHORS` a chur san áireamh i do phaiste má dhéanann "
"tú níos mó ná athrú tábhachtach amháin."

msgid "JavaScript style"
msgstr "Stíl JavaScript"

msgid ""
"For details about the JavaScript code style used by Django, "
"see :doc:`javascript`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí faoin stíl cód JavaScript a úsáideann Django, féach:doc: "
"`javascript`."

msgid "How to submit a patch to Django for new and/or fixed behavior"
msgstr ""
"Conas paiste a chur isteach chuig Django le haghaidh iompar nua agus/nó "
"seasta"

msgid "How to write and run tests"
msgstr "Conas tástálacha a scríobh agus a rith"

msgid "How to run Django's unit tests"
msgstr "Conas tástálacha aonaid Django a reáchtáil"

msgid "How to work with Git and GitHub"
msgstr "Conas oibriú le Git agus GitHub"

msgid ""
"So you'd like to write some code, documentation or tests to improve Django? "
"There are several ways you can help Django's development."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin, ba mhaith leat roinnt cód, doiciméadú nó tástálacha a scríobh chun "
"Django a fheabhsú? Tá bealaí éagsúla ann is féidir leat cabhrú le forbairt "
"Django."

msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr "Ranganna teagaisc"

msgid ""
"The Django tutorial contains a whole section that walks you step-by-step "
"through the contributing code process."
msgstr ""
"Tá rannóg iomlán sa rang teagaisc Django a shiúlann tú céim ar chéim tríd an "
"bpróiseas cód rannchuidithe."

msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr "Treoracha conas"

msgid ""
"If you already have some familiarity with the processes and principles, our "
"documentation also contains useful guidance on specific topics:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá eolas agat cheana féin ar na próisis agus ar na prionsabail, tá treoir "
"úsáideach inár ndoiciméadú freisin maidir le hábhair ar leith:"

msgid "Related topics"
msgstr "Ábhar gaolmhara"

msgid "It's important to understand how we work and the conventions we adopt."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach a thuiscint conas a oibrímid agus na coinbhinsiúin a "
"ghlacaimid."

msgid ""
"We maintain a curated list of small issues suited to first-time or less "
"experienced contributors, using the \"easy pickings\" filter. These are "
"strongly recommended for those contributors looking to make a contribution."
msgstr ""
"Coinnímid liosta coimeádaithe de shaincheisteanna beaga atá oiriúnach do "
"rannpháirtithe céaduaire nó níos lú taithí, ag baint úsáide as an scagaire "
"“pictithe éasca”. Moltar iad seo go láidir do na ranníocóirí sin atá ag "
"iarraidh ranníocaíocht a dhéanamh."

msgid "Browse `easy pickings`_ tickets."
msgstr "Brabhsáil ticéid `éasca pickings`_."

msgid "JavaScript code"
msgstr "Cód JavaScript"

msgid ""
"While most of Django core is Python, the ``admin`` and ``gis`` contrib apps "
"contain JavaScript code."
msgstr ""
"Cé gur Python an chuid is mó de chroí Django, tá cód JavaScript sna "
"feidhmchláir contrib ``admin`` agus `gis``."

msgid ""
"Please follow these coding standards when writing JavaScript code for "
"inclusion in Django."
msgstr ""
"Lean na caighdeáin chódú seo le do thoil agus cód JavaScript á scríobh le "
"haghaidh áireamh i Django."

msgid "Code style"
msgstr "Stíl an chód"

msgid ""
"Please conform to the indentation style dictated in the ``.editorconfig`` "
"file. We recommend using a text editor with `EditorConfig`_ support to avoid "
"indentation and whitespace issues. Most of the JavaScript files use 4 spaces "
"for indentation, but there are some exceptions."
msgstr ""
"Comhlíonadh leis an stíl ionghabhála a ordaítear sa chomhad "
"``.editorconfig``. Molaimid eagarthóir téacs a úsáid le tacaíocht "
"`EditorConfig`_ chun saincheisteanna insint agus spás bán a sheachaint. "
"Úsáideann an chuid is mó de na comhaid JavaScript 4 spás le haghaidh "
"ionbhrú, ach tá roinnt eisceachtaí ann."

msgid ""
"When naming variables, use ``camelCase`` instead of ``underscore_case``. "
"Different JavaScript files sometimes use a different code style. Please try "
"to conform to the code style of each file."
msgstr ""
"Agus athróga á ainmniú agat, bain úsáid as ``camelcase`` in ionad "
"``underscore_case``. Uaireanta úsáideann comhaid éagsúla JavaScript stíl "
"chód difriúil. Déan iarracht cloí le stíl chód gach comhad le do thoil."

msgid ""
"Use the `ESLint`_ code linter to check your code for bugs and style errors. "
"ESLint will be run when you run the JavaScript tests. We also recommended "
"installing a ESLint plugin in your text editor."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an linter cód `eSlint `_ chun do chód a sheiceáil le haghaidh "
"fabhtanna agus earráidí stíl. Reáchtálfar eSlint nuair a reáchtáil tú na "
"tástálacha JavaScript. Molamar freisin breiseán eSlint a shuiteáil i "
"d'eagarthóir téacs."

msgid ""
"Where possible, write code that will work even if the page structure is "
"later changed with JavaScript. For instance, when binding a click handler, "
"use ``$('body').on('click', selector, func)`` instead of ``$"
"(selector).click(func)``. This makes it easier for projects to extend "
"Django's default behavior with JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Nuair is féidir, scríobh cód a oibreoidh fiú má athraítear struchtúr an "
"leathanaigh níos déanaí le JavaScript. Mar shampla, nuair a bhíonn "
"láimhseálaí cliceála á cheangal agat, bain úsáid as ``$ ('body') .on "
"('click', roghnóir, func) ``in ionad ``$ (roghnóir) .click (func)``. Fágann "
"sé seo go bhfuil sé níos éasca do thionscadail iompar réamhshocraithe Django "
"a leathnú le JavaScript."

msgid "JavaScript patches"
msgstr "Paistí JavaScript"

msgid ""
"Django's admin system leverages the jQuery framework to increase the "
"capabilities of the admin interface. In conjunction, there is an emphasis on "
"admin JavaScript performance and minimizing overall admin media file size."
msgstr ""
"Giarálann córas riaracháin Django creat jQuery chun cumais an chomhéadain "
"riaracháin a mhéadú. I gcomhar, tá béim ar fheidhmíocht riaracháin "
"JavaScript agus méid foriomlán comhad meán riaracháin a íoslaghdú."

msgid "JavaScript tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha JavaScript"

msgid ""
"Django's JavaScript tests can be run in a browser or from the command line. "
"The tests are located in a top level :source:`js_tests` directory."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir tástálacha JavaScript Django a reáchtáil i mbrabhsálaí nó ón líne "
"ordaithe. Tá na tástálacha suite in eolaire barrleibhéil: source: `js_tests`."

msgid "Writing tests"
msgstr "Tástála scríbhneo"

msgid "Django's JavaScript tests use `QUnit`_. Here is an example test module:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann tástálacha JavaScript Django `Qunit`_. Seo sampla modúl tástála:"

msgid ""
"Please consult the ``QUnit`` documentation for information on the types of "
"`assertions supported by QUnit <https://api.qunitjs.com/assert/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Féach le do thoil ar an gcáipéisíocht ``QUnit`` chun faisnéis a fháil faoi "
"na cineálacha `dearbhuithe a fhaigheann tacaíocht ó QUnit <https://"
"api.qunitjs.com/assert/>`_."

msgid "Running tests"
msgstr "Rith tástálacha"

msgid ""
"The JavaScript tests may be run from a web browser or from the command line."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na tástálacha JavaScript a reáchtáil ó bhrabhsálaí gréasáin nó ón "
"líne ordaithe."

msgid "Testing from a web browser"
msgstr "Tástáil ó bhrabhsálaí gréasáin"

msgid ""
"To run the tests from a web browser, open up :source:`js_tests/tests.html` "
"in your browser."
msgstr ""
"Chun na tástálacha a reáchtáil ó bhrabhsálaí gréasáin, oscail:source: "
"`js_tests/tests.html` i do bhrabhsálaí."

msgid ""
"To measure code coverage when running the tests, you need to view that file "
"over HTTP. To view code coverage:"
msgstr ""
"Chun clúdach cód a thomhas agus na tástálacha á reáchtáil agat, ní mór duit "
"an comhad sin a fheiceáil thar HTTP. Chun clúdach cód a fheiceáil:"

msgid ""
"Execute ``python -m http.server`` from the root directory (not from inside "
"``js_tests``)."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmigh ``python -m http.server`` ón eolaire fréimhe (ní ón taobh istigh "
"``js_tests``)."

msgid "Open http://localhost:8000/js_tests/tests.html in your web browser."
msgstr ""
"Oscail http://localhost:8000/js_tests/tests.html i do bhrabhsálaí gréasáin."

msgid "Testing from the command line"
msgstr "Tástáil ón líne ordaithe"

msgid ""
"To run the tests from the command line, you need to have `Node.js`_ "
"installed."
msgstr ""
"Chun na tástálacha a reáchtáil ón líne ordaithe, ní mór duit `Node.js `_ a "
"bheith suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"After installing ``Node.js``, install the JavaScript test dependencies by "
"running the following from the root of your Django checkout:"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis duit `Node.js ``a shuiteáil, suiteáil na spleáchais tástála "
"JavaScript tríd an méid seo a leanas a reáchtáil ó fhréamh do sheiceáil "
"Django:"

msgid "Then run the tests with:"
msgstr "Ansin reáchtáil na tástálacha le:"

msgid "Submitting contributions"
msgstr "Ranníocaí a chur isteach"

msgid ""
"We're always grateful for contributions to Django's code. Indeed, bug "
"reports with associated contributions will get fixed *far* more quickly than "
"those without a solution."
msgstr ""
"Táimid buíoch i gcónaí as ranníocaíochtaí le cód Django. Go deimhin, "
"socraítear tuairiscí fabhtanna le ranníocaíochtaí gaolmhara *i bhfad níos "
"gasta ná iad siúd gan réiteach."

msgid "Typo fixes and trivial documentation changes"
msgstr "Socruithe clóscríbe agus athruithe doiciméadaithe"

msgid ""
"If you are fixing a really trivial issue, for example changing a word in the "
"documentation, the preferred way to provide the patch is using GitHub pull "
"requests without a Trac ticket."
msgstr ""
"Má tá saincheist fíor-thábhachtach á shocrú agat, mar shampla focal a athrú "
"sa dhoiciméadú, is é an bealach is fearr chun an paiste a sholáthar ná "
"iarratais tarraingthe GitHub a úsáid gan ticéad Trac."

msgid ""
"See the :doc:`working-with-git` for more details on how to use pull requests."
msgstr ""
"Féach in:doc: `working-with-git` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí maidir le "
"conas iarratais tarraingthe a úsáid."

msgid "\"Claiming\" tickets"
msgstr "Ticéid “Éileamh”"

msgid ""
"In an open-source project with hundreds of contributors around the world, "
"it's important to manage communication efficiently so that work doesn't get "
"duplicated and contributors can be as effective as possible."
msgstr ""
"I dtionscadal foinse oscailte leis na céadta ranníocóirí ar fud an domhain, "
"tá sé tábhachtach an chumarsáid a bhainistiú go héifeachtach ionas nach "
"ndúblaítear an obair agus gur féidir le rannpháirtithe a bheith chomh "
"héifeachtach agus is féidir."

msgid ""
"Hence, our policy is for contributors to \"claim\" tickets in order to let "
"other developers know that a particular bug or feature is being worked on."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, is é ár mbeartas ná do rannpháirtithe ticéid a “éileamh” "
"d'fhonn a chur in iúl d'fhorbróirí eile go bhfuil fabht nó gné áirithe á n-"
"oibriú air."

msgid ""
"If you have identified a contribution you want to make and you're capable of "
"fixing it (as measured by your coding ability, knowledge of Django internals "
"and time availability), claim it by following these steps:"
msgstr ""
"Má aithníodh tú ranníocaíocht a theastaíonn uait a dhéanamh agus má tá tú in "
"ann é a shocrú (mar a thomhaistear de réir do chumas códaithe, eolas ar "
"inmheánacha Django agus infhaighteacht ama), éileamh é trí na céimeanna seo "
"a leanúint:"

msgid ""
"`Login using your GitHub account`_ or `create an account`_ in our ticket "
"system. If you have an account but have forgotten your password, you can "
"reset it using the `password reset page`_."
msgstr ""
"`Logáil isteach ag baint úsáide as do chuntas GitHub `_ nó `cruthaigh "
"cuntas`_ inár gcóras ticéad. Má tá cuntas agat ach má tá dearmad déanta agat "
"ar do phasfhocal, is féidir leat é a athshocrú ag baint úsáide as an "
"`leathanach athshocraithe pasfhocal`_."

msgid ""
"If a ticket for this issue doesn't exist yet, create one in our `ticket "
"tracker`_. Remember that proposals for new features should follow "
"the :ref:`process for suggesting new features <requesting-features>`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a ticket for this issue already exists, make sure nobody else has claimed "
"it. To do this, look at the \"Owned by\" section of the ticket. If it's "
"assigned to \"nobody,\" then it's available to be claimed. Otherwise, "
"somebody else may be working on this ticket. Either find another bug/feature "
"to work on, or contact the developer working on the ticket to offer your "
"help. If a ticket has been assigned for weeks or months without any "
"activity, it's probably safe to reassign it to yourself."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ticéad don tsaincheist seo ann cheana féin, déan cinnte nach éiligh "
"aon duine eile é. Chun seo a dhéanamh, féach ar an gcuid “Úinéireacht ag” "
"den ticéad. Má shanntar é do “duine ar bith,” ansin tá sé ar fáil le "
"héileamh. Seachas sin, d'fhéadfadh duine eile a bheith ag obair ar an ticéad "
"seo. Faigh bot/gné eile le bheith ag obair air, nó déan teagmháil leis an "
"bhforbróir atá ag obair ar an ticéad chun do chabhair a thairiscint. Má "
"shannadh ticéad ar feadh seachtainí nó míonna gan aon ghníomhaíocht, is "
"dócha go bhfuil sé sábháilte é a athshannadh duit féin."

msgid ""
"Log into your account, if you haven't already, by clicking \"GitHub Login\" "
"or \"DjangoProject Login\" in the upper left of the ticket page. Once logged "
"in, you can then click the \"Modify Ticket\" button near the bottom of the "
"page."
msgstr ""
"Logáil isteach i do chuntas, mura bhfuil tú cheana féin, trí chliceáil "
"“Logáil Isteach GitHub” nó “Logáil Isteach DjangoProject” ar an taobh clé "
"uachtarach den leathanach ticéad. Nuair a bheidh tú logáilte isteach, is "
"féidir leat an cnaipe “Athraigh Ticéad” a chliceáil in aice le bun an "
"leathanaigh."

msgid ""
"Claim the ticket by clicking the \"assign to\" radio button in the "
"\"Action\" section. Your username will be filled in the text box by default."
msgstr ""
"Éileamh an ticéad trí chliceáil ar an gcnaipe raidió “sannadh chuig” sa "
"chuid “Gníomhaíocht”. Líonfar d'ainm úsáideora sa bhosca téacs de réir "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid "Finally click the \"Submit changes\" button at the bottom to save."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh cliceáil ar an gcnaipe “Cuir isteach athruithe” ag an mbun "
"chun sábháil."

msgid ""
"The Django software foundation requests that anyone contributing more than "
"a :ref:`trivial change <trivial-change>`, to Django sign and submit a "
"`Contributor License Agreement`_, this ensures that the Django Software "
"Foundation has clear license to all contributions allowing for a clear "
"license for all users."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ticket claimers' responsibility"
msgstr "Freagracht éilimh ticéad"

msgid ""
"Once you've claimed a ticket, you have a responsibility to work on that "
"ticket in a reasonably timely fashion. If you don't have time to work on it, "
"either unclaim it or don't claim it in the first place!"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh ticéad éileamh agat, tá freagracht agat oibriú ar an ticéad "
"sin ar bhealach réasúnta tráthúil. Mura bhfuil am agat oibriú air, déan é a "
"éileamh nó ná éileamh é ar an gcéad dul síos!"

msgid ""
"If there's no sign of progress on a particular claimed ticket for a week or "
"two, another developer may ask you to relinquish the ticket claim so that "
"it's no longer monopolized and somebody else can claim it."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil aon chomhartha dul chun cinn ar thicéad éilimh áirithe ar feadh "
"seachtaine nó dhó, féadfaidh forbróir eile iarraidh ort an t-éileamh ticéad "
"a fhágáil ionas nach mbeidh sé monaplaithe a thuilleadh agus gur féidir le "
"duine eile é a éileamh."

msgid ""
"If you've claimed a ticket and it's taking a long time (days or weeks) to "
"code, keep everybody updated by posting comments on the ticket. If you don't "
"provide regular updates, and you don't respond to a request for a progress "
"report, your claim on the ticket may be revoked."
msgstr ""
"Má éiligh tú ticéad agus má thógann sé tamall fada (laethanta nó seachtainí) "
"chun cóid a dhéanamh, coinnigh gach duine ar an dáta trí thuairimí a "
"phostáil ar an ticéad. Mura gcuireann tú nuashonruithe rialta ar fáil, agus "
"mura bhfreagraíonn tú iarratas ar thuarascáil ar dhul chun cinn, féadfar "
"d'éileamh ar an ticéad a chúlghairm."

msgid "As always, more communication is better than less communication!"
msgstr "Mar is gnách, is fearr níos mó cumarsáide ná níos lú cumarsáide!"

msgid "Which tickets should be claimed?"
msgstr "Cé na ticéid ba chóir a éileamh?"

msgid "Going through the steps of claiming tickets is overkill in some cases."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé ró-mhór dul trí na céimeanna chun ticéid a éileamh i gcásanna áirithe."

msgid ""
"In the case of small changes, such as typos in the documentation or small "
"bugs that will only take a few minutes to fix, you don't need to jump "
"through the hoops of claiming tickets. Submit your changes directly and "
"you're done!"
msgstr ""
"I gcás athruithe beaga, mar shampla clóscríobh sa dhoiciméadú nó fabhtanna "
"beaga nach dtógfaidh ach cúpla nóiméad iad a shocrú, ní gá duit léim trí "
"chrupaí ticéid a éileamh. Cuir isteach d'athruithe go díreach agus tá tú "
"déanta!"

msgid ""
"It is *always* acceptable, regardless whether someone has claimed it or not, "
"to link proposals to a ticket if you happen to have the changes ready."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé inghlactha i gcónaí*, is cuma má éiligh duine é nó nach bhfuil, tograí "
"a nascadh le ticéad má tharlaíonn go bhfuil na hathruithe réidh agat."

msgid "Contribution style"
msgstr "Stíl ranníocaíochta"

msgid ""
"Make sure that any contribution you do fulfills at least the following "
"requirements:"
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go gcomhlíonann aon ranníocaíocht atá agat na ceanglais seo a "
"leanas ar a laghad:"

msgid ""
"The code required to fix a problem or add a feature is an essential part of "
"a solution, but it is not the only part. A good fix should also include "
"a :doc:`regression test <unit-tests>` to validate the behavior that has been "
"fixed and to prevent the problem from arising again. Also, if some tickets "
"are relevant to the code that you've written, mention the ticket numbers in "
"some comments in the test so that one can easily trace back the relevant "
"discussions after your patch gets committed, and the tickets get closed."
msgstr ""
"Is cuid riachtanach de réiteach é an cód a theastaíonn chun fadhb a shocrú "
"nó gné a chur leis, ach ní hé an t-aon chuid é. Ba cheart go n-áireofaí a: "
"doc: `tástá <unit-tests>il aischéimniúna` i socrú maith chun an t-iompar atá "
"socraithe a bhailíochtú agus chun an fhadhb a chosc ó eascraíonn arís. Chomh "
"maith leis sin, má tá roinnt ticéid ábhartha don chód a scríobh tú, luaigh "
"na huimhreacha ticéad i roinnt tuairimí sa tástáil ionas gur féidir le duine "
"na díospóireachtaí ábhartha a rianú siar go héasca tar éis do phaiste "
"tiomanta, agus na ticéid a dhúnadh."

msgid ""
"If the code adds a new feature, or modifies the behavior of an existing "
"feature, the change should also contain documentation."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann an cód gné nua leis, nó má athraíonn sé iompar gné atá ann "
"cheana, ba cheart go mbeadh cáipéisíocht san athrú freisin."

msgid ""
"When you think your work is ready to be reviewed, send :doc:`a GitHub pull "
"request <working-with-git>`. If you can't send a pull request for some "
"reason, you can also use patches in Trac. When using this style, follow "
"these guidelines."
msgstr ""
"<working-with-git>Nuair a cheapann tú go bhfuil do chuid oibre réidh le "
"hathbhreithniú, seol: doc: `iarratas tarraingthe GitHub `. Mura féidir leat "
"iarratas tarraingthe a sheoladh ar chúis éigin, is féidir leat paistí a "
"úsáid i Trac freisin. Agus an stíl seo á úsáid agat, lean na treoirlínte seo."

msgid "Submit patches in the format returned by the ``git diff`` command."
msgstr ""
"Cuir isteach paistí san fhormáid a thugtar ar ais leis an ordú ``git diff``."

msgid ""
"Attach patches to a ticket in the `ticket tracker`_, using the \"attach "
"file\" button. Please *don't* put the patch in the ticket description or "
"comment unless it's a single line patch."
msgstr ""
"Ceangail paistí le ticéad sa `rianaitheoir ticéad`_, ag baint úsáide as an "
"gcnaipe “comhad ceangail”. * Ná cuir an paiste sa tuairisc nó trácht ar an "
"ticéad mura bhfuil paiste líne amháin ann."

msgid ""
"Name the patch file with a ``.diff`` extension; this will let the ticket "
"tracker apply correct syntax highlighting, which is quite helpful."
msgstr ""
"Ainmnigh an comhad paiste le síneadh `.diff``; ligfidh sé seo don "
"rianaitheoir ticéad aibhsiú comhréireachta ceart a chur i bhfeidhm, rud atá "
"cabhrach go leor."

msgid "Regardless of the way you submit your work, follow these steps."
msgstr ""
"Beag beann ar an mbealach a chuireann tú do chuid oibre isteach, lean na "
"céimeanna seo."

msgid ""
"Make sure your code fulfills the requirements in our :ref:`contribution "
"checklist <patch-review-checklist>`."
msgstr ""
"<patch-review-checklist>Déan cinnte go gcomhlíonann do chód na riachtanais "
"inár: ref: `seicliosta ranníocaíochta `."

msgid ""
"Check the \"Has patch\" box on the ticket and make sure the \"Needs "
"documentation\", \"Needs tests\", and \"Patch needs improvement\" boxes "
"aren't checked. This makes the ticket appear in the \"Patches needing "
"review\" queue on the `Development dashboard`_."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil an bosca “Tá paiste” ar an ticéad agus déan cinnte nach ndéantar na "
"boscaí “Doiciméadú riachtanais”, “Tástálacha riachtanais”, agus “Feabhsú "
"riachtanais” a sheiceáil. Fágann sé sin go bhfuil an ticéad le feiceáil sa "
"scuaine “Paistí a theastaíonn athbhreithniú” ar an “dashboard Forbartha” _."

msgid "Contributions which require community feedback"
msgstr "Ranníocaí a dteastaíonn aiseolas"

msgid ""
"A wider community discussion is required when a patch introduces new Django "
"functionality and makes some sort of design decision. This is especially "
"important if the approach involves a :ref:`deprecation <deprecating-a-"
"feature>` or introduces breaking changes."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn plé pobail níos leithne nuair a thugann paiste feidhmiúlacht nua "
"Django isteach agus déanann sé cinneadh dearaidh de chineál éigin. Tá sé seo "
"tábhachtach go háirithe má bhaineann leis an gcur chuige a: ref: "
"`diprecation <deprecating-a-feature>`nó má thugann sé athruithe briseadh "
"isteach."

msgid ""
"The following are different approaches for gaining feedback from the "
"community."
msgstr "Seo a leanas cur chuige éagsúla chun aiseolas a fháil ón bpobal."

msgid "The new feature ideas tracker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have an idea for a new feature, please create a new proposal (or join "
"an existing discussion) following the :ref:`process for suggesting new "
"features <requesting-features>`. You should explain the need for the change, "
"go into details of the approach and discuss alternatives."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Django Forum"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can propose a change (that is not a new feature idea) on the `Django "
"Forum`_. You should explain the need for the change, go into details of the "
"approach and discuss alternatives."
msgstr ""

msgid "Please include a link to such discussions in your contributions."
msgstr "Cuir nasc chuig díospóireachtaí den sórt sin i do chuid tuairimí."

msgid "Third party package"
msgstr "Pacáiste tríú páirtí"

msgid ""
"Django does not accept experimental features. All features must follow "
"our :ref:`deprecation policy <internal-release-deprecation-policy>`. Hence, "
"it can take months or years for Django to iterate on an API design."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann Django le gnéithe turgnamhacha. <internal-release-deprecation-"
"policy>Caithfidh gach gné ár n:ref: `beartas díréachtaithe `a leanúint. Dá "
"bhrí sin, féadfaidh sé míonna nó blianta a thógáil ar Django athrú ar "
"dhearadh API."

msgid ""
"If you need user feedback on a public interface, it is better to create a "
"third-party package first. You can iterate on the public API much faster, "
"while also validating the need for the feature."
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn aiseolas úsáideora uait ar chomhéadan poiblí, is fearr "
"pacáiste tríú páirtí a chruthú ar dtús. Is féidir leat athrá a dhéanamh ar "
"an API poiblí i bhfad níos gasta, agus an gá atá leis an ngné a bhailíochtú "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"Once this package becomes stable and there are clear benefits of "
"incorporating aspects into Django core, the next step is to propose its "
"inclusion by following the :ref:`process for suggesting new features "
"<requesting-features>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Django Enhancement Proposal (DEP)"
msgstr "Togra Feabhsúcháin Django (DEP)"

msgid ""
"Similar to Python’s PEPs, Django has `Django Enhancement Proposals`_ or "
"DEPs. A DEP is a design document which provides information to the Django "
"community, or describes a new feature or process for Django. They provide "
"concise technical specifications of features, along with rationales. DEPs "
"are also the primary mechanism for proposing and collecting community input "
"on major new features."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le PEPanna Python, tá `Tograí Feabhsaithe Django `_ nó DEPanna ag "
"Django. Is doiciméad dearaidh é DEP a sholáthraíonn faisnéis do phobal "
"Django, nó a dhéanann cur síos ar ghné nó próiseas nua do Django. "
"Soláthraíonn siad sonraíochtaí teicniúla gonta de ghnéithe, mar aon le "
"réasúnaí. Is iad DEPanna an príomh-mheicníocht freisin chun ionchur pobail a "
"mholadh agus a bhailiú ar phríomhghnéithe nua."

msgid ""
"Before considering writing a DEP, it is recommended to first open a "
"discussion following the :ref:`process for suggesting new features "
"<requesting-features>`. This allows the community to provide feedback and "
"helps refine the proposal. Once the DEP is ready the :ref:`Steering Council "
"<steering-council>` votes on whether to accept it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Some examples of DEPs that have been approved and fully implemented:"
msgstr ""
"Roinnt samplaí de DEPanna atá ceadaithe agus curtha i bhfeidhm go hiomlán:"

msgid ""
"`DEP 181: ORM Expressions <https://github.com/django/deps/blob/main/final/"
"0181-orm-expressions.rst>`_"
msgstr ""
"< https://github.com/django/deps/blob/main/final/0181-orm-"
"expressions.rst>`DEP 181: Expressions ORM `_"

msgid ""
"`DEP 182: Multiple Template Engines <https://github.com/django/deps/blob/"
"main/final/0182-multiple-template-engines.rst>`_"
msgstr ""
"< https://github.com/django/deps/blob/main/final/0182-multiple-template-"
"engines.rst>`DEP 182: Innill Teimpléad Iolracha `_"

msgid ""
"`DEP 201: Simplified routing syntax <https://github.com/django/deps/blob/"
"main/final/0201-simplified-routing-syntax.rst>`_"
msgstr ""
"< https://github.com/django/deps/blob/main/final/0201-simplified-routing-"
"syntax.rst>`DEP 201: Syntax ródú simplithe `_"

msgid "Deprecating a feature"
msgstr "Gné a dhíspreagadh"

msgid "There are a couple of reasons that code in Django might be deprecated:"
msgstr "Tá cúpla cúis ann go bhféadfadh cód i Django a dhíchur:"

msgid ""
"If a feature has been improved or modified in a backwards-incompatible way, "
"the old feature or behavior will be deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Má tá gné feabhsaithe nó modhnaithe ar bhealach atá neamhchomhoiriúnach le "
"cúlra, déanfar an sean-ghné nó an t-iompar a dhíchur."

msgid ""
"Sometimes Django will include a backport of a Python library that's not "
"included in a version of Python that Django currently supports. When Django "
"no longer needs to support the older version of Python that doesn't include "
"the library, the library will be deprecated in Django."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta cuimsíonn Django backport de leabharlann Python nach bhfuil san "
"áireamh i leagan de Python a thacaíonn Django faoi láthair. Nuair nach gá "
"Django tacú leis an leagan níos sine de Python nach n-áirítear an "
"leabharlann a thuilleadh, déanfar an leabharlann a dhíchur i Django."

msgid ""
"As the :ref:`deprecation policy<internal-release-deprecation-policy>` "
"describes, the first release of Django that deprecates a feature (``A.B``) "
"should raise a ``RemovedInDjangoXXWarning`` (where XX is the Django version "
"where the feature will be removed) when the deprecated feature is invoked. "
"Assuming we have good test coverage, these warnings are converted to errors "
"when :ref:`running the test suite <running-unit-tests>` with warnings "
"enabled: ``python -Wa runtests.py``. Thus, when adding a "
"``RemovedInDjangoXXWarning`` you need to eliminate or silence any warnings "
"generated when running the tests."
msgstr ""
"Mar a thuairiscíonn an:ref: `beartas díscoireach <internal-release-"
"deprecation-policy>`, ba cheart don chéad scaoileadh de Django a "
"dhíspreagann gné (`A.B``) ``removedindjangoxxWarning`` a ardú (áit gurb é XX "
"an leagan Django ina mbainfear an ghné) nuair a ghairmtear an ghné díscoite. "
"Ag glacadh leis go bhfuil clúdach maith tástála againn, déantar na rabhaidh "
"seo a thiontú go earráidí nuair: ref: `reáchtáil an tsraith tástála <running-"
"unit-tests>`le rabhaidh cumasaithe: ``python -Wa runtests.py``. Dá bhrí sin, "
"nuair a chuireann tú ``removedindjangoxxWarning``, ní mór duit deireadh a "
"chur le haon rabhaidh a ghintear agus na tástálacha á reáchtáil agat."

msgid ""
"The first step is to remove any use of the deprecated behavior by Django "
"itself. Next you can silence warnings in tests that actually test the "
"deprecated behavior by using the ``ignore_warnings`` decorator, either at "
"the test or class level:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad chéim ná aon úsáid a bhaint as an iompar dlús ag Django féin. "
"Ansin is féidir leat rabhaidh a thostú i dtástálacha a thástáil i ndáiríre "
"an t-iompar míchuir tríd an maisitheoir `ignore_warnings ``a úsáid, ag an "
"leibhéal tástála nó ag an rang:"

msgid "In a particular test::"
msgstr "I dtástáil áirithe:"

msgid "For an entire test case::"
msgstr "Maidir le cás tástála iomlán:"

msgid "You should also add a test for the deprecation warning::"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit tástáil a chur leis freisin maidir leis an rabhadh "
"díscrúdaithe:"

msgid ""
"It's important to include a ``RemovedInDjangoXXWarning`` comment above code "
"which has no warning reference, but will need to be changed or removed when "
"the deprecation ends. This could include hooks which have been added to keep "
"the previous behavior, or standalone items that are unnecessary or unused "
"when the deprecation ends. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach trácht ``RemovedindjangoXXWarning` a chur san áireamh "
"thuas an chód nach bhfuil aon tagairt rabhaidh aige, ach go gcaithfear é a "
"athrú nó a bhaint nuair a chríochnaíonn an díghabháil. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a "
"bheith san áireamh crúcaí a cuireadh leis chun an t-iompar roimhe seo a "
"choinneáil, nó míreanna neamhspleácha nach bhfuil gan ghá nó neamhúsáidte "
"nuair a chríochnaíonn Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Finally, there are a couple of updates to Django's documentation to make:"
msgstr "Faoi dheireadh, tá cúpla nuashonrú ar dhoiciméadú Django le déanamh:"

msgid ""
"If the existing feature is documented, mark it deprecated in documentation "
"using the ``.. deprecated:: A.B`` annotation. Include a short description "
"and a note about the upgrade path if applicable."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéantar an ghné atá ann cheana doiciméadaithe, déan é a mharcáil go "
"díluasaithe i ndoiciméadú ag baint úsáide as an anótáil ``.. diúscartha:: "
"A.B``. Cuir tuairisc ghearr agus nóta faoin gcosán uasghrádaithe más "
"infheidhme."

msgid ""
"Add a description of the deprecated behavior, and the upgrade path if "
"applicable, to the current release notes (``docs/releases/A.B.txt``) under "
"the \"Features deprecated in A.B\" heading."
msgstr ""
"Cuir cur síos ar an iompar míchuir, agus an cosán uasghrádaithe más "
"infheidhme, leis na nótaí scaoileadh reatha (`Docs/releases/A.B.txt``) faoin "
"gceannteideal “Gnéithe a dhíchur in AB”."

msgid ""
"Add an entry in the deprecation timeline (``docs/internals/"
"deprecation.txt``) under the appropriate version describing what code will "
"be removed."
msgstr ""
"Cuir iontráil san amlíne díscrúdaithe (``docs/internals/deprecation.txt``) "
"faoin leagan cuí ag cur síos ar an gcód a bhainfear."

msgid ""
"Once you have completed these steps, you are finished with the deprecation. "
"In each :term:`feature release <Feature release>`, all "
"``RemovedInDjangoXXWarning``\\s matching the new version are removed."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh na céimeanna seo críochnaithe agat, tá tú críochnaithe leis "
"an díghabháil. I ngach:term: `gné scaoileadh `<Feature release>, baintear "
"gach ``RemovedindJangOxxWarning`` a mheaitseálann leis an leagan nua."

msgid "Testing with a Django project"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It's important to test local changes using a Django project. This allows "
"ensuring that the changes behave as expected in a real environment, "
"especially for user-facing features such as templates, forms, or the admin."
msgstr ""

msgid "To do this:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create a virtual environment and :ref:`install the cloned copy of Django in "
"editable mode <intro-contributing-install-local-copy>`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set up a Django project outside the source tree (you can use the :doc:`first "
"part of the tutorial </intro/tutorial01>` for guidance)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this setup, any changes made to the Django checkout will take effect "
"immediately in the test project, allowing manual testing of contributions "
"against a new or existing app."
msgstr ""

msgid "JavaScript contributions"
msgstr "Ranníocaíochtaí JavaScript"

msgid ""
"For information on JavaScript contributions, see the :ref:`javascript-"
"patches` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh faisnéise maidir le ranníocaíochtaí JavaScript, féach an "
"doiciméadach:ref: `javascript-patches`."

msgid "Optimization patches"
msgstr "Paistí optamaithe"

msgid ""
"Patches aiming to deliver a performance improvement should provide "
"benchmarks showing the before and after impact of the patch and sharing the "
"commands for reviewers to reproduce."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go soláthródh paistí a bhfuil sé mar aidhm acu feabhas "
"feidhmíochta a sheachadadh tagarmharcanna a thaispeánann iarmhairt an "
"phaiste agus ina dhiaidh sin agus na horduithe a roinnt le hathbhreithneoirí "
"a atáirgeadh."

msgid "``django-asv`` benchmarks"
msgstr "Tagarmharcanna ``django-asv``"

msgid ""
"`django-asv`_ monitors the performance of Django code over time. These "
"benchmarks can be run on a pull request by labeling the pull request with "
"``benchmark``. Adding to these benchmarks is highly encouraged."
msgstr ""
"Monatóireacht `django-asv`_ ar fheidhmíocht cód Django le himeacht ama. Is "
"féidir na tagarmharcanna seo a reáchtáil ar iarratas tarraingthe tríd an "
"iarraidh tarraingthe a lipéadú le “tagarmharc”. Spreagtar go mór leis na "
"tagarmharcanna seo a chur leis."

msgid "Contribution checklist"
msgstr "Seicliosta ranníocaíochta"

msgid ""
"Use this checklist to review a pull request. If this contribution would not "
"be :ref:`considered trivial <trivial-change>`, first ensure it has an "
"accepted ticket before proceeding with the review."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the pull request passes all the criteria below and is not your own, "
"please set the \"Triage Stage\" on the corresponding Trac ticket to \"Ready "
"for checkin\". If you've left comments for improvement on the pull request, "
"please tick the appropriate flags on the Trac ticket based on the results of "
"your review: \"Patch needs improvement\", \"Needs documentation\", and/or "
"\"Needs tests\". As time and interest permits, mergers do final reviews of "
"\"Ready for checkin\" tickets and will either commit the changes or bump it "
"back to \"Accepted\" if further work needs to be done."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you're looking to become a member of the `triage & review team <https://"
"www.djangoproject.com/foundation/teams/#triage-review-team>`_, doing "
"thorough reviews of contributions is a great way to earn trust."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Looking for a patch to review? Check out the \"Patches needing review\" "
"section of the `Django Development Dashboard <https://"
"dashboard.djangoproject.com/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Ag lorg paiste le hathbhreithniú? Amharc ar an rannán \"Paistí a dteastaíonn "
"athbhreithniú uathu\" den Phainéal Forbartha Django <https://"
"dashboard.djangoproject.com/>`_."

msgid ""
"Looking to get your pull request reviewed? Ensure the Trac flags on the "
"ticket are set so that the ticket appears in that queue."
msgstr ""
"Ag iarraidh d'iarratas tarraingthe a athbhreithniú Déan cinnte go bhfuil "
"bratacha Trac ar an ticéad socraithe ionas go mbeidh an ticéad le feiceáil "
"sa scuaine sin."

msgid ""
"Does the documentation build without any errors (``make html``, or "
"``make.bat html`` on Windows, from the ``docs`` directory)?"
msgstr ""
"An dtógann an doiciméadú gan aon earráidí (``make html``, nó ``make.bat "
"html`` ar Windows, ón eolaire ``docs`)?"

msgid ""
"Does the documentation follow the writing style guidelines in :doc:`/"
"internals/contributing/writing-documentation`?"
msgstr ""
"An leanann an doiciméadú na treoirlínte stíl scríbhneoireachta in:doc: `/"
"inmheán/ranníoc/scríbhneoireach-doiciméadúcháin `?"

msgid "Are there any :ref:`spelling errors <documentation-spelling-check>`?"
msgstr ""
"<documentation-spelling-check>An bhfuil aon earráidí litrithe ann: ref: "
"`earráidí litrithe `?"

msgid "Bugs"
msgstr "Fabhtanna"

msgid ""
"Is there a proper regression test (the test should fail before the fix is "
"applied)?"
msgstr ""
"An bhfuil tástáil cheart aischéimnithí ann (ba cheart go dteipfeadh ar an "
"tástáil sula gcuirtear an deisiú i bhfeidhm)?"

msgid ""
"If it's a bug that :ref:`qualifies for a backport <supported-versions-"
"policy>` to the stable version of Django, is there a release note in ``docs/"
"releases/A.B.C.txt``? Bug fixes that will be applied only to the main branch "
"don't need a release note."
msgstr ""
"Más fabht é a cháilíonn :ref:` le haghaidh cúlport <supported-versions-"
"policy>` chuig an leagan cobhsaí de Django, an bhfuil nóta eisiúna in ``docs/"
"releases/A.B.C.txt``? Ní gá nóta scaoilte a bheith ag ceartúcháin fabhtanna "
"a chuirfear i bhfeidhm sa phríomhbhrainse amháin."

msgid "New Features"
msgstr "Gnéithe Nua"

msgid "Are there tests to \"exercise\" all of the new code?"
msgstr "An bhfuil tástálacha ann chun an cód nua go léir a “feidhmiú”?"

msgid "Is there a release note in ``docs/releases/A.B.txt``?"
msgstr "An bhfuil nóta scaoileadh i `Docs/releases/a.b.txt``?"

msgid ""
"Is there documentation for the feature and is it :ref:`annotated "
"appropriately <documenting-new-features>` with ``.. versionadded:: A.B`` or "
"``.. versionchanged:: A.B``?"
msgstr ""
"An bhfuil cáipéisíocht ann don ghné agus an bhfuil sé: ref: `anótáilte go "
"cuí `le` <documenting-new-features>`.. leaganadded:: A.B`` nó ``.. "
"leaganmodified:: A.B``?"

msgid "See the :ref:`deprecating-a-feature` guide."
msgstr "Féach an treor:ref: `deprecating-a-feature`."

msgid "All code changes"
msgstr "Athraíonn gach cód"

msgid ""
"Does the :doc:`coding style </internals/contributing/writing-code/coding-"
"style>` conform to our guidelines? Are there any  ``black``, ``blacken-"
"docs``, ``flake8``, or ``isort`` errors? You can install the :ref:`pre-"
"commit <coding-style-pre-commit>` hooks to automatically catch these errors."
msgstr ""
"An gcomhlíonann an:doc: `stíl chódú `lenár dtreoirlín</internals/"
"contributing/writing-code/coding-style> te? An bhfuil aon earráidí "
"``black``, `blacken-docs``, `flake8``, nó `isort``? Is féidir leat crúcaí: "
"ref: `pre-commit <coding-style-pre-commit>`a shuiteáil chun na hearráidí seo "
"a ghabháil go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"If the change is backwards incompatible in any way, is there a note in the "
"release notes (``docs/releases/A.B.txt``)?"
msgstr ""
"Má tá an t-athrú ag teacht ar ais ar bhealach ar bith, an bhfuil nóta sna "
"nótaí scaoilte (`Docs/releases/a.b.txt``)?"

msgid "Is Django's test suite passing?"
msgstr "An bhfuil sraith tástála Django ag rith?"

msgid ""
"If the change affects the Django admin or rendered HTML output, "
"has :ref:`accessibility testing <accessibility-testing-baseline>` been done?"
msgstr ""

msgid "All tickets"
msgstr "Gach ticéad"

msgid ""
"Is the pull request a single squashed commit with a message that follows "
"our :ref:`commit message format <committing-guidelines>`?"
msgstr ""
"<committing-guidelines>An bhfuil an t-iarratas tarraingthe ná tiomantas "
"aonair le teachtaireacht a leanann inn:ref: `formáid teachtaireachta "
"comhartha `?"

msgid ""
"Are you the patch author and a new contributor? Please add yourself to "
"the :source:`AUTHORS` file and submit a `Contributor License Agreement`_."
msgstr ""
"An tusa an t-údar paiste agus ranníocóir nua? Cuir tú féin leis an "
"gcomhad:source: `AUTHORS` le do thoil agus cuir isteach `Comhaontú Ceadúnais "
"Ranníoca`_."

msgid ""
"Does this have an accepted ticket on Trac? All contributions require a "
"ticket unless the :ref:`change is considered trivial <trivial-change>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Unit tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha aonaid"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a test suite of its own, in the ``tests`` directory of the "
"code base. It's our policy to make sure all tests pass at all times."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le sraith tástála féin, in eolaire ``tástálacha ``den bhonn "
"cód. Is é ár mbeartas a chinntiú go dtéann gach tástáil i gcónaí."

msgid "We appreciate any and all contributions to the test suite!"
msgstr "Táimid buíoch as aon ranníocaíochtaí go léir leis an tsraith tástála!"

msgid ""
"The Django tests all use the testing infrastructure that ships with Django "
"for testing applications. See :doc:`/topics/testing/overview` for an "
"explanation of how to write new tests."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann tástálacha Django go léir an bonneagar tástála a sheolann le "
"Django chun feidhmchláir a thástáil Féach:doc: `/topics/tástáil/léirmheas` "
"le haghaidh míniú ar conas tástálacha nua a scríobh."

msgid "Running the unit tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha aonaid a rith"

msgid "Quickstart"
msgstr "Tosaigh gasta"

msgid ""
"First, `fork Django on GitHub <https://github.com/django/django/fork>`__."
msgstr ""
"< https://github.com/django/django/fork>Ar dtús, `fork Django ar Github`__."

msgid ""
"Second, create and activate a virtual environment. If you're not familiar "
"with how to do that, read our :doc:`contributing tutorial </intro/"
"contributing>`."
msgstr ""
"Ar an dara dul síos, cruthaigh agus gníomhachtaigh timpeallacht f Mura "
"bhfuil tú eolach ar conas é sin a dhéanamh, léigh inn:doc: `teagaisc "
"rannchuidiúcháin` </intro/contributing>."

msgid "Next, clone your fork, install some requirements, and run the tests:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, clóin do fhorc, suiteáil roinnt riachtanais, agus reáchtáil na "
"tástálacha:"

msgid ""
"Installing the requirements will likely require some operating system "
"packages that your computer doesn't have installed. You can usually figure "
"out which package to install by doing a web search for the last line or so "
"of the error message. Try adding your operating system to the search query "
"if needed."
msgstr ""
"Is dócha go mbeidh gá le roinnt pacáistí córais oibriúcháin nach bhfuil "
"suiteáilte ar do ríomhaire chun na ceanglais a shuiteáil. Is féidir leat a "
"dhéanamh amach de ghnáth cén pacáiste atá le suiteáil trí chuardach gréasáin "
"a dhéanamh don líne dheireanach nó mar sin den teachtaireacht earráide. Bain "
"triail as do chóras oibriúcháin a chur leis an bhfiosrúchán cuardaigh más gá."

msgid ""
"If you have trouble installing the requirements, you can skip that step. "
"See :ref:`running-unit-tests-dependencies` for details on installing the "
"optional test dependencies. If you don't have an optional dependency "
"installed, the tests that require it will be skipped."
msgstr ""
"Má tá deacracht agat na riachtanais a shuiteáil, is féidir leat an chéim sin "
"a scipeáil. Féach: Ref: `running-unit-tests-dependencies` le haghaidh sonraí "
"maidir leis na spleáchais tástála roghnacha a shuiteáil. Mura bhfuil "
"spleáchas roghnach suiteáilte agat, scipeánfar na tástálacha a éilíonn é."

msgid ""
"Running the tests requires a Django settings module that defines the "
"databases to use. To help you get started, Django provides and uses a sample "
"settings module that uses the SQLite database. See :ref:`running-unit-tests-"
"settings` to learn how to use a different settings module to run the tests "
"with a different database."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn modúl socruithe Django a shainmhíníonn na bunachair sonraí atá le "
"húsáid. Chun cabhrú leat tosú, soláthraíonn agus úsáideann Django modúl "
"socruithe samplach a úsáideann bunachar sonraí SQLite. Féach:ref: `running-"
"unit-tests-settings` chun foghlaim conas modúl socruithe difriúil a úsáid "
"chun na tástálacha a reáchtáil le bunachar sonraí difriúil."

msgid ""
"Having problems? See :ref:`troubleshooting-unit-tests` for some common "
"issues."
msgstr ""
"Ag fadhbanna agat? Féach:ref: `trouoting-unitt-tests` le haghaidh roinnt "
"saincheisteanna coitianta."

msgid "Running tests using ``tox``"
msgstr "Tástálacha reatha ag baint úsáide as ``tocs``"

msgid ""
"`Tox <https://tox.wiki/>`_ is a tool for running tests in different virtual "
"environments. Django includes a basic ``tox.ini`` that automates some checks "
"that our build server performs on pull requests. To run the unit tests and "
"other checks (such as :ref:`import sorting <coding-style-imports>`, "
"the :ref:`documentation spelling checker <documentation-spelling-check>`, "
"and :ref:`code formatting <coding-style-python>`), install and run the "
"``tox`` command from any place in the Django source tree:"
msgstr ""
"Is uirlis é `Tox`_ chun tá< https://tox.wiki/> stálacha a reáchtáil i "
"dtimpeallachtaí fíorúla difriúla Cuimsíonn Django bunúsach ``tox.ini`` a "
"uathoibriú roinnt seiceálacha a dhéanann ár bhfreastalaí tógála ar iarratais "
"tarraingthe. <coding-style-imports>Chun na tástálacha aonaid agus na "
"seiceálacha eile a reáchtáil (mar shampla:ref: `sórtáil allmhairiúcháin `, "
"an:ref: `seiceálaí litrithe doiciméadaithe', agus <documentation-spelling-"
"check>:ref: `formáidiú cód`<coding-style-python>), suiteáil agus reáchtáil "
"an t-ordú `tox`` ó aon áit sa chrann foinse Django:"

msgid ""
"By default, ``tox`` runs the test suite with the bundled test settings file "
"for SQLite, ``black``, ``blacken-docs``, ``flake8``, ``isort``, and the "
"documentation spelling checker. In addition to the system dependencies noted "
"elsewhere in this documentation, the command ``python3`` must be on your "
"path and linked to the appropriate version of Python. A list of default "
"environments can be seen as follows:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ritheann ``tox`` an tsraith tástála leis an gcomhad "
"socruithe tástála cuachta le haghaidh SQLite, ``black``, `blacken-docs``, "
"``flake8``, `isort``, agus an seiceálaí litrithe doiciméadaithe. Chomh maith "
"leis na spleáchais chórais a thugtar faoi deara in áiteanna eile sa "
"doiciméadú seo, caithfidh an t-ordú `python3` a bheith ar do chonair agus "
"nasctha leis an leagan cuí de Python. Is féidir liosta de thimpeallachtaí "
"réamhshocraithe a fheiceáil mar seo a leanas:"

msgid "Testing other Python versions and database backends"
msgstr "Leaganacha Python eile agus cúltaca bunachar sonraí a thástáil"

msgid ""
"In addition to the default environments, ``tox`` supports running unit tests "
"for other versions of Python and other database backends. Since Django's "
"test suite doesn't bundle a settings file for database backends other than "
"SQLite, however, you must :ref:`create and provide your own test settings "
"<running-unit-tests-settings>`. For example, to run the tests on Python 3.10 "
"using PostgreSQL:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na timpeallachtaí réamhshocraithe, tacaíonn ``tox` le "
"tástálacha aonaid a reáchtáil do leaganacha eile de Python agus cúltaca "
"bunachar sonraí eile. <running-unit-tests-settings>Ós rud é nach gcuireann "
"sraith tástála Django comhad socruithe le haghaidh cúltaca bunachar sonraí "
"seachas SQLite, áfach, ní mór duit: ref: `do shocruithe tástála féin a "
"chruthú agus a sholáthar `. Mar shampla, chun na tástálacha a reáchtáil ar "
"Python 3.10 ag baint úsáide as PostgreSQL:"

msgid ""
"This command sets up a Python 3.10 virtual environment, installs Django's "
"test suite dependencies (including those for PostgreSQL), and calls "
"``runtests.py`` with the supplied arguments (in this case, ``--"
"settings=my_postgres_settings``)."
msgstr ""
"Bunaíonn an t-ordú seo timpeallacht fhíorúil Python 3.10, suiteálann sé "
"spleáchais sraith tástála Django (lena n-áirítear iad siúd do PostgreSQL), "
"agus glaonn sé ``runtests.py`` leis na hargóintí a sholáthraítear (sa chás "
"seo, ``--settings=my_postgres_settings``)."

msgid ""
"The remainder of this documentation shows commands for running tests without "
"``tox``, however, any option passed to ``runtests.py`` can also be passed to "
"``tox`` by prefixing the argument list with ``--``, as above."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an chuid eile den doiciméadú seo orduithe chun tástálacha a "
"reáchtáil gan `tox`, áfach, is féidir aon rogha a chuirtear chuig "
"`runtests.py`` a chur chuig `tox`` tríd an liosta argóintí a réamhshocrú le "
"``--``, mar atá thuas."

msgid ""
"``Tox`` also respects the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment "
"variable, if set. For example, the following is equivalent to the command "
"above:"
msgstr ""
"Tá meas ag ``Tox`` freisin ar an athróg comhshaoil: envvar: "
"`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`, má tá sé socraithe. Mar shampla, tá an méid seo a "
"leanas comhionann leis an ordú thuas:"

msgid "Windows users should use:"
msgstr "Ba chóir d'úsáideoirí Windows a úsáid:"

msgid "Running the JavaScript tests"
msgstr "Na tástálacha JavaScript a rith"

msgid ""
"Django includes a set of :ref:`JavaScript unit tests <javascript-tests>` for "
"functions in certain contrib apps. The JavaScript tests aren't run by "
"default using ``tox`` because they require ``Node.js`` to be installed and "
"aren't necessary for the majority of patches. To run the JavaScript tests "
"using ``tox``:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django sraith de:ref: `Tástálacha aonad JavaScript <javascript-"
"tests>`le haghaidh feidhmeanna in aipeanna contrib áirithe. Ní reáchtáiltear "
"na tástálacha JavaScript de réir réamhshocraithe ag baint úsáide as `tox`` "
"toisc go n-éilíonn siad ``Node.js ``a shuiteáil agus nach bhfuil gá le "
"haghaidh formhór na bpaistí. Chun na tástálacha JavaScript a reáchtáil ag "
"baint úsáide as ``tox``:"

msgid ""
"This command runs ``npm install`` to ensure test requirements are up to date "
"and then runs ``npm test``."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann an t-ordú seo ``npm install ``chun a chinntiú go bhfuil riachtanais "
"tástála cothrom le dáta agus ansin ritheann sé ``npm tástáil``."

msgid "Running tests using ``django-docker-box``"
msgstr "Tástálacha a reáchtáil ag baint úsáide as ``django-docker-box``"

msgid ""
"`django-docker-box`_ allows you to run the Django's test suite across all "
"supported databases and python versions. See the `django-docker-box`_ "
"project page for installation and usage instructions."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann `django-docker-box `_ duit sraith tástála Django a reáchtáil ar fud "
"na bunachair sonraí go léir agus leaganacha python tacaithe. Féach "
"leathanach tionscadail `django-docker-box`_ le haghaidh treoracha suiteála "
"agus úsáide."

msgid "Using another ``settings`` module"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as modúl eile ``socruithe ``"

msgid ""
"The included settings module (``tests/test_sqlite.py``) allows you to run "
"the test suite using SQLite. If you want to run the tests using a different "
"database, you'll need to define your own settings file. Some tests, such as "
"those for ``contrib.postgres``, are specific to a particular database "
"backend and will be skipped if run with a different backend. Some tests are "
"skipped or expected failures on a particular database backend (see "
"``DatabaseFeatures.django_test_skips`` and "
"``DatabaseFeatures.django_test_expected_failures`` on each backend)."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modúl socruithe san áireamh (``tests/test_sqlite.py``) duit an "
"tsraith tástála a reáchtáil ag baint úsáide as SQLite. Más mian leat na "
"tástálacha a reáchtáil ag baint úsáide as bunachar sonraí difriúil, beidh "
"ort do chomhad socruithe féin a shainiú. Tá roinnt tástálacha, mar shampla "
"iad siúd do `contrib.postgres``, go sonrach le cúltaca bunachar sonraí "
"áirithe agus scipeánfar iad má reáchtáiltear le cúltaca difriúil. Scaiptear "
"roinnt tástálacha nó ag súil le teipeanna ar chúlcheann bunachar sonraí "
"áirithe (féach ``DatabaseFeatures.django_test_skips`` agus`` "
"databaseFeatures.django_test_expected_failures`` ar gach cúltaca)."

msgid ""
"To run the tests with different settings, ensure that the module is on "
"your :envvar:`PYTHONPATH` and pass the module with ``--settings``."
msgstr ""
"Chun na tástálacha a reáchtáil le socruithe éagsúla, cinntigh go bhfuil an "
"modúl ar do: envvar: `PYTHONPATH` agus pas an modúl le ``--socruithe ``."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`DATABASES` setting in any test settings module needs to define "
"two databases:"
msgstr ""
"Ní mór don socrú: SETTING: `DATABASES` in aon mhodúl socruithe tástála dhá "
"bhunachar sonraí a shainiú:"

msgid ""
"A ``default`` database. This database should use the backend that you want "
"to use for primary testing."
msgstr ""
"Bunachar sonraí ``réamhshocraithe``. Ba chóir go n-úsáideodh an bunachar "
"sonraí seo an cúltaca is mian leat a úsáid le haghaidh tástála bunscoile."

msgid ""
"A database with the alias ``other``. The ``other`` database is used to test "
"that queries can be directed to different databases. This database should "
"use the same backend as the ``default``, and it must have a different name."
msgstr ""
"Bunachar sonraí leis an ainm ``eile ``. Úsáidtear an bunachar sonraí ``eile "
"``chun a thástáil gur féidir ceisteanna a threorú chuig bunachair sonraí "
"éagsúla. Ba chóir go n-úsáidfeadh an bunachar sonraí seo an cúltaca céanna "
"leis an ``default``, agus caithfidh ainm difriúil a bheith aige."

msgid ""
"If you're using a backend that isn't SQLite, you will need to provide other "
"details for each database:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá cúltaca á úsáid agat nach SQLite, beidh ort sonraí eile a sholáthar do "
"gach bunachar sonraí:"

msgid ""
"The :setting:`USER` option needs to specify an existing user account for the "
"database. That user needs permission to execute ``CREATE DATABASE`` so that "
"the test database can be created."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an rogha :setting:`USER` cuntas úsáideora atá ann cheana a shonrú "
"don bhunachar sonraí. Teastaíonn cead ón úsáideoir sin ``CREATE DATABASE`` a "
"rith ionas gur féidir an bunachar sonraí tástála a chruthú."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`PASSWORD` option needs to provide the password for "
"the :setting:`USER` that has been specified."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór don rogha: SETTING: `PASSWORD` an pasfhocal a sholáthar don: socrú: "
"`USER` atá sonraithe."

msgid ""
"Test databases get their names by prepending ``test_`` to the value of "
"the :setting:`NAME` settings for the databases defined "
"in :setting:`DATABASES`. These test databases are deleted when the tests are "
"finished."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann bunachair shonraí tástála a n-ainmneacha trí ``tástáil_`` a réamh-"
"mheas ar luach na socruithe :setting:`NAME` do na bunachair shonraí atá "
"sainmhínithe i :suíomh:`BUNACHTAÍ SONRAÍ`. Scriostar na bunachair shonraí "
"tástála seo nuair a bhíonn na tástálacha críochnaithe."

msgid ""
"You will also need to ensure that your database uses UTF-8 as the default "
"character set. If your database server doesn't use UTF-8 as a default "
"charset, you will need to include a value for :setting:`CHARSET "
"<TEST_CHARSET>` in the test settings dictionary for the applicable database."
msgstr ""
"Beidh ort a chinntiú freisin go n-úsáideann do bhunachar sonraí UTF-8 mar an "
"tacar carachtair réamhshocraithe. Mura n-úsáideann do fhreastala "
"<TEST_CHARSET>í bunachar sonraí UTF-8 mar chartacar réamhshocraithe, beidh "
"ort luach fao:setting: `CHARSET `a chur san áireamh sa fhoclóir socruithe "
"tástála don bhunachar sonraí is infheidhme."

msgid "Running only some of the tests"
msgstr "Níl ach cuid de na tástálacha á rith"

msgid ""
"Django's entire test suite takes a while to run, and running every single "
"test could be redundant if, say, you just added a test to Django that you "
"want to run quickly without running everything else. You can run a subset of "
"the unit tests by appending the names of the test modules to ``runtests.py`` "
"on the command line."
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé tamall le sraith tástála iomlán Django a rith, agus d'fhéadfadh sé "
"a bheith iomarcach gach tástáil amháin a reáchtáil má chuir tú, abair, "
"díreach tástáil le Django gur mhaith leat a rith go tapa gan gach rud eile a "
"rith. Is féidir leat fo-thacar de na tástálacha aonaid a reáchtáil trí "
"ainmneacha na modúil tástála a chur leis ``runtests.py`` ar an líne ordaithe."

msgid ""
"For example, if you'd like to run tests only for generic relations and "
"internationalization, type:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, más mian leat tástálacha a reáchtáil ach le haghaidh caidreamh "
"cineálach agus idirnáisiúnú, clóscríobh:"

msgid ""
"How do you find out the names of individual tests? Look in ``tests/`` — each "
"directory name there is the name of a test."
msgstr ""
"Conas a aimsíonn tú ainmneacha na dtástálacha aonair? Féach in ``tástálacha/"
"`` - gach ainm eolaire tá ainm tástála ann."

msgid ""
"If you want to run only a particular class of tests, you can specify a list "
"of paths to individual test classes. For example, to run the "
"``TranslationTests`` of the ``i18n`` module, type:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ach aicme áirithe tástálacha a reáchtáil, is féidir leat "
"liosta cosáin a shonrú chuig ranganna tástála aonair. Mar shampla, chun an "
"`TranslationTests`` den mhodúl ``i18n`` a reáchtáil, cineál:"

msgid "Going beyond that, you can specify an individual test method like this:"
msgstr ""
"Ag dul níos faide ná sin, is féidir leat modh tástála aonair mar seo a "
"shonrú:"

msgid ""
"You can run tests starting at a specified top-level module with ``--start-"
"at`` option. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat tástálacha a reáchtáil ag tosú ag modúl barrleibhéil "
"sonraithe le rogha ``--start-at``. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"You can also run tests starting after a specified top-level module with ``--"
"start-after`` option. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat tástálacha a reáchtáil freisin ag tosú tar éis modúl "
"barrleibhéil sonraithe le rogha ``- start-after``. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Note that the ``--reverse`` option doesn't impact on ``--start-at`` or ``--"
