"likely to be merged into Django."
msgstr ""
"Anseo thíos, táimid chun a thaispeáint conas iarratas tarraingthe GitHub a "
"chruthú ina bhfuil na hathruithe ar thicéad Trac #xxxxx. Trí iarratas "
"tarraingthe go hiomlán réidh a chruthú, déanfaidh tú post an "
"athbhreithnitheora níos éasca, rud a chiallaíonn gur dóichí go ndéanfar "
"d'obair a chumasc i Django."

msgid ""
"You could also upload a traditional patch to Trac, but it's less practical "
"for reviews."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfá paiste traidisiúnta a uaslódáil chuig Trac freisin, ach níl sé "
"chomh praiticiúil le haghaidh athbhreithnithe."

msgid "Installing Git"
msgstr "Git á shuiteáil"

msgid ""
"Django uses `Git`_ for its source control. You can `download <https://git-"
"scm.com/download>`_ Git, but it's often easier to install with your "
"operating system's package manager."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django `Git `_ chun a rialú foinse. Is féidir leat `íoslódáil `_ < "
"https://git-scm.com/download> Git, ach is minic a bhíonn sé níos éasca a "
"shuiteáil le bainisteoir pacáiste do chórais oibriúcháin."

msgid ""
"Django's `Git repository`_ is hosted on `GitHub`_, and it is recommended "
"that you also work using GitHub."
msgstr ""
"Óstáiltear `Stórlann Git `_ Django ar `GitHub`_, agus moltar duit oibriú ag "
"baint úsáide as GitHub freisin."

msgid ""
"After installing Git, the first thing you should do is set up your name and "
"email:"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis Git a shuiteáil, is é an chéad rud ba chóir duit a dhéanamh ná "
"d'ainm agus ríomhphost a chur ar bun:"

msgid ""
"Note that ``user.name`` should be your real name, not your GitHub nick. "
"GitHub should know the email you use in the ``user.email`` field, as this "
"will be used to associate your commits with your GitHub account."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur chóir gurb é `user.name`` d'ainm fíor, ní d'ainm "
"GitHub. Ba chóir go mbeadh a fhios ag GitHub an ríomhphost a úsáideann tú sa "
"réimse ``user.email`, mar úsáidfear é seo chun do thiomantas a cheangal le "
"do chuntas GitHub."

msgid "Setting up local repository"
msgstr "Stóra áitiúil a bhunú"

msgid ""
"When you have created your GitHub account, with the nick \"GitHub_nick\", "
"and `forked Django's repository <https://github.com/django/django/fork>`__, "
"create a local copy of your fork:"
msgstr ""
"< https://github.com/django/django/fork>Nuair a bheidh do chuntas GitHub "
"cruthaithe agat, leis an nick “GitHub_nick”, agus `stór Django forctha `__, "
"cruthaigh cóip áitiúil de do fhorc:"

msgid ""
"This will create a new directory \"django\", containing a clone of your "
"GitHub repository. The rest of the git commands on this page need to be run "
"within the cloned directory, so switch to it now:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthóidh sé seo eolaire nua “django”, ina bhfuil clón de do stór GitHub. "
"Caithfear an chuid eile de na horduithe git ar an leathanach seo a reáchtáil "
"laistigh den eolaire clónaithe, mar sin aistrigh air anois:"

msgid "Your GitHub repository will be called \"origin\" in Git."
msgstr "Tugfar “bunús” ar do stór GitHub i Git."

msgid ""
"You should also set up ``django/django`` as an \"upstream\" remote (that is, "
"tell git that the reference Django repository was the source of your fork of "
"it):"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit ``django/django`` a chur ar bun mar iargúlta “suas sruth” (is "
"é sin, inis do git gurb é an stór tagartha Django foinse do fhorc de):"

msgid "You can add other remotes similarly, for example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat iargúlta eile a chur leis ar an gcaoi chéanna, mar shampla:"

msgid "Working on a ticket"
msgstr "Ag obair ar thicéad"

msgid ""
"When working on a ticket, create a new branch for the work, and base that "
"work on ``upstream/main``:"
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag obair ar thicéad, cruthaigh brainse nua don obair, agus bunaigh "
"an obair sin ar `upstream/main``:"

msgid ""
"The -b flag creates a new branch for you locally. Don't hesitate to create "
"new branches even for the smallest things - that's what they are there for."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn an bratach -b brainse nua duit go háitiúil. Ná bíodh aon leisce "
"ort brainsí nua a chruthú fiú do na rudaí is lú - sin a bhfuil siad ann."

msgid "If instead you were working for a fix on the 1.4 branch, you would do:"
msgstr ""
"Dá mbeadh tú ag obair ina ionad sin le haghaidh socrú ar an mbrainse 1.4, "
"déanfá:"

msgid ""
"Assume the work is carried on the ticket_xxxxx branch. Make some changes and "
"commit them:"
msgstr ""
"Glac leis go ndéantar an obair ar an mbrainse ticket_xxxxx. Déan roinnt "
"athruithe agus déan iad a dhéanamh:"

msgid ""
"When writing the commit message, follow the :ref:`commit message guidelines "
"<committing-guidelines>` to ease the work of the merger. If you're "
"uncomfortable with English, try at least to describe precisely what the "
"commit does."
msgstr ""
"Agus an teachtaireacht gealltanais á scríobh, lean na "
"treoirlínte :ref:`commit message <commit-guidelines>` chun obair an chumaisc "
"a éascú. Mura bhfuil tú compordach leis an mBéarla, déan iarracht ar a "
"laghad cur síos beacht a dhéanamh ar a ndéanann an tiomantas."

msgid ""
"If you need to do additional work on your branch, commit as often as "
"necessary:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit obair bhreise a dhéanamh ar do bhrainse, déan tiomantas chomh "
"minic agus is gá:"

msgid "Publishing work"
msgstr "Obair fhoilsithe"

msgid "You can publish your work on GitHub by running:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat do chuid oibre a fhoilsiú ar GitHub trí rith:"

msgid ""
"When you go to your GitHub page, you will notice a new branch has been "
"created."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a théann tú chuig do leathanach GitHub, tabharfaidh tú faoi deara go "
"bhfuil brainse nua cruthaithe."

msgid ""
"If you are working on a Trac ticket, you should mention in the ticket that "
"your work is available from branch ticket_xxxxx of your GitHub repo. Include "
"a link to your branch."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag obair ar thicéad Trac, ba chóir duit a lua sa ticéad go bhfuil "
"d'obair ar fáil ó bhrainse ticket_xxxxx de do repo GitHub. Cuir nasc chuig "
"do bhrainse san áireamh."

msgid ""
"Note that the above branch is called a \"topic branch\" in Git parlance. You "
"are free to rewrite the history of this branch, by using ``git rebase`` for "
"example. Other people shouldn't base their work on such a branch, because "
"their clone would become corrupt when you edit commits."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go dtugtar \"brainse ábhar\" ar an mbrainse thuas i "
"parlance Git. Tá cead agat stair an bhrainse seo a athscríobh, trí ``git "
"rebase`` a úsáid mar shampla. Níor cheart do dhaoine eile a gcuid oibre a "
"bhunú ar bhrainse den sórt sin, mar go n-éireodh a gclón truaillithe nuair a "
"dhéanann tú eagarthóireacht ar ghealltanais."

msgid ""
"There are also \"public branches\". These are branches other people are "
"supposed to fork, so the history of these branches should never change. Good "
"examples of public branches are the ``main`` and ``stable/A.B.x`` branches "
"in the ``django/django`` repository."
msgstr ""
"Tá “brainsí poiblí” ann freisin. Is brainsí iad seo atá ceaptha do dhaoine "
"eile a fhorc, mar sin níor chóir go n-athródh stair na mbrainsí seo riamh. "
"Is iad samplaí maithe de bhrainsí poiblí na brainsí ``main`` agus `stable/"
"A.B.X`` sa stór `django/django``."

msgid ""
"When you think your work is ready to be pulled into Django, you should "
"create a pull request at GitHub. A good pull request means:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a cheapann tú go bhfuil do chuid oibre réidh le tarraingt isteach i "
"Django, ba cheart duit iarratas tarraingthe a chruthú ag GitHub. Ciallaíonn "
"iarratas tarraingthe maith:"

msgid ""
"commits with one logical change in each, following the :doc:`coding style "
"<coding-style>`,"
msgstr ""
"<coding-style>geallann sé le hathrú loighciúil amháin i ngach ceann, ag "
"leanúint na:doc: `stíl chódú `,"

msgid ""
"well-formed messages for each commit: a summary line and then paragraphs "
"wrapped at 72 characters thereafter -- see the :ref:`committing guidelines "
"<committing-guidelines>` for more details,"
msgstr ""
"teachtaireachtaí dea-fhoirmithe do gach tiomantas: líne achoimre agus ansin "
"míreanna atá fillte ag 72 carachtar ina dhiaidh sin - féach in:ref: "
"`treoirlínte tiomanta <committing-guidelines>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí,"

msgid ""
"documentation and tests, if needed -- actually tests are always needed, "
"except for documentation changes."
msgstr ""
"doiciméadú agus tástálacha, más gá -- bíonn tástálacha de dhíth i gcónaí, "
"ach amháin má dhéantar athruithe ar dhoiciméid."

msgid ""
"The test suite must pass and the documentation must build without warnings."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an seomra tástála pas a fháil agus ní mór na doiciméid a thógáil "
"gan rabhadh."

msgid ""
"Once you have created your pull request, you should add a comment in the "
"related Trac ticket explaining what you've done. In particular, you should "
"note the environment in which you ran the tests, for instance: \"all tests "
"pass under SQLite and MySQL\"."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh d'iarratas tarraingthe cruthaithe agat, ba cheart duit trácht "
"a chur leis sa ticéad Trac gaolmhar ag míniú cad atá déanta agat. Go "
"háirithe, ba chóir duit an timpeallacht inar reáchtáil tú na tástálacha a "
"thabhairt faoi deara, mar shampla: “téann gach tástáil faoi SQLite agus "
"MySQL”."

msgid ""
"Pull requests at GitHub have only two states: open and closed. The merger "
"who will deal with your pull request has only two options: merge it or close "
"it. For this reason, it isn't useful to make a pull request until the code "
"is ready for merging -- or sufficiently close that a merger will finish it "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
"Níl ach dhá stát ag iarratais tarraingthe ag GitHub: oscailte agus dúnta. "
"Níl ach dhá rogha ag an gcumasc a dhéileálfaidh le d'iarratas tarraingthe: é "
"a chumasc nó é a dhúnadh. Ar an gcúis seo, níl sé úsáideach iarratas "
"tarraingthe a dhéanamh go dtí go mbeidh an cód réidh le cumasc - nó gar go "
"leor go gcríochnóidh cumaisc é féin."

msgid "Rebasing branches"
msgstr "Brainsí a athbhunú"

msgid ""
"In the example above, you created two commits, the \"Fixed ticket_xxxxx\" "
"commit and \"Added two more tests\" commit."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, chruthaigh tú dhá thiomantas, an tiomantas “Ticéad Seasta "
"xxxxx” agus “Cuireadh dhá thástáil eile leis”."

msgid ""
"We do not want to have the entire history of your working process in your "
"repository. Your commit \"Added two more tests\" would be unhelpful noise. "
"Instead, we would rather only have one commit containing all your work."
msgstr ""
"Níl muid ag iarraidh stair iomlán do phróisis oibre a bheith agat i do stór. "
"Bheadh torann neamhchabhrach do thiomantas “Cuireadh dhá thástáil eile "
"leis”. Ina áit sin, b'fhearr linn ach tiomantas amháin a mbeadh do chuid "
"oibre go léir ann."

msgid ""
"To rework the history of your branch you can squash the commits into one by "
"using interactive rebase:"
msgstr ""
"Chun stair do bhrainse a athoibriú is féidir leat na gealltanais a scuabadh "
"i gceann amháin trí athbhunú idirghníomhach a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"The HEAD~2 above is shorthand for two latest commits. The above command will "
"open an editor showing the two commits, prefixed with the word \"pick\"."
msgstr ""
"Is gearrthóg é an HEAD ~ 2 thuas do dhá thiomantas is déanaí. Osclóidh an t-"
"ordú thuas eagarthóir a thaispeánann an dá thiomantas, réamhshocraithe leis "
"an bhfocal “pioc”."

msgid ""
"Change \"pick\" on the second line to \"squash\" instead. This will keep the "
"first commit, and squash the second commit into the first one. Save and quit "
"the editor. A second editor window should open, so you can reword the commit "
"message for the commit now that it includes both your steps."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh “pioc” ar an dara líne go “squash” ina ionad sin. Coinneoidh sé seo "
"an chéad tiomantas, agus cuirfidh sé an dara tiomantas isteach sa chéad "
"cheann. Sábháil agus scor an t-eagarthóir. Ba chóir go n-osclaíonn an dara "
"fuinneog eagarthóra, ionas gur féidir leat an teachtaireacht tiomanta don "
"tiomantas a athfhocal anois go bhfuil an dá chéim ann."

msgid ""
"You can also use the \"edit\" option in rebase. This way you can change a "
"single commit, for example to fix a typo in a docstring:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an rogha “eagarthóireacht” a úsáid i rebase freisin. Ar an "
"mbealach seo is féidir leat tiomantas amháin a athrú, mar shampla chun "
"clóscríobh a shocrú i docstring:"

msgid ""
"If your topic branch is already published at GitHub, for example if you're "
"making minor changes to take into account a review, you will need to force-"
"push the changes:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá do bhrainse ábhar foilsithe cheana féin ag GitHub, mar shampla má tá "
"mionathruithe á dhéanamh agat chun athbhreithniú a chur san áireamh, beidh "
"ort na hathruithe a bhrú go foréigeach:"

msgid ""
"Note that this will rewrite history of ticket_xxxxx - if you check the "
"commit hashes before and after the operation at GitHub you will notice that "
"the commit hashes do not match anymore. This is acceptable, as the branch is "
"a topic branch, and nobody should be basing their work on it."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go n-athscríobfaidh sé seo stair ticket_xxxxx - má "
"sheiceálann tú na hashes tiomanta roimh agus tar éis na hoibríochta ag "
"GitHub tabharfaidh tú faoi deara nach n-oireann na hashes tiomanta níos mó. "
"Tá sé seo inghlactha, toisc gur brainse ábhar í an bhrainse, agus níor "
"cheart d'aon duine a bheith ag bhunú a gcuid oibre air."

msgid "After upstream has changed"
msgstr "Tar éis athrú suas sruth"

msgid ""
"When upstream (``django/django``) has changed, you should rebase your work. "
"To do this, use:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a athraíonn suas sruth (``django/django``), ba cheart duit do chuid "
"oibre a athbhunú. Chun seo a dhéanamh, bain úsáid as:"

msgid ""
"The work is automatically rebased using the branch you forked on, in the "
"example case using ``upstream/main``."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an obair a athbhunú go huathoibríoch ag baint úsáide as an mbrainse "
"a rinne tú air, sa chás samplach ag baint úsáide as `upstream/main``."

msgid ""
"The rebase command removes all your local commits temporarily, applies the "
"upstream commits, and then applies your local commits again on the work."
msgstr ""
"Baineann an t-ordú rebase do ghealltanais áitiúla go léir go sealadach, "
"cuireann an gealltanas in aghaidh an tsrutha i bhfeidhm, agus ansin cuireann "
"do ghealltanas áitiúil i bhfeidhm arís ar an obair."

msgid ""
"If there are merge conflicts, you will need to resolve them and then use "
"``git rebase --continue``. At any point you can use ``git rebase --abort`` "
"to return to the original state."
msgstr ""
"Má tá coinbhleachtaí cumaisc ann, beidh ort iad a réiteach agus ansin ``git "
"rebase --continue`` a úsáid. Ag pointe ar bith is féidir leat ``git rebase --"
"abort`` a úsáid chun filleadh ar an stát bunaidh."

msgid "Note that you want to *rebase* on upstream, not *merge* the upstream."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go dteastaíonn uait* a athbhunú* ar an sruth, ne*cumasch* "
"an suas sruth."

msgid ""
"The reason for this is that by rebasing, your commits will always be *on top "
"of* the upstream's work, not *mixed in with* the changes in the upstream. "
"This way your branch will contain only commits related to its topic, which "
"makes squashing easier."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chúis atá leis seo ná go mbeidh do thiomantas i gcónaí* ar bharr* "
"obair an tsraith, ne*measctha la* na hathruithe ar an sruth suas. Ar an "
"mbealach seo ní bheidh ach gealltanais a bhaineann lena ábhar i do bhrainse, "
"rud a fhágann go bhfuil sé níos éasca squashing."

msgid "After review"
msgstr "Tar éis léirmheas"

msgid ""
"It is unusual to get any non-trivial amount of code into core without "
"changes requested by reviewers. In this case, it is often a good idea to add "
"the changes as one incremental commit to your work. This allows the reviewer "
"to easily check what changes you have done."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé neamhghnách aon mhéid cód neamh-thráthúil a fháil isteach i gcroílár "
"gan athruithe a iarrann athbhreithnithe. Sa chás seo, is minic gur "
"smaoineamh maith é na hathruithe a chur leis mar thiomantas incriminteach "
"amháin do do chuid oibre. Ligeann sé seo don athbhreithneoir na hathruithe "
"atá déanta agat a sheiceáil go héasca."

msgid ""
"In this case, do the changes required by the reviewer. Commit as often as "
"necessary. Before publishing the changes, rebase your work. If you added two "
"commits, you would run:"
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, déan na hathruithe a theastaíonn ón athbhreithneoir. Tiomantas "
"chomh minic agus is gá. Sula bhfoilsíonn na hathruithe, déan do chuid oibre "
"a athbhun Má chuir tú dhá thiomantas leis, rith tú:"

msgid ""
"Squash the second commit into the first. Write a commit message along the "
"lines of:"
msgstr ""
"Squash an dara tiomantas isteach sa chéad cheann. Scríobh teachtaireacht "
"tiomanta ar na línte de:"

msgid ""
"Finally, push your work back to your GitHub repository. Since you didn't "
"touch the public commits during the rebase, you should not need to force-"
"push:"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, brúigh do chuid oibre ar ais chuig do stór GitHub. Ós rud é "
"nár chuir tú teagmháil leis na gealltanais phoiblí le linn an athbhunaithe, "
"níor cheart go mbeadh ort brú go foréigeantach:"

msgid "Your pull request should now contain the new commit too."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an tiomantas nua i d'iarratas tarraingthe anois freisin."

msgid ""
"Note that the merger is likely to squash the review commit into the previous "
"commit when committing the code."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur dócha go gcuirfidh an cumasc an gealltanas "
"athbhreithnithe isteach sa ghealltanas roimhe seo agus an cód á ghealladh."

msgid "Working on a patch"
msgstr "Ag obair ar phaiste"

msgid ""
"One of the ways that developers can contribute to Django is by reviewing "
"patches. Those patches will typically exist as pull requests on GitHub and "
"can be easily integrated into your local repository:"
msgstr ""
"Ceann de na bealaí is féidir le forbróirí cur le Django ná trí phaistí a "
"athbhreithniú. De ghnáth beidh na paistí sin ann mar iarratais tarraingthe "
"ar GitHub agus is féidir iad a chomhtháthú go héasca i do stór áitiúil:"

msgid ""
"This will create a new branch and then apply the changes from the pull "
"request to it. At this point you can run the tests or do anything else you "
"need to do to investigate the quality of the patch."
msgstr ""
"Cruthóidh sé seo brainse nua agus ansin cuirfidh sé na hathruithe ón "
"iarratas tarraingthe i bhfeidhm air. Ag an bpointe seo is féidir leat na "
"tástálacha a reáchtáil nó aon rud eile a dhéanamh a chaithfidh tú a dhéanamh "
"chun cáilíocht an phaiste a imscrúdú."

msgid ""
"For more detail on working with pull requests see the :ref:`guidelines for "
"mergers <handling-pull-requests>`."
msgstr ""
"<handling-pull-requests>Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí maidir le hoibriú le "
"hiarratais tarraingthe féach in:ref: `treoirlínte maidir le cumaisc `."

msgid "Summary"
msgstr "Achoimre"

msgid "Work on GitHub if you can."
msgstr "Oibrigh ar GitHub más féidir leat."

msgid "Announce your work on the Trac ticket by linking to your GitHub branch."
msgstr ""
"Fógraigh d'obair ar thicéad Trac trí nasc a dhéanamh le do bhrainse GitHub."

msgid "When you have something ready, make a pull request."
msgstr "Nuair a bhíonn rud éigin réidh agat, déan iarratas tarraingthe."

msgid "Make your pull requests as good as you can."
msgstr "Déan d'iarratais tarraingthe chomh maith agus is féidir leat."

msgid ""
"When doing fixes to your work, use ``git rebase -i`` to squash the commits."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag déanamh ceartúcháin ar do chuid oibre, bain úsáid as ``git rebase "
"-i`` chun na gealltanais a scuabadh."

msgid "When upstream has changed, do ``git fetch upstream; git rebase``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh athraithe suas sruth, déan ``git fetch upstream; git rebase``."

msgid "Writing documentation"
msgstr "Scríobh cáipéis"

msgid ""
"We place high importance on the consistency and readability of "
"documentation. After all, Django was created in a journalism environment! So "
"we treat our documentation like we treat our code: we aim to improve it as "
"often as possible."
msgstr ""
"Cuirimid an-tábhacht ar chomhsheasmhacht agus ar inléiteacht na ndoiciméad. "
"Tar éis an tsaoil, cruthaíodh Django i dtimpeallacht iriseoireachta! Mar sin "
"caithimid lenár ndoiciméadú mar a chaithimid lenár gcód: tá sé mar aidhm "
"againn é a fheabhsú chomh minic agus is féidir."

msgid "Documentation changes generally come in two forms:"
msgstr "De ghnáth is dhá fhoirm a bhíonn athruithe doiciméadaithe:"

msgid ""
"General improvements: typo corrections, error fixes and better explanations "
"through clearer writing and more examples."
msgstr ""
"Feabhsuithe ginearálta: ceartúcháin tíopála, earráidí a cheartú agus "
"míniúcháin níos fearr trí scríobh níos soiléire agus níos mó samplaí."

msgid ""
"New features: documentation of features that have been added to the "
"framework since the last release."
msgstr ""
"Gnéithe nua: doiciméadú gnéithe a cuireadh leis an gcreat ón scaoileadh "
"deireanach."

msgid ""
"This section explains how writers can craft their documentation changes in "
"the most useful and least error-prone ways."
msgstr ""
"Mínítear sa chuid seo conas is féidir le scríbhneoirí athruithe a dhéanamh "
"ar a ndoiciméadú ar na bealaí is úsáidí agus is lú seans go mbeidh earráidí "
"ann."

msgid "The Django documentation process"
msgstr "An próiseas doiciméadaithe Django"

msgid ""
"Though Django's documentation is intended to be read as HTML at https://"
"docs.djangoproject.com/, we edit it as a collection of plain text files "
"written in the reStructuredText markup language for maximum flexibility."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil sé beartaithe doiciméadú Django a léamh mar HTML ag https://"
"docs.djangoproject.com/, déanaimid é a chur in eagar mar bhailiúchán de "
"chomhaid téacs simplí atá scríofa sa teanga marcála RestructuredText chun an "
"tsolúbthacht is mó a fháil."

msgid ""
"We work from the development version of the repository because it has the "
"latest-and-greatest documentation, just as it has the latest-and-greatest "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Oibrímid ó leagan forbartha an stór toisc go bhfuil an doiciméadú is déanaí "
"agus is mó aige, díreach mar atá an cód is déanaí agus is mó aige."

msgid ""
"We also backport documentation fixes and improvements, at the discretion of "
"the merger, to the last release branch. This is because it's advantageous to "
"have the docs for the last release be up-to-date and correct "
"(see :ref:`differences-between-doc-versions`)."
msgstr ""
"Déanaimid socruithe agus feabhsuithe doiciméadaithe ar ais freisin, de réir "
"rogha an chumaisc, go dtí an bhrainse scaoilte deireanach. Tá sé seo toisc "
"go bhfuil sé buntáisteach go mbeadh na doiciméid don eisiúint deireanach "
"cothrom le dáta agus ceart (féach: ref: `difríochtaí idir doc-versions`)."

msgid ""
"Django's documentation uses the Sphinx__ documentation system, which in turn "
"is based on docutils__. The basic idea is that lightly-formatted plain-text "
"documentation is transformed into HTML, PDF, and any other output format."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann cáipéisíocht Django córas doiciméadaithe Sphinx__, atá bunaithe ar "
"docutils__ ina dhiaidh sin. Is é an smaoineamh bunúsach ná go ndéantar "
"doiciméadú téacs simplí formáidithe go héadrom a athrú go HTML, PDF, agus "
"aon fhormáid aschuir eile."

msgid ""
"Sphinx includes a ``sphinx-build`` command for turning reStructuredText into "
"other formats, e.g., HTML and PDF. This command is configurable, but the "
"Django documentation includes a ``Makefile`` that provides a shorter ``make "
"html`` command."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Sphinx ordú ``sphinx-build`` chun RestructuredText a iompú i "
"bhformáidí eile, m.sh., HTML agus PDF. Tá an t-ordú seo inchumraithe, ach "
"cuimsíonn cáipéisíocht Django ``Makefile`` a sholáthraíonn ordú ``make "
"html`` níos giorra."

msgid "How the documentation is organized"
msgstr "Conas a eagraítear na doiciméid"

msgid "The documentation is organized into several categories:"
msgstr "Tá an doiciméadú eagraithe i roinnt catagóirí:"

msgid ""
":doc:`Tutorials </intro/index>` take the reader by the hand through a series "
"of steps to create something."
msgstr ""
":doc: Tógann `Tutorials` </intro/index> an léitheoir de láimh trí shraith "
"céimeanna chun rud éigin a chruthú."

msgid ""
"The important thing in a tutorial is to help the reader achieve something "
"useful, preferably as early as possible, in order to give them confidence."
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud tábhachtach i rang teagaisc cabhrú leis an léitheoir rud éigin "
"úsáideach a bhaint amach, b'fhearr chomh luath agus is féidir, d'fhonn "
"muinín a thabhairt dóibh."

msgid ""
"Explain the nature of the problem we're solving, so that the reader "
"understands what we're trying to achieve. Don't feel that you need to begin "
"with explanations of how things work - what matters is what the reader does, "
"not what you explain. It can be helpful to refer back to what you've done "
"and explain afterward."
msgstr ""
"Mínigh nádúr na fadhbanna atá á réiteach againn, ionas go dtuigeann an "
"léitheoir cad atá againn ag iarraidh a bhaint amach. Ná mhothaigh gur gá "
"duit tosú le mínithe ar an gcaoi a n-oibríonn rudaí - is é an rud is "
"tábhachtaí ná cad a dhéanann an léitheoir, ní an méid a mhíníonn tú "
"D'fhéadfadh sé a bheith cabhrach tagairt a dhéanamh ar ais don méid a rinne "
"tú agus míniú ina dhiaidh sin."

msgid ""
":doc:`Topic guides </topics/index>` aim to explain a concept or subject at a "
"fairly high level."
msgstr ""
":doc: Tá sé mar aidhm ag `treoracha topaic' coin</topics/index> cheap nó "
"ábhar a mhíniú ag leibhéal réasúnta ard."

msgid ""
"Link to reference material rather than repeat it. Use examples and don't be "
"reluctant to explain things that seem very basic to you - it might be the "
"explanation someone else needs."
msgstr ""
"Nasc le hábhar tagartha seachas é a athdhéanamh. Úsáid samplaí agus ná bíodh "
"drogall ort rudaí atá an-bhunúsach duit a mhíniú - b'fhéidir gurb é an míniú "
"a theastaíonn ó dhuine eile."

msgid ""
"Providing background context helps a newcomer connect the topic to things "
"that they already know."
msgstr ""
"Trí chomhthéacs cúlra a sholáthar cabhraíonn sé le núíosach an topaic a "
"nascadh le rudaí atá ar eolas acu cheana féin."

msgid ""
":doc:`Reference guides </ref/index>` contain technical references for APIs. "
"They describe the functioning of Django's internal machinery and instruct in "
"its use."
msgstr ""
":doc: Tá tagairtí teicniúla do APIs in `treoracha </ref/index> tagartha. "
"Déanann siad cur síos ar fheidhmiú innealra inmheánach Django agus tugann "
"siad treoir maidir lena úsáid."

msgid ""
"Keep reference material tightly focused on the subject. Assume that the "
"reader already understands the basic concepts involved but needs to know or "
"be reminded of how Django does it."
msgstr ""
"Coinnigh ábhar tagartha dírithe go docht ar an ábhar. Glac leis go dtuigeann "
"an léitheoir cheana féin na bunchoincheapa atá i gceist ach go gcaithfidh sé "
"fios a bheith aige nó a mheabhrú conas a dhéanann Django é."

msgid ""
"Reference guides aren't the place for general explanation. If you find "
"yourself explaining basic concepts, you may want to move that material to a "
"topic guide."
msgstr ""
"Ní hé treoracha tagartha an áit le haghaidh míniú ginearálta. Má fhaigheann "
"tú tú féin ag míniú bunchoincheapa, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an t-ábhar sin "
"a aistriú chuig treoir ábhair."

msgid ""
":doc:`How-to guides </howto/index>` are recipes that take the reader through "
"steps in key subjects."
msgstr ""
":doc: Is oidis iad `treoirlínte cona' a thó</howto/index> gann an léitheoir "
"trí chéimeanna sna príomhábhair."

msgid ""
"What matters most in a how-to guide is what a user wants to achieve. A how-"
"to should always be result-oriented rather than focused on internal details "
"of how Django implements whatever is being discussed."
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud is tábhachtaí i dtreoir conas is féidir leis an úsáideoir a "
"bhaint amach. Ba chóir go mbeadh conas-le-dírithe i gcónaí ar thorthaí "
"seachas a bheith dírithe ar shonraí inmheánacha faoin gcaoi a gcuireann "
"Django i bhfeidhm cibé rud atá á phlé."

msgid ""
"These guides are more advanced than tutorials and assume some knowledge "
"about how Django works. Assume that the reader has followed the tutorials "
"and don't hesitate to refer the reader back to the appropriate tutorial "
"rather than repeat the same material."
msgstr ""
"Tá na treoracha seo níos airde ná ranganna teagaisc agus glacann siad roinnt "
"eolais faoi conas a oibríonn Django. Glac leis gur lean an léitheoir na "
"ranganna teagaisc agus ná bíodh aon leisce ort an léitheoir a tharchur ar "
"ais chuig an rang teagaisc cuí seachas an t-ábhar céanna a athdhéanamh."

msgid "How to start contributing documentation"
msgstr "Conas tosú ag cur cáipéisíocht"

msgid "Clone the Django repository to your local machine"
msgstr "Clóin stór Django chuig do mheaisín áitiúil"

msgid ""
"If you'd like to start contributing to our docs, get the development version "
"of Django from the source code repository (see :ref:`installing-development-"
"version`):"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat tosú ag cur lenár ndoiciméad, faigh an leagan forbartha de "
"Django ón stór cód foinse (féach: ref: `installing-development-version`):"

msgid ""
"If you're planning to submit these changes, you might find it useful to make "
"a fork of the Django repository and clone this fork instead."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé ar intinn agat na hathruithe seo a chur isteach, b'fhéidir go "
"mbeadh sé úsáideach duit forc a dhéanamh de stór Django agus an forc seo a "
"chlónú ina ionad sin."

msgid "Set up a virtual environment and install dependencies"
msgstr "Cuir timpeallacht fhíorúil ar bun agus spleáchais a shuiteáil"

msgid ""
"Create and activate a virtual environment, then install the dependencies:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh agus gníomhachtaigh timpeallacht fhíorúil, ansin suiteáil na "
"spleáchais:"

msgid "Build the documentation locally"
msgstr "Tóg an doiciméadú go háiti"

msgid "We can build HTML output from the ``docs`` directory:"
msgstr "Is féidir linn aschur HTML a thógáil ón eolaire ``docs`:"

msgid ""
"Your locally-built documentation will be accessible at ``_build/html/"
"index.html`` and it can be viewed in any web browser, though it will be "
"themed differently than the documentation at `docs.djangoproject.com "
"<https://docs.djangoproject.com/>`_. This is OK! If your changes look good "
"on your local machine, they'll look good on the website."
msgstr ""
"Beidh do dhoiciméadú tógtha go háitiúil inrochtana ag ``_build/html/"
"index.html`` agus is féidir é a fheiceáil in aon bhrabhsálaí gréasáin, cé go "
"mbeidh téama difriúil air ná an doiciméadú ag `docs.djangoproject.com`_. < "
"https://docs.djangoproject.com/> Tá sé seo ceart go leor! Má tá cuma mhaith "
"ar d'athruithe ar do mheaisín áitiúil, beidh cuma mhaith orthu ar an suíomh "
"Gréasáin."

msgid "Making edits to the documentation"
msgstr "Eagarthóireachtaí a dhéanamh ar an doiciméadacht"

msgid "The source files are ``.txt`` files located in the ``docs/`` directory."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na comhaid foinse comhaid ``.txt`` atá lonnaithe san eolaire ``docs/"
"``."

msgid ""
"These files are written in the reStructuredText markup language. To learn "
"the markup, see the :ref:`reStructuredText reference <sphinx:rst-index>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá na comhaid seo scríofa sa teanga marcála RestructuredText. <sphinx:rst-"
"index>Chun an marcáil a fhoghlaim, féach an tagairt: ref: `RestructuredText "
"`."

msgid ""
"To edit this page, for example, we would edit the file :source:`docs/"
"internals/contributing/writing-documentation.txt` and rebuild the HTML with "
"``make html``."
msgstr ""
"Chun an leathanach seo a chur in eagar, mar shampla, déanfaimis an "
"comhad:source: `docs/internals/contributing/writing-documentation.txt` a "
"chur in eagar agus an HTML a atógáil le ``make html``."

msgid "Documentation quality checks"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Several checks help maintain Django's documentation quality, "
"including :ref:`spelling <documentation-spelling-check>` and :ref:`code "
"block formatting <documentation-code-block-format-check>`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These checks are run automatically in CI and must pass before documentation "
"changes can be merged. They can also be run locally with a single command:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This command runs all current checks and will include any new checks added "
"in the future."
msgstr ""

msgid "Spelling check"
msgstr "Seiceáil litrithe"

msgid ""
"Before you commit your docs, it's a good idea to run the spelling checker. "
"You'll need to install :pypi:`sphinxcontrib-spelling` first. Then from the "
"``docs`` directory, run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Wrong words (if any) along with the file and line number where they occur "
"will be saved to ``_build/spelling/output.txt``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you encounter false-positives (error output that actually is correct), do "
"one of the following:"
msgstr ""
"Má thagann tú ar dhearfacha bréagacha (aschur earráide atá ceart i "
"ndáiríre), déan ceann de na nithe seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Surround inline code or brand/technology names with double grave accents "
"(``)."
msgstr ""
"Cód inlíne timpeall nó ainmneacha branda/teicneolaíochta le haicintí uaigh "
"dúbailte (``)."

msgid "Find synonyms that the spell checker recognizes."
msgstr "Faigh comhchiallaigh a aithníonn an seiceálaí litrithe."

msgid ""
"If, and only if, you are sure the word you are using is correct - add it to "
"``docs/spelling_wordlist`` (please keep the list in alphabetical order)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú cinnte go bhfuil an focal atá á úsáid agat ceart - cuir é le `docs/"
"spelling_wordlist`` (coinnigh an liosta in ord aibítre le do thoil)."

msgid "Code block format check"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All Python code blocks should be formatted using the :pypi:`blacken-docs` "
"auto-formatter. This is automatically run by the :ref:`pre-commit hook "
"<coding-style-pre-commit>` if configured."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The check can also be run manually: provided that ``blacken-docs`` is "
"installed, run the following command from the ``docs`` directory:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The formatter will report any issues by printing them to the terminal and "
"will reformat code blocks where possible."
msgstr ""

msgid "Link check"
msgstr "Seiceáil nasc"

msgid ""
"Links in documentation can become broken or changed such that they are no "
"longer the canonical link. Sphinx provides a builder that can check whether "
"the links in the documentation are working. From the ``docs`` directory, run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Output is printed to the terminal, but can also be found in ``_build/"
"linkcheck/output.txt`` and ``_build/linkcheck/output.json``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The execution of the command requires an internet connection and takes "
"several minutes to complete, because the command tests all the links that "
"are found in the documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Entries that have a status of \"working\" are fine, those that are "
"\"unchecked\" or \"ignored\" have been skipped because they either cannot be "
"checked or have matched ignore rules in the configuration."
msgstr ""
"Tá iontrálacha a bhfuil stádas “ag obair” acu go breá, scipeánadh iad siúd "
"nach bhfuil “neamh-sheiceáil” nó “neamhaird orthu” toisc nach féidir iad a "
"sheiceáil nó gur mheaitseáil siad rialacha neamhaird sa chumraíocht."

msgid ""
"Entries that have a status of \"broken\" need to be fixed. Those that have a "
"status of \"redirected\" may need to be updated to point to the canonical "
"location, e.g. the scheme has changed ``http://`` → ``https://``. In certain "
"cases, we do not want to update a \"redirected\" link, e.g. a rewrite to "
"always point to the latest or stable version of the documentation, e.g. ``/"
"en/stable/`` → ``/en/3.2/``."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór iontrálacha a bhfuil stádas “briste” acu a shocrú. B'fhéidir go "
"gcaithfear iad siúd a bhfuil stádas “atreoraithe” acu a nuashonrú chun an "
"suíomh canónach a chur in iúl, m.sh. tá athrú tagtha ar an scéim ``http: //"
"`` → ``https: //``. I gcásanna áirithe, níl muid ag iarraidh nasc "
"“atreoraithe” a nuashonrú, m.sh. athscríobh chun an leagan is déanaí nó "
"cobhsaí den doiciméad a chur in iúl i gcónaí, m.sh. `/en/stable/`` → ``/en/"
"3.2/``."

msgid "Writing style"
msgstr "Stíl scríobh"

msgid ""
"When using pronouns in reference to a hypothetical person, such as \"a user "
"with a session cookie\", gender-neutral pronouns (they/their/them) should be "
"used. Instead of:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear forainmneacha i dtagairt do dhuine hipitéiseach, mar "
"shampla “úsáideoir le fianán seisiúin”, ba cheart ainmneacha neodrach ó "
"inscne (siú/iad féin) a úsáid. In ionad:"

msgid "he or she... use they."
msgstr "úsáideann sé nó sí... iad."

msgid "him or her... use them."
msgstr "é nó í... bain úsáid as iad."

msgid "his or her... use their."
msgstr "a chuid nó í... bain úsáid as a gcuid."

msgid "his or hers... use theirs."
msgstr "a chuid féin nó a... bain úsáid as a gcuid féin."

msgid "himself or herself... use themselves."
msgstr "é féin nó í féin... bain úsáid as iad féin."

msgid ""
"Try to avoid using words that minimize the difficulty involved in a task or "
"operation, such as \"easily\", \"simply\", \"just\", \"merely\", "
"\"straightforward\", and so on. People's experience may not match your "
"expectations, and they may become frustrated when they do not find a step as "
"\"straightforward\" or \"simple\" as it is implied to be."
msgstr ""
"Déan iarracht focail a úsáid a sheachaint a íoslaghdaíonn an deacracht a "
"bhaineann le tasc nó oibríocht, mar shampla “go héasca”, “go simplí”, "
"“díreach”, “díreach”, “simplí”, agus mar sin de. B'fhéidir nach n-oireann "
"taithí daoine le d'ionchais, agus d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh frustrachas orthu "
"nuair nach bhfaigheann siad céim chomh “simplí” nó “simplí” agus a thugtar "
"le tuiscint a bheith."

msgid "Commonly used terms"
msgstr "Téarmaí a úsáidtear go co"

msgid ""
"Here are some style guidelines on commonly used terms throughout the "
"documentation:"
msgstr ""
"Seo roinnt treoirlínte stíle ar théarmaí a úsáidtear go coitianta ar fud an "
"doiciméid:"

msgid ""
"**Django** -- when referring to the framework, capitalize Django. It is "
"lowercase only in Python code and in the djangoproject.com logo."
msgstr ""
"**Django** - agus tú ag tagairt don chreat, caipitligh Django. Níl sé le "
"litreacha beaga ach i gcód Python agus i lógó djangoproject.com."

msgid "**email** -- no hyphen."
msgstr "**ríomhphost** - gan aon bhreith."

msgid ""
"**HTTP** -- the expected pronunciation is \"Aitch Tee Tee Pee\" and "
"therefore should be preceded by \"an\" and not \"a\"."
msgstr ""
"**HTTP** - is é “Aitch Tee Tee Pee” an fuaimniú a bhfuil súil leis agus dá "
"bhrí sin ba cheart “an” agus ní “a” roimh ré."

msgid "**MySQL**, **PostgreSQL**, **SQLite**"
msgstr "**MySQL**, **PostgreSQL**, **SQLite**"

msgid ""
"**SQL** -- when referring to SQL, the expected pronunciation should be \"Ess "
"Queue Ell\" and not \"sequel\". Thus in a phrase like \"Returns an SQL "
"expression\", \"SQL\" should be preceded by \"an\" and not \"a\"."
msgstr ""
"**SQL** - agus tú ag tagairt do SQL, ba chóir go mbeadh “Ess Queue Ell” an "
"fuaimniú ag súil leis agus ní “seicheamh”. Dá bhrí sin i abairt mar “Tugann "
"sé abairt SQL ar ais”, ba chóir “an” a bheith roimh “SQL” agus ní “a”."

msgid "**Python** -- when referring to the language, capitalize Python."
msgstr "**Python** - agus tú ag tagairt don teanga, caipitligh Python."

msgid ""
"**realize**, **customize**, **initialize**, etc. -- use the American \"ize\" "
"suffix, not \"ise.\""
msgstr ""
"**a bhaint amach, **saincheapach**, **tosaithe**, srl. - bain úsáid as "
"iarmhír “ize” Meiriceánach, ní “ise.”"

msgid ""
"**subclass** -- it's a single word without a hyphen, both as a verb "
"(\"subclass that model\") and as a noun (\"create a subclass\")."
msgstr ""
"**fo-rang** - is focal amháin é gan bhriathar, mar bhriathar (“fo-aicme an "
"tsamhail sin”) agus mar ainmfhocal (“cruthaigh fo-aicme”)."

msgid "**the web**, **web framework** -- it's not capitalized."
msgstr "**an gréasán**, **creat gréasán** - níl sé caipitlithe."

msgid "**website** -- use one word, without capitalization."
msgstr "**láithreán gréasáin** - bain úsáid as focal amháin, gan caipitliú."

msgid "Django-specific terminology"
msgstr "Téarmaíocht Django-shonrach"

msgid "**model** -- it's not capitalized."
msgstr "**samhail** - níl sé caipitlithe."

msgid "**template** -- it's not capitalized."
msgstr "**teimpléad** - níl sé caipitlithe."

msgid ""
"**URLconf** -- use three capitalized letters, with no space before \"conf.\""
msgstr ""
"**URLConf** - bain úsáid as trí litir chaipitealaithe, gan aon spás roimh "
"“conf.”"

msgid "**view** -- it's not capitalized."
msgstr "**amharc** - níl sé caipitlithe."

msgid "Guidelines for reStructuredText files"
msgstr "Treoirlínte maidir le comhaid RestructuredText"

msgid ""
"These guidelines regulate the format of our reST (reStructuredText) "
"documentation:"
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn na treoirlínte seo formáid ár ndoiciméad REst (ReStructuredText):"

msgid "In section titles, capitalize only initial words and proper nouns."
msgstr ""
"I dteidil rannán, ní dhéanann caipitliú ach focail tosaigh agus ainmfhocail "
"cheart."

msgid ""
"Wrap the documentation at 80 characters wide, unless a code example is "
"significantly less readable when split over two lines, or for another good "
"reason."
msgstr ""
"Fill an doiciméadú ag 80 carachtar ar leithead, mura bhfuil sampla cód i "
"bhfad níos lú inléite nuair a roinntear thar dhá líne, nó ar chúis mhaith "
"eile."

msgid ""
"The main thing to keep in mind as you write and edit docs is that the more "
"semantic markup you can add the better. So:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud is mó atá le coinneáil i gcuimhne agus tú ag scríobh agus a chur "
"in eagar doiciméid ná is fearr an marcáil shéimeantach is féidir leat a chur "
"leis. Mar sin:"

msgid "Isn't nearly as helpful as:"
msgstr "Níl sé beagnach chomh cabhrach le:"

msgid ""
"This is because Sphinx will generate proper links for the latter, which "
"greatly helps readers."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo toisc go nginfidh Sphinx naisc cheart don dara ceann, rud a "
"chabhraíonn go mór le léitheoirí."

msgid ""
"You can prefix the target with a ``~`` (that's a tilde) to get only the "
"\"last bit\" of that path. So ``:mod:`~django.contrib.auth``` will display a "
"link with the title \"auth\"."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an sprioc a réamhriú le ``~`` (sin tilde) chun ach an “giotán "
"deireanach” den chosáin sin a fháil. Mar sin, taispeánfaidh ``:mod: "
"`~django.contrib.auth`` nasc leis an teideal “auth”."

msgid ""
"Use :mod:`~sphinx.ext.intersphinx` to reference Python's and Sphinx' "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: MOD: `~sphinx.ext.intersphinx` chun tagairt a dhéanamh do dhoiciméadú "
"Python agus Sphinx."

msgid ""
"Add ``.. code-block:: <lang>`` to literal blocks so that they get "
"highlighted. Prefer relying on automatic highlighting using ``::`` (two "
"colons). This has the benefit that if the code contains some invalid syntax, "
"it won't be highlighted. Adding ``.. code-block:: python``, for example, "
"will force highlighting despite invalid syntax."
msgstr ""
"Cuir ``.. code-block::<lang>`` le bloic litriúla ionas go dtabharfar aird "
"orthu. Is fearr leat brath ar aibhsiú uathoibríoch ag baint úsáide as ``::`` "
"(dhá cholún). Tá an buntáiste aige seo, má tá roinnt comhréireachta "
